            { title = 'Content: Overview', note = '• CatsEye is home to a variety of custom content. In addition, some content found in retail FFXI may be changed on this server to varying degrees. These changes and additions are detailed below.\n• If content is not listed in the menu above, then assume it is the same as retail. Also, keep in mind with any link you click that if the URL or title of the wiki page does not say "CatsEyeXI" in it, then you are looking at retail info, which may or may not be accurate to this server.\n• Just getting started? Check out the New Player Guide (ACE) or New Player Guide (Crystal Warrior)!' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: Overview', note = '• __NoTOC__' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: Accelerated CatsEye (ACE) Character', note = '• Accelerated CatsEye (ACE) is the most common game mode played on CatsEyeXI. It is designed to minimize resistance to progression, allowing you to establish a character quickly and experience all areas of the game without the time sink associated with 75-era retail FFXI.' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: Core mechanics and boosted rates', note = '• ACE characters benefit from significantly accelerated rates in key areas:\n• Feature: Experience (EXP) Rate; ACE Value: x1.5\n• Feature: Weapons/Magic Skill Up Rate; ACE Value: x2.0\n• Feature: Crafting Skill Rate; ACE Value: x1.5\n• Feature: Crafting Skill Up Value; ACE Value: x2.0 (0.3 and 0.6)\n• Feature: Fishing Skill Up Rate; ACE Value: x3.0\n• Feature: Trust Capacity; ACE Value: Up to 5\n• Feature: Level Cap Restrictions; ACE Value: No\n• Feature: Dual Boxing; ACE Value: 2 simultaneous logins' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features', note = '• ACE characters possess numerous quality-of-life benefits that streamline movement, inventory management, and early progression, aligning with the CatsEye Accelerated vision:' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features › Travel and movement', note = '• Outpost Warps: All Outposts are unlocked from the start for ACE characters, allowing immediate travel access across Vana\'diel.\n• Home Point travel & restoration: Enabled for ACE characters. HP crystals also restore HP/MP upon use.\n• Survival guide & Unity Warp: ACE characters may utilize Survival Guide travel and limited Unity Warp travel.\n• All maps unlocked: Immediate access to custom in-game maps, to aid navigation.\n• Mount access: Mounts are enabled for ACE characters (available at level 20).\n• Explorer moogles: Easy city teleportation for convenience.' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features › Progression support', note = '• Trusts: Having access to a full party of up to five Trusts allows ACE characters to accomplish milestones and delay certain group activities. It is recommended that players prioritize increasing their Trust capacity by completing Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel missions.\n• Equipment Boosts: The Sprout Beret & Echad Ring are enabled for ACE, offering additional EXP boosts.\n• Wizardoll NPC: A specialized NPC allows ACE players to learn spells using Sparks of Eminence, bypassing the typical need for farming or Auction House purchases. See: Wizardoll' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features › Economic access and support', note = '• ACE mode grants full access to vital economic and passive progression systems:\n• Auction House Access: ACE characters can utilize the Auction House (AH), trade, and bazaar functions.\n• Records of Eminence (RoE) & Sparks: ACE characters have full access to Records of Eminence (the venture system) and Sparks of Eminence systems, allowing them to earn passive gil and obtain early equipment. The monetary exchange amount is capped at 150,000 sparks per week.\n• Fields of Valor (FoV): ACE accounts receive higher rewards from FoV, with Tabs offering a reward rate of x5.0.\n• Goblin Mystery Box: ACE characters have access to this system. See. Gobbie Mystery Box\n• Login Campaign: Custom daily login campaign for additional rewards. See: Login campaign\n• Global Linkshell: Access to the global linkshell for server events, community support, and organized activities.' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features › Exclusive rewards', note = '• ACE accounts benefit from several exclusive reward systems designed to accelerate character establishment and prepare for endgame:\n• Milestone reward: An exclusive reward program for new ACE players upon reaching level 75 and Rank 10 in nation missions. Players can choose relic weapon assistance, mythic weapon assistance, an Octave Club, or a Defending Ring. See: Milestone rewards\n• Crafting rewards: ACE accounts receive two rewards upon hitting Crafting Level 100 in a craft: a free relic weapon voucher and a Kupo Shield (all crafts +3). See: Crafting rewards' },
            { title = 'Accelerated: ACE features › Progression path', note = '• Early endgame path: Domain Invasion (DI) and Sky are recommended as early endgame options to obtain gear and Aeonic Weapon Skills. Domain Invasion is particularly good for farming materials for Oboro Weapons and Aeonic Weapon Skills. See: Content progression\n• While ACE mode provides extensive solo capability, all major endgame challenges and the acquisition of best-in-slot rewards will require organized group cooperation. Becoming a member of a Linkshell is highly recommended for end game content.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Introduction', note = '• CatsEyeXI is a private server which provides a customized Final Fantasy XI experience. If you are new to FFXI entirely, keep in mind that the game was released in 2002, during a time when MMORPG design tended towards extreme complexity and "grindiness" with sparse information disseminated via rumor in online message boards. Over the decades, the game has become considerably less grindy but only more complex, as new expansions and quality-of-life improvements have added more and more systems and content. Even using Google to research this game can be confusing, as not everything in retail FFXI is available in CatsEyeXI, and the server also has its own systems on top of what\'s in retail.\n• All in all, starting FFXI for the first time on CatsEyeXI can be an intimidating or even overwhelming experience. And even if you played FFXI in its heyday, a lot has changed over the years! This guide is intended to help get you up-to-speed on things every new player should know. And overall, CatsEyeXI is full of very friendly, helpful, and proactive people. If you still have questions or need assistance with anything, don’t be afraid to ask in the Catseye linkshell!\n• This guide assumes you have some familiarity with retail FFXI. If you are totally new to the game, or if you haven\'t played in many years, please check out other online guides that can get you acquainted with the basics. A great new player guide can be found here on bg-wiki; just start reading at "Starting Jobs," and ignore all the mentions of Abyssea since we can\'t enter Abyssea here until level 70. Pay special attention to the Macro User\'s Guide on that page, as learning the macro syntax will be a huge help in streamlining your gameplay experience.\n• Returning players are encouraged to check out bg-wiki\'s Returning to Vana\'diel guide.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Important Links', note = '• https://www.catseyexi.com\n• Features links to access the discord, wiki, and user area. The database tools tab has some very useful features such as:\n• Auction House\n• Bazaar Lookup\n• Character Lookup\n• Crafter list\n• Crafting Recipe Lookup\n• Monster Bestiary\n• Weather Lookup\n• Item Database\n    ◦ Item Search is incredibly useful to use on this server, as it not only shows you an item\'s Auction House listing, but also which mobs drop which items, and at what % drop rate. If you ever find yourself needing to farm an item, check here (over other FFXI wikis) first!\n• The Sidebar Guide has helpful instructions on how to customize the left-hand navigation panel to better suit your needs - fill it with various CatsEye pages, for example.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Quick Tips and FAQs', note = '• The following list includes answers to some of the most frequently-asked questions on the CatsEye linkshell. If many of these questions don\'t make sense to you, don\'t worry, just skip \'em and reference this list again once you\'ve gotten your feet wet.\n• How do I talk in the server-wide linkshell, the green text channel I see people using?\n    ◦ Type \'/l2\' or \'/linkshell2\' followed by whatever you want to say. You can also use the shortcut ctrl+x.\n• The minimap is blocking my macro menu, how do I move it? (or any other addon)\n    ◦ Hold shift and click+drag any addon wherever you\'d like.\n• Which Unity should I choose?\n    ◦ Apururu, Sylvie, and Yoran-Oran are the only Unity trusts that are implemented and usable, and even those three are not fully coded (their weaponskill Nott isn\'t yet implemented). Do not choose any others until they are working! For a comparison of these unity trusts, see Trust Recommendations. Also, keep in mind you must earn 5000 or more Unity accolades each week in order for your Unity trust to appear in your list.\n• I\'m trying to earn a support job through the Rhapsodies of Vanadiel mission, but instead of receiving Gilgamesh\'s introductory letter, I got an Anniversary Ring instead. What gives?\n    ◦ This is by design. Earning a support job must be done the "old fashioned way": either through the quest Elder Memories in Selbina or The Old Lady in Mhaura. Despite this, completing the early RoV quests is still highly recommended at the beginning of your adventuring career, as they give you a permanent experience point bonus, extra trust slots, cheaper home-point teleports, and more.\n• I\'m trying to complete RoV mission 1-9, The Lion\'s Roar, the fight against Ophiotaurus in Qufim. But when I summon the monster, my trusts disappear! That shouldn\'t happen! What\'s going on?\n    ◦ Yes, this fight caps your level at 50 and *despawns your trusts*. This is by design and is not a bug. You need to get a party together to defeat "the monkey" and advance the RoV plotline. Check the CatsEyeXI Missions page for more details on how RoV missions are implemented here.\n• Where should I go to earn experience at ?\n    ◦ Check out bg-wiki\'s guide Fantastic EXPs and Where to Find Them.\n• I can\'t afford better gear, and I can\'t use the sparks NPC until I complete the Magicite mission and Limit Break 1. Is there a way I can request help from other players?\n    ◦ Yes! In addition to asking for help in the server linkshell, you can also check out this New Player Sparks Gear Request Thread on the discord.\n• When is daily reset?\n    ◦ Japanese Midnight (15:00 UTC, 07:00 PST, 10:00 EST)' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Quick Tips and FAQs › Miscellaneous Tips', note = '• There are a few handy shortcuts that you can use:\n    ◦ !help - will display a list of all available commands to you, other commands can be found under the Commands section in the table above.\n    ◦ !mog - opens nomad moogle menu (can only be used in cities). Use this to check your storage, change your job, check your delivery box, and send stuff to other players.\n    ◦ !signet, !sigil, !sanction - these give you the corresponding area buffs. Make sure you keep these up (and the right ones in the right zones). Use Sanction for Treasures of Aht Urhgan areas, Sigil for Wings of the Goddess areas, and Signet for everywhere else. There is now an addon to handle this automatically for you preinstalled, just toggle on "CrystalBuff".\n    ◦ !chef - a food shop that you can access anywhere. Very handy if you forgot to eat. If you are in a city, you can also use this command to sell items to an NPC.\n• You can obtain a free Relic Weapon for leveling your first craft to 100. Working on a craft is one of the first things you should be doing once you hit 75! If you want to hit 100 the cheapest/fastest, do cooking. You can always change later.\n• Fast way to make gil: exchange Sparks of Eminence for items to NPC/sell on AH. The sparks exchange amount is capped at 150,000 per week, but resets on Sunday. NOTE: As of March 31 2025, new players must have completed Nation Mission 4-1 ("Magicite") and the first Limit Break quest in order to make use of the Sparks of Eminence NPC.\n    ◦ For a mid-game location you might farm for profit, consider Castle Oztroja—the yagudo there drop lots of gear and spells which sell well, either on the auction house or even directly to NPCs. Other areas with beastmen spellcasters (e.g. Sea Serpent Grotto) also tend to yield good loot.\n• You can put on equipment that is stored in one of your eight wardrobes in your Mog House; it doesn\'t have to be in your inventory. For this reason, you don\'t really need to keep any equipment in your inventory unless you need it for a quest or you plan to sell it or something. You can access your wardrobes at any time by going into the menu and selecting "View House." You can move items between your inventory and your wardrobes there (as well as your satchel, sack, and case) even when out in the field.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Gear', note = '• The first thing you should do is speak with any of the following Trial NPCs to recieve:\n• Destrier Beret\n• Chocobo Shirt\n• Trial NPCs have a Yellow/Green pedal logo on the /map and can be found at:\n• Note: this process used to require trading an Adventurer Coupon to the NPC, but now new players can simply speak with the NPC to receive their beret and shirt.\n• Once you have completed the first Rhapsodies mission and earned the Rhapsody in White, you can access the Curio Moogle, who provides many helpful items. (Alternatively, you can unlock the Curio Moogle via the quest Out of Stock.\n• You can find the Moogle at:\n• Port San d\'Oria (J-9)\n• Port Bastok (K-13)\n• Port Windurst (M-4)\n• While you can\'t immediately access the full Sparks of Eminence shop as a new player, you can access a limited version of the shop that sells weapons, shields, and musical instruments, up to level 60. You can only purchase each item once per character, and the selection available to you depends on your current job and level. Talk to one of these NPCs to begin:\n• Rolandienne - Southern San d\'Oria (G-10)\n• Isakoth - Bastok Markets (E-11)\n• Fhelm Jobeizat - Windurst Woods (J-10)' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Gear › Items from RoEs', note = '• By completing some Records of Eminence quests, players can earn useful items in addition to EXP and Sparks. Here are a select few easy-to-complete RoEs:\n• Reward: Onyx Earring; Level: 10; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Yughott Grotto\n• Reward: Opal Earring; Level: 10; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Giddeus\n• Reward: Lapis Lazuli Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Konschtat Highlands\n• Reward: Amethyst Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Gusgen Mines\n• Reward: Sardonyx Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in La Theine Plateau\n• Reward: Clear Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Ordelle\'s Caves\n• Reward: Clear Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Ordelle\'s Caves\n• Reward: Amber Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Dangruf Wadi\n• Reward: Tourmaline Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Tahrongi Canyon\n• Reward: Opal Ring; Level: 14; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in King Ranperre\'s Tomb\n• Reward: Bone Earring; Level: 16; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Maze of Shakhrami\n• Reward: Focus Collar; Level: 18; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Qufim Island\n• Reward: Beetle Earring; Level: 21; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Ranguemont Pass\n• Consumables\n• Reward: Meat Mithkabob x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Jugner Forest\n• Reward: Crab Sushi x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Pashhow Marshlands\n• Reward: Apple Pie x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Meriphataud Mountains\n• Reward: Snoll Gelato x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower\n• Reward: Sole Sushi x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Middle Delkfutt\'s Tower\n• Reward: Prism Powder x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Eastern Altepa Desert\n• Reward: Silent Oil x12; Record of Eminence: Defeat 10 enemies in Western Altepa Desert\n• For the full list, see: Records of Eminence.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Gear › Novice Trials', note = '• On CatsEyeXI, many pieces of early-level gear can be augmented by completing Novice Trials. These quests do not give the base item, they make existing items stronger. To obtain the base item, players may need to purchase them with Sparks of Eminence, complete a quest, defeat a low-level Notorious Monster, or perform a low-level craft. Some of them can also be simply purchased from the Auction House if players have the gil for them. Then, players can trade that item to a Novice Trial NPC to be assigned a set of monsters to defeat in order to add Augments to the item.\n• Take a look at those upgrades to find equipment that suits your playstyle as you level up. The following are just a few Novice Trial pieces that aren\'t too difficult for new ACE players to obtain:\n• Base Item: Beestinger; Level: 7; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Critical hit rate+1%; Required Monsters to Defeat: Maneating Hornet x15 (North Gustaberg) Maneating Hornet x15 (South Gustaberg)\n• Base Item: Pelte; Level: 8; [Augmented] Augments: INT+1 MND+1 MP recovered while healing+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: River Crab x15 (East Sarutabaruta) River Crab x15 (West Sarutabaruta)\n• Base Item: Pilgrim\'s Wand; Level: 8; [Augmented] Augments: MP+5 Conserve MP+2 MP Recovered while healing +1; Required Monsters to Defeat: Carrion Crow x 15 (West Sarutabaruta) Akbaba x 10 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Base Item: Clipeus; Level: 9; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 Shield Skill+3; Required Monsters to Defeat: Scarab Beetle x15 (East Ronfaure) Copper Beetle x10 (Palborough Mines)\n• Base Item: Armiger\'s Lace; Level: 9; [Augmented] Augments: HP+2 Accuracy+1; Required Monsters to Defeat: Vulture x10 (South Gustaberg) Vulture x10 (North Gustaberg)\n• Base Item: Scale Cuisses; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 HP+8; Required Monsters to Defeat: Goblin Armorer (Konschtat Highlands) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Bronze Ingot x3 to Lost Tongs (G-7)\n• Base Item: Brais; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: Evasion+2 Accuracy+1; Required Monsters to Defeat: Goblin Burglar (La Theine Plateau) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Sheep Leather x3 to Lost Lockpick (C-5)\n• Base Item: Linen Slops; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: MP+5 Magic Accuracy +1; Required Monsters to Defeat: Goblin Tailor (Tahrongi Canyon) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Cotton Thread x3 to Lost Needle (G-9)\n• Base Item: Light Axe; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: DMG: +3 CHR+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Forest Hare x15 (East Ronfaure) Forest Hare x15 (West Ronfaure)\n• Base Item: Entrancing Ribbon; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: Fast Cast+1% Pet: Accuracy+2 Ranged Accuracy+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Steppe Hare x15 (La Theine Plateau) Canyon Rarab x15 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Base Item: Bee Spatha; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: MP+15 DEF+4; Required Monsters to Defeat: Huge Wasp x15 (Konschtat Highlands) Huge Wasp x15 (La Theine Plateau)\n• Base Item: Brass Hammer; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DMG: +3 MND+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Skeleton Warrior x7 (Konschtat Highlands) Skeleton Warrior x7 (La Theine Plateau) Skeleton Warrior x7 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Base Item: Greataxe; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DMG: +5 DEF+5; Required Monsters to Defeat: Young Quadav x15 (North Gustaberg) Young Quadav x15 (South Gustaberg)\n• Base Item: Guerilla Gloves; Level: 13; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 MP+4 Attack+2 Pet: STR+1; Required Monsters to Defeat: Greater Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines) Veteran Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines) Onyx Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines)\n• Base Item: Mettle Leggings Note: Also equippable as PUP; Level: 17; [Augmented] Augments: HP+4 DEX+1 Pet:Attack+2 Ranged Attack+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Wild Sheep x25 (East Ronfaure (S)) Brutal Sheep x20 (Jugner Forest)\n• Base Item: Beetle Mittens; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: Attack+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Stag Beetle x15 (Jugner Forest) Stag Beetle x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Base Item: Beetle Subligar; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: Attack+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Stag Beetle x15 (Jugner Forest) Stag Beetle x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Base Item: Beetle Leggings; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: AGI+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Copper Beetle x15 (Palborough Mines) Beady Beetle x15 (Carpenters\' Landing)\n• The following weapons and equipment you can get using 2,000 Conquest Points at a gate guard in your home nation, or if it isn\'t available there, from the Jeuno Envoy in Ru\'Lude Gardens for 4,000 Conquest Points. Once you have the item, you can augment it via the normal Novice Trials process.\n• Base Item: Decurion\'s Hammer; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Enhancing Magic Skill+2 Healing Magic Skill+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Wolf Zombie x20 (Konschtat Highlands) Ghost x5 (Konschtat Highlands) Skeleton Warrior x10 (Gusgen Mines)\n• Base Item: Ryl.Spr. Spear; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Conserve TP+1 Resist Blind+3; Required Monsters to Defeat: Orcish Wallbreacher x1 (Ghelsba Outpost) Orcish Barricader x1 (Ghelsba Outpost) Orcish Flamethrower x5 (Fort Ghelsba)\n• Base Item: Mercenary\'s Pole; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Magic Defense Bonus+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Four of Batons x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Coins x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Cups x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Swords x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins)\n• Base Item: Decurion\'s Dagger; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+2 Accuracy+2 Resist Silence+3; Required Monsters to Defeat: Greater Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Veteran Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Onyx Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands)\n• Base Item: Decurion\'s Shield; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 AGI+1 Magic Defense Bonus+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Greater Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Veteran Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Onyx Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands)\n• Base Item: Ryl.Spr. Horn; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: Song Recast Delay-1 Attack+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Orcish Grunt x15 (Jugner Forest) Orcish Neckchopper x15 (Jugner Forest) Orcish Stonechucker x15 (Jugner Forest)\n• Base Item: Mercenary\'s Knife; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Ranged Accuracy+2; Required Monsters to Defeat: Yagudo Mendicant x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Persecutor x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Piper x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Base Item: Mrc. Greatsword; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 MP+5 Resist Sleep+3; Required Monsters to Defeat: Yagudo Mendicant x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Persecutor x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Piper x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Gear › Level 30 Gear', note = '• When you reach level 31, your destrier beret and chocobo shirt will not work anymore. To bridge the gap between here and level 50+ when you can unlock Artifact Armor and Sparks gear, players can complete any of these six quests to gain access to powerful gear with special augments custom to our server:\n• Empty Handed (Shade set)\n• Navigating the Nest (Noct set)\n• Negotiating the Necropolis (Eisen set) (Can be equipped by DRK and DRG as well)\n• Searching the Citadel (Seer\'s set)\n• Running on the Range (Garish set)\n• Horutoto Hakken (Soil set) (Can be equipped by PUP as well)\n• Optionally, once you have obtained one of these rewards, you can transfer its augments to the high-quality (crafted) version. Trade the augmented piece to the repairer NPC you got it from to learn more.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Spells', note = '• Since new players aren\'t able to spend Sparks of Eminence that they earn from Records of Eminence until they complete Nation Mission 4-1 ("Magicite") and the first Limit Break quest, they might struggle to earn enough gil to afford spells as they level up their character. Thankfully, a custom CatsEyeXI NPC can help!\n• The Wizardoll offers new adventurers a chance to learn a variety of spells, in exchange for Sparks of Eminence. Players can learn spells from the Wizardoll even if they have not completed the prerequisites to use the Sparks store. The Wizardoll is located near each of the three Sparks NPCs:\n• Southern San d\'Oria (G-10)\n• Bastok Markets (E-11)\n• Windurst Woods (J-10)\n• Spells taught by the Wizardoll get added directly to the player\'s spell list, so the player will not receive a Scroll like they normally would. The spells available are broken up into three tiers:\n• Tier 1: Approximately level 1-20. Requirement: Memorandoll key item.\n• Tier 2: Approximately level 21-35. Requirement: Nation Rank 3.\n• Tier 3: Approximately level 36-50. Requirement: Nation Rank 4.\n• For the full list of available spells, see the Wizardoll page.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Experience Points', note = '• Make sure you use your Sprout Beret daily, and get an Empress Band from the Gate Guard once you have enough Conquest Points (earned by defeating monsters in Conquest areas with Signet active). These exp bonuses do not stack, but the Sprout Beret has a 20-hour cooldown, so it helps to have multiple sources of Dedication.\n• Note 1: After using your Sprout Beret to gain the exp bonus "Dedication" effect, you can (and should) swap it out for your Destrier Beret or other head equipment.\n• Note 2: If you created your character before June 2022, you may not have a Sprout Beret in your inventory. You will then need to do the goblin daily quests listed on the wiki to earn one.\n• The Curio Moogle also sells the Kupofried trust (he is customized here on CatsEyeXI) for 500k (after completing RoV 2-3). When near him, you and your party members will receive the effect of Corsair\'s Roll which gives and extra 20% EXP gained when defeating a foe. This does stack with other Experience Point buffs.\n• At some point you may want to look into doing EXP Ventures to gain Venture Points to obtain the Echad Ring for 750 Venture Points.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Records of Eminence (RoE’s)', note = '• Please Note: Not all RoE objectives are currently coded, and there is no indicator that a given quest does or doesn\'t work until you attempt to activate it. Please feel free to explore the menu and find which ones are currently working.\n• Update March 31 2025: New players must have completed Nation Mission 4-1 ("Magicite") and the first Limit Break quest in order to access the Sparks of Eminence store. Before then, they can make use of the Wizardoll to exchange Sparks for spells.\n• The BEST way to gain extra XP while leveling! Records of Eminence quests also provide Sparks of Eminence, which allow new players to learn spells via the Wizardoll. After new players complete the prerequisites, Sparks are a great source of equipment and gil. Completing an RoE quest for the first time also usually grants a bonus reward such as equipment, skill-up books, copper vouchers, and food. RoEs can be found in the Quest Tab (hit Main Menu button twice to scroll to the second page).\n• You start RoE’s by going to:\n• Quests > Objective List > Tutorial > Basics > First Steps Forward\n• Then talk to one of the NPC that is listed. This will unlock further RoE Quests. Next you should accept the following (not mandatory, but very useful):\n• Quests > Objective List > Tutorial > Basics\n    ◦ Heal without using magic - /heal after taking damage\n    ◦ Vanquish One Enemy\n    ◦ Call Forth an Alter Ego - This part is covered in the Trusts section below. Complete these quests as soon as possible!\n• Quests > Objective List > Tutorial > Quest 1\n    ◦ Obtain an Alter Ego: (Your home City)\n• Quests > Objective List > Combat (Wide Area) > Combat (General)\n    ◦ Vanquish Multiple Enemies I\n    ◦ Deal 10-20 Damage\n    ◦ Total Damage I\n    ◦ Total Healing I (if you are a healer)\n    ◦ Total Damage Taken I\n    ◦ Weapon Skills I\n• Quests > Objective List > Combat (Wide Area) > Combat (Spoils) 1\n    ◦ Accept all Spoils (Crystals) (If you’re hitting RoE limit, you can add/remove certain crystals as you need to, like light crystal, dark crystal, depending on what you’re exping on)\n• Here is a great exp maker. If any mob you are fighting drops any of these items, you should have the Spoil enabled. I will list the ones I nearly always have enabled, but check this periodically if you need to add any others.\n• Quests > Objective List > Combat (Wide Area) > Combat (Spoils) 2\n    ◦ Spoils (Bat Wing)\n    ◦ Spoils (Flint Stone)\n    ◦ Spoils (Rabbit Hide)\n    ◦ Spoils (Honey)\n    ◦ Spoils (Sheep Skin)\n    ◦ Spoils (Lizard Skin) - super important leveling 39-75 in Crawler’s Nest.\n    ◦ Spoils (Treant Bulb)\n    ◦ Spoils (Wild Onion)\n    ◦ Spoils (Sleepshroom)\n    ◦ Spoils (Zinc Ore)\n    ◦ Spoils (Beehive Chip)\n• While this one is not currently available when starting out, every new zone you enter will populate with a Conflict: Area RoE, that is very helpful in boosting your exp. Remember to always set the one for the zone you are in!\n• Quests > Objective List > Combat Region) > Conflict: Area\n• Quests > Objective List > Other > Daily Objectives\n• Vanquish Multiple Enemies (D) - Remember to select this every day! Also grants a Copper Voucher.\n• Note: Certain RoE quests give items. If your inventory is full you will get an error message. Once you make space in inventory you must go to Quest tab Records of Eminence under Current and accept reward on the completed task.\n• Also: Despite the message that displays each time you complete a repeatable quest, you only receive the item from a RoE quest upon completing it the first time. That is, you only receive an Invisible Mantle the first time you defeat 10 enemies in Batallia Downs, not every ten.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Unity RoE’s and joining a Unity', note = '• In order to participate, players must have completed ten or more Records of Eminence objectives and then visit one of the following areas:\n• Southern San d\'Oria / Northern San d\'Oria / Port San d\'Oria\n• Bastok Mines / Bastok Markets / Port Bastok\n• Windurst Waters / Port Windurst / Windurst Woods\n• Players may then join a Unity by setting the Records of Eminence objective All for One (Which is in the Tutorial part), and speaking to one of the NPCs given below, and selecting a Unity to join:\n• Unity Service NPCs:\n• Urbiolaine in Southern San d\'Oria (G-10)\n• Igsli in Bastok Markets (E-11)\n• Teldro-Kesdrodo in Windurst Woods (J-10)\n• Yonolala in Windurst Woods (J-10)\n• Note: Apururu (UC), Sylvie (UC), and Yoran-Oran (UC) are the only Unity Leader Trust Magic that are fully functional.\n• Please select one of these three choices at this time.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › Spending Sparks of Eminence (Sparks)', note = '• New players must have completed Nation Mission 4-1 ("Magicite") and the first Limit Break quest in order to access the full Sparks of Eminence store. But before then, players have access to a limited selection of weapons, shields, and musical instruments that they can purchase with Sparks. You can only purchase each item once per character, and the selection available to you depends on your current job and level, up to level 60. Speak to one of the NPCs listed below to see what\'s on offer.\n• Players can also make use of the Wizardoll to learn a variety of White Magic, Black Magic, Songs, and Ninjutsu in exchange for Sparks.\n• After meeting the prerequisites, Sparks of Eminence can be exchanged for items and equipment at the following A.M.A.N. NPCs:\n• Rolandienne - Southern San d\'Oria (G-10)\n• Isakoth - Bastok Markets (E-11)\n• Fhelm Jobeizat - Windurst Woods (J-10)\n• Players can hold 150,000 sparks at a time, and the exchange amount is capped at 150,000 per week, and resets on Sunday at JP Midnight.\n• Spark items are capped at a ratio of 1 Spark:10 Gil. While some low level items are less rewarding and can even sell for 0, 1:10 is the cap. Players need only go into "Equipment (Lv.71 - 98)" and buy Acheron Shields for 2,755 sparks, and NPC them. Any lesser remaining sparks can be spent on the cheaper items in the same category if you wish to spend anything left over.\n• CatsEyeXI supplies two addons (located in the launcher under the addons tab) that help to facilitate the buying and selling of Sparks items. Check both sparks and sellit addons to auto load when the game launches. If already in game and you don\'t have the addons loaded yet, you can use the Ashita command /addon load sparks and /addon load sellit to load them. Once loaded, use the command /sparks buyall acheron shield to buy either as many shields as your inventory can hold or until you run out of sparks. Now that you have a bunch of shields use the command /sellit acheron shield to sell all the shields you just bought. These need to be used near the Sparks NPC.\n• Don’t let this be your only source of making gil. You will need to find additional ways to make gil, but this goes a long way, especially as a new player.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Starting Out › "Gainz": Limited-time Challenges', note = '• Throughout the week at specific times of day, every character will be given a repeatable limited-time RoE quest, such as "Vanquish Arcana" or "Crack Treasure Caskets." These quests are available for four hours, and grant a Copper Voucher (first completion only), Sparks of Eminence, Unity Accolades, and Experience Points.\n• By far the most valuable and sought-after limited-time challenge is Gain Experience. This quest comes around three times per week, and the times when it is active are referred to as "gains" or "gainz" by the community. This quest grants you experience (and sparks, and accolades) for simply gaining experience. Logging in during gainz and fighting exp-granting enemies can skyrocket your progression, allowing you to gain dozens of levels or merits and hundreds of thousands of gil (by converting sparks into Acheron shields and selling them to an NPC).\n• Two of the most commonly asked questions on the server are "When is gainz?" and "How much longer is gainz?" Please refer to the below schedule. Times are shown in UTC and EST; use this tool, google, or any number of other online tools to convert these times to your local time zone. (Note that, as of September 2024, these challenges tend to start and end 3-4 minutes early on this server).\n• UTC\n• Sunday 11:00 - 15:00 UTC\n• Tuesday 03:00 - 07:00 UTC\n• Wednesday 19:00 - 23:00 UTC\n• Add one hour to each of the above times during British Summer Time (March-October), if you live in an area which observes it.\n• EST\n• Sunday 6:00 - 10:00 AM EST\n• Monday 10:00 PM - Tuesday 2:00 AM EST\n• Wednesday 2:00 - 6:00 PM EST\n• Add one hour to each of the above times during US Daylight Savings Time (March-November), if you live in an area which observes it.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Trust Magic', note = '• The most effective way to level up solo is by using Trust Magic. These are Alter Egos of NPCs such as Shantotto, Prince Trion, Koru-Moru, etc. that are able to be used in battle.\n• Starting out you can only summon 3 trusts at one time. By progressing in Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel, you can unlock the ability to summon up to 5 trusts:\n• Rhapsody in White unlocks the ability to summon 4 trusts.\n    ◦ It is recommended that new players earn this key item as soon as possible. It can be done as soon as you reach Selbina or Mhaura.\n• Rhapsody in Crimson unlocks the ability to summon 5 trusts.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Trust Magic › Initial Trust Guide', note = '• Once you hit your first level 5 job (shouldn’t take long with Sprout Beret or an exp ring active), talk to the NPC listed below based on your Home City. Make sure you enable the Obtain an Alter Ego: (Your home City) RoE listed above.\n• Trust NPCs:\n• Gondebaud - South San d’Oria (L-6)\n    ◦ Unlocks Trust: Excenmille - Northern San d’Oria (D-9)\n• Wetata - Windurst Woods (G-10)\n    ◦ Unlocks Trust: Kupipi - Heavens Tower (in Windurst Walls)\n• Clarion Star - Port Bastok (K-7)\n    ◦ Unlocks Trust: Naji - Metalworks (J-8)\n• Once you obtain your first trust, go outside the city and summon him to complete the Obtain an Alter Ego: (Your home City) RoE.\n• You MUST go back to Excenmille or Kupipi or Naji (depending on your city) to finish the quest and the RoE.\n• You can also go to each of the other 2 cities and obtain the first Trust, but I would do this after completing the next part of this guide.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Trust Magic › RoE Trusts', note = '• Upon summoning your first Trust, you will obtain a Cipher of Valaineral’s alter ego. Trade this item to a Trust NPC listed above. Once you do this, and after a short cutscene, you will learn Trust: Valaineral.\n• You MUST accept ROE quest:\n• Quests > Objective List > Tutorial > Basics > Alter Ego: Valaineral\n• Now go outside and summon Valaineral. Because you enabled the RoE quest, upon summoning the Trust you will obtain a Cipher of Mihli’s alter ego.\n• If you repeat steps 1-3, you will obtain the following\n• Valaineral - Paladin / Warrior\n• Mihli Aliapoh - White Mage\n• Tenzen - Samurai\n• Adelheid - Scholar / Black Mage\n• Joachim - Bard\n• If for some reason you do not get a Cipher after summoning one of these Trusts (with the exception of Joachim - he is the final Trust obtained via this method) make sure you have the RoE quest relating to the Trust enabled.\n• Note: Joachim will not start casting songs until around level 35-40\n• The Curio Vendor Moogle has some very good additional trust ciphers, including: Kupofried, Koru-Moru, and Qultada. Zeid II is also for sale here, but this cipher is also earned over the course of completing the RoV missions, so purchasing it is not recommended.\n• Note: as this is a private server, not all trusts are coded and working 100% the same as retail. Many have been customized and have unique features. Read in detail about our custom trust magic system here.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Trust Magic › Trust Recommendations', note = '• Particularly useful trusts include:\n• Nanaa Mihgo and/or Lion II are useful to unlock before a player levels the Thief job, as they have access to Treasure Hunter just like a player character does. This increases to the tier 2 trait at level 45. Note that Nanaa Mihgo also uses the Despoil ability.\n• The two premier tank trusts on the CatsEye server are Halver and Gessho. Halver has a sizable enmity bonus, allowing him to keep hate better than most other trusts; he also has been customized to specialize as a tank, so he never uses Berserk unlike his retail version. Gessho is great at staying alive with Utsusemi, but usually needs a thief to Trick Attack him to keep enmity; with the right party setup, Gessho can tank even sky gods quite well. Other tank trusts have their uses, but generally are outclassed by these two.\n• Sylvie and Apururu Unity trusts are both great healer/support options, but you can only have one of the two, and they have slightly different uses.\n    ◦ Sylvie\'s behavior changes based on what job you are when you summon her; if you are a mage, she casts Indi-Refresh (MP recovery), otherwise she casts Indi-Regen (HP recovery). In either case, Sylvie is better suited for general adventuring, as her persistent regen or refresh keep your party alive and running without the expenditure of much MP. However, she struggles when dealing with "spike" damage as her direct heals are less impactful than Apururu\'s.\n    ◦ Apururu is better suited for harder fights, as she uses Cure V and Protectra/Shellra V, and can also cast Stona; however, she tends to assume every fight is life-or-death, and runs out of MP very quickly. Other white mage trusts such as Kupipi can fill Apururu\'s role in a party, but most players consider Apu a better choice if you have her.\n    ◦ Yoran-Oran is also a great Unity trust choice, able to use Afflatus Solace and casts Cursna on party members with Doom.\n    ◦ Overall: Apururu is the best WHM trust, perhaps tied with Yoran-Oran. But because other WHM options exist, many players prefer Sylvie due to her low maintenance and flexibility.\n• Koru-Moru is a very useful support trust, able to cast Haste, Refresh, and Dispel while also healing and debuffing.\n• Tenzen is a powerful damage-dealer during early levels, but his accuracy begins to fall off as you level up, to the point where he will miss much more often than he hits by level 75. Many players prefer Nashmeira II, Zeid II, Shikaree Z, or Semih Lafihna for trust damage-dealers.\n    ◦ Zeid has the added benefit of using Stun when enemies use TP moves or spells, though he is occasionally too late.\n    ◦ Shikaree Z has the added benefit of casting -na spells (removing negative status effects) due to her white mage subjob.\n    ◦ Nashmeira can also heal.\n• Kupofried is MVP. Does literally nothing in combat, but grants you a sweet 20% experience point bonus. If you are in a party with another player who has summoned Kupofried, make sure to stay close enough to the moogle that you see the dice icon in your buffs when you defeat an enemy, or else you won\'t benefit from his bonus.\n• Qultada on this server only performs two abilities: Samurai Roll, and Fighter\'s Roll. Store TP and Double Attack are very useful traits for any melee job. However, many players find him underwhelming, since he only rolls once and doesn\'t use Double-Up.\n• Cornelia (purchased with obsidian fragments) is useful for her persistent Indi-Haste, which stacks with ordinary Haste.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Outpost Warps', note = '• All Outpost Warps are unlocked from level 1, however your main job must meet the level requirement for the region to which you wish to teleport.\n• Outpost Warp NPCs:\n• Conrad - Bastok Mines (K-8)\n• Jeanvirgaud - Northern San d’Oria (L-10)\n• Rottata - Port Windurst (L-4)' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Home Point Crystals', note = '• Once you initially click on any Home Point crystal you find, you unlock the ability to teleport to it for a fee. While in a city, teleporting to another home point within that city is free. Fees are lowered 80% once the Rhapsody in White has been obtained.\n• Most home points also restore your HP/MP back to full.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Survival Guides', note = '• Once you initially click on a survival guide you find, you unlock the ability to teleport to it for a fee of gil or tabs (the currency obtained from completing ground tomes). There are typically 1 Survival Guide in every zone (with some exceptions). Cities only have 1 Survival Guide located somewhere in the city zones.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Chocobos and Mounts', note = '• At level 20, head to Jeuno to unlock the ability to ride on Chocobos, and subsequently unlock a Raptor mount that you can summon at-will. You should prioritize getting a mount as soon as you reach level 20, as doing so allows you to quickly move through overworld areas without being attacked by aggressive mobs.\n• The first quest you need to complete is called Chocobo\'s Wounds. To complete it:\n• Talk to Brutus - Upper Jeuno (G-7) (May need to talk multiple times to trigger the right quest)\n• Feed the chocobo 4 clumps of gausebit grass (You only need to wait 1 real-life minute between each feed)\n• Congratulations, you can now ride a Chocobo from any city! The next step is to complete the quest Full Speed Ahead! to unlock the Raptor mount:\n• Speak with Mapitoto in Upper Jeuno (G-7) after completing the chocobo quest above\n• Run around Batallia Downs on the mount, looking for the food.\n    ◦ They are located on your map, and they are inside the hills - you have to go in!\n    ◦ If the mount slows down (motivation <50%), use /cheer to increase its motivation back up\n• Sometimes the food inside the hills will not load. You still need to go inside the hills all the way to the center and get the message prompt that your raptor overcame the munchies. You will need to do this 5 times total, then head over to the west end of Batallia where Syrillia is located.\n• Once you complete the quest, you unlock the ability to use /mount Raptor in any zone it’s possible to ride a chocobo in.\n• You can get additional mount options from the Greeter Moogles using login points, as well as from Goblin daily quests. These different mounts are cosmetic changes only, and their mobility is identical to that of the raptor mount. Trade these "astral notebook" items to Mapitoto to add the new mount to your list.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Unity Warp', note = '• You can teleport to certain Wanted areas. Some of the warps have been disabled on this server.\n• Available Unity Warps are:\n• 99 & Below\n• East Ronfaure\n• South Gustaberg\n• East Sarutabaruta\n• La Theine Plateau\n• Konschtat Highlands\n• Tahrongi Canyon\n• Content Level 119\n• Valkurm Dunes\n• Buburimu Peninsula\n• Qufim Island\n• Content Level 122\n• Jugner Forest\n• Pashhow Marshlands\n• Meriphataud Mountains\n• Content Level 125\n• Rolanberry Fields\n• Batallia Downs (A nice shortcut to Jeuno!)\n• Sauromugue Champaign\n• Beaucedine Glacier\n• Xarcabard\n• Garlaige Citadel\n• Content Level 128\n• Fei\'Yin\n• Content Level 135\n• Behemoth\'s Dominion' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Getting Around Vana\'diel › Explorer Moogles', note = '• Before you have access to home points or survival guides in a given city, Explorer Moogles can teleport you directly to Bastok, San d\'Oria, or Windurst for 300 gil. You must be at least level 20 to use this service. Explorer Moogles can be found in the three starting cities as well as Selbina and Mhaura.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Auction House', note = '• The Auction House is the market system that allows players to buy a wide variety of items from each other. All Auction Houses are connected and there is no limit to how many items you can sell.\n• We used to have an AH bot that stocked the AH, but since the economy has become self-sustaining, it has been disabled.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Crafting', note = '• Crafting, also known as Synthesis, is a means by which players can combine ingredients with an elemental Crystal to create a variety of items, including equipment, food, and potions. Categories of synthesis include Smithing, Leathercraft, and Alchemy. On this server, you can obtain a free Relic Weapon and a Kupo Shield for leveling your first craft to 100; see Crafting Rewards for more information.\n• The easiest craft to level is Cooking, but lacks the value of other crafts. All crafts are relatively quick to level from 1-50, as the crafting kits are sold at the guilds.\n• You can farm Crystals or Clusters, or buy Clusters from the Curio Vendor Moogle.\n• For Cooking, you can buy all materials to synth to level 100 at vendors around Vana’diel. As mentioned above, all of the crafting test items are sold at the Auction House.\n• It’s recommended you view the crafting guide listed here.' },
            { title = 'New Player Guide: Progression', note = '• 20 — 30 — 40 — 50 — 60 — 70 — 75 — Tier 1 — Tier 2 — Tier 3\n• Mount — Lv 30 Gear — Artifact Armor — Relic Armor — Dynamis wins — Dynamis 2.0\n• Garrison — Goblin Dailies — Sea — Jailer of Love\n• BSNMs, KSNMs, ENMs — Domain Invasion\n• Crafting — Sky — Sky 2.0\n• Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel Missions — Limbus — Bahamut\n• WSNMs — Nyzul Isle — ZNMs and HNMs\n• Mythic WSs — Augment AF+1 and Abjuration Armor\n• Aeonic WSs — Oboro Weapons — Relic & Mythic Weapons\n• Novice Trials — Grand Trials — Adept Reforging\n• Immortalized Authors\n• Toxic [@CatsEyeXI], 2021. "Welcome to CatsEye XI Server!"\n• Fallen (ACE) / Xvs (CW) [@CatsEyeXI], 2022. "CatseyeXI - New Player Guide (v2)"\n• GM Box [@CatsEyeXI], 2023. "CatsEyeXI - New Player Guide (v3)"\n• JDEV Aeltorian [@CatsEyeXI], 2023. "CatsEyeXI - New Player Guide (BG-Wiki v1)"' },
    } },
    { name = 'Rates and progression', group = 'Server', desc = 'Experience points, camps, milestone rewards and login campaigns. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Content/EXP, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Milestone_Rewards, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Login_Campaigns', steps = {
            { title = 'EXP: Overview', note = '• Experience points are not split when partying server-wide, in order to encourage partying rather than penalize teaming up.\n• [ACE] ACE accumulate EXP points at an increased x1.5 rate, but get no EXP Chain bonus.\n• [CW] CW receive a EXP and Chain bonus after lv.40 while in parties (see CW Experience Points).\n• [WEW] WEW receive a Chain bonus at lv.75 (see WEW Experience Points)' },
            { title = 'EXP: EXP Guide', note = '• See CatsEyeXI NPCs § EXP Guide.' },
            { title = 'EXP: EXP Guide (S)', note = '• See CatsEyeXI NPCs § EXP Guide (S).' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations', note = '• Locations which satisfy the mobs must be 3 levels higher than the highest level party member requirement of Ventures.' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Batallia Downs', note = '• (J-10), lv. 19~25, Clipper at lower levels, then Ba (no page)\n    ◦ Can start at 18 with a solid group\n• (J-6), lv. 22~25, Ba (no pages)\n    ◦ There are more Ba than on the J-10 camp' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Batallia Downs (S)', note = '• (I-9), lv. 21~28, Lycopodium (no page)\n• (J-10), lv. 28~32, Clipper & Ba (no page)\n    ◦ The party needs to roam a bit\n    ◦ Can push to 33~34 on birds only' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Bhaflau Thickets', note = '• (I-8) Map1, lv. 56~61, Lesser Colibri\n    ◦ Can push to 62 but very slow\n    ◦ Careful about undeads and formor at night' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Bostaunieux Oubliette', note = '• (D-9) Map2, lvl 49-53 Werebat (Mob Level 55-59)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Buburimu Peninsula', note = '• (K-9), lv. 15~19, Carnivorous Crawler & Bull Dhalmel (page 3)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Caedarva Mire', note = '• (E-10), lv. 56~63, Marsh Murre (no page)\n    ◦ West exit from Nashmau\n• (I-10), lv. 56~63, Marsh Murre (no page)\n    ◦ South exit from Nashmau\n    ◦ Harder to pull without links than the West camp' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Crawler\'s Nest', note = '• (K-8/L-8), lv. 31~38, Worker Crawler & Death Jacket (page 1)\n• (F-7/F-9), lv. 38+, Soldier Crawler & Nest Beetle (page 2)\n    ◦ Careful with linking when pulling the crawlers, as well as aggroing the scorpion' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › East Ronfaure (S)', note = '• (G-8/H-8), lv. 17~20, Scarab Beetle (no page)\n    ◦ Just keep moving\n• (I-9/I-9), lv. 37-44, Colibri (no page)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Eastern Altepa Desert', note = '• (I-6), lv. 31+, Sand Beetle & Desert Dhalmel (no page)\n    ◦ Careful with Donnergugi lottery pop NM from the beetles, and Earth Elementals during weather\n    ◦ Dhalmels from 33' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Korroloka Tunnel', note = '• (H-8/J-8) Map1, lv. 16~24, Land Worm & Seeker Bats (page 1)\n    ◦ Make sure to Silence the worms\n    ◦ Can start at 15 with a good group, focussing only on the worms until 18.\n• (H-8/I-8) Map5, lv. 24~29, Lacerator & Spool Leech (page 8)\n    ◦ You\'ll need sneak/invisible to get there, which you can get from the book by selecting Circumspection for 5 tabs.\n    ◦ There\'s a book right there, handy to re-set regen/refresh' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Kuftal Tunnel', note = '• (I/J-8/9/10) NW, lv. 54~58, Sand Lizard & Rober Crab (page 1)\n    ◦ Careful with lizards links and crab aggros' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Meriphataud Mountains', note = '• (H-5) NW, lv. 15~20, Crane Fly & Hill Lizard (page 1)\n    ◦ Mobs are spread out, the party will have to constantly move up and down the canyon\n• (E-6) SW of Outpost area.\n    ◦ Multiple mobs around this area. Start on saplings, then can change to flies/Lizards and then finally goblins/Boggarts all in this one area.' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Qufim Island', note = '• (F-6) in front of the tower, lv20~23, Clippers\n    ◦ Stick with lv25~26 clippers for the first couple levels\n• (H-6) in the corridor, lv24~27, Clippers & Greater Pugils (page 3)\n    ◦ Clippers won\'t really count for the venture anymore, but since the page is 7 pugils & 3 clippers, it shouldn\'t slow things down too much' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Rolanberry Fields (S)', note = '• (E-9) by the lake, lv. 40~42, Snipper (no page)\n• (E-9) in the trees, lv. 42~47, Berry Grub (no page)\n• (F-9), lv. 43~49, Champion Crawler (no page)\n• (G-7), lv. 45~52, Champion Crawler (no page)\n    ◦ Can start at 43 with a good group\n• (F/G-6/7), lv. 52~60, Dragonfly (no page)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Sea Serpent Grotto', note = '• (L-5) Map 1, lv. 31~36, Royal Leech and Undead Bats (page 1)\n    ◦ Can start at 28 with a good group\n• (N-14) Map1, lv. 32~37, Sahagin and Vampire Bat (page 3)\n• (N-14) Map1, lv. 33~38, Sahagin and Bigclaw (page 4)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Sauromugue Champaign', note = '• (G-8), lv. 17~25, Hill Lizard & Diving Beetle (page 1)\n    ◦ Focus on lizards fist\n    ◦ Can start at 15 with a solid group\n• (F-6), lv. 26~32, Tabar Beak (no page)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › The Boyahda Tree', note = '• (H-10) Map 1, lv. 58~63, Mourioche & Robber Crab (page 2)\n• (F-6) Map 1, lv. 58~64, Moss Eater (page 3)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah', note = '• (F-8/G-8), lv. 35~42, Ogrefly, Myoxmycete, Goobbue Parasite' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › West Sarutabaruta (S)', note = '• (I-7), lv. 15~, Crawler (no page)\n• (H-11/I-11), lv19~22, River Crab (no page)\n• (J-6), lv. 30~34, Savanna Dhalmel (no page)\n• (F-10/F-11), lv. 35~40, Toad (no page)' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Standard Camps › Yuhtunga Jungle', note = '• (G-5/6), lv. 22~28, Yuhtunga Mandragora (no page)\n    ◦ Watch out for Goblins at this level range\n• (I-7), lv. 28~32, Death Jackets and Goblins (page 2)\n    ◦ Down the hole at (H-6), towards (I-7). Careful with gobs in the tunnel.' },
            { title = 'EXP: Ventures Locations › Manaburn Camps', note = '• Custom Manaburn Venture camps.\n• Monster Lvl: 20-22; Name: Enchanted Leech; Zone: Buburimu Peninsula; Location: (J-6/7)\n• Enchanted Leech — Jugner Forest — (J-9)\n• Enchanted Leech — Maze of Shakhrami — (E-7) Map 2 — Dead End Tunnel Access via A or B\n• Enchanted Leech — Meriphataud Mountains — (D-8)\n• Enchanted Leech — Pashhow Marshlands — (F-10)\n• Enchanted Leech — Valkurm Dunes — (I-6) (D/E-7) — Alcove by cliff Southern borner, against the mini-mountain.\n• Enchanted Crab — West Sarutabaruta (S) — (I-11)\n• Monster Lvl: 21-23; Name: Enchanted Crab; Zone: North Gustaberg (S); Location: (G-8) (Upper left corner)\n• Monster Lvl: 25-27; Name: Mystic Leech; Zone: Buburimu Peninsula; Location: (I-6) & (J-5/6)\n• Mystic Leech — Jugner Forest — (L-7)\n• Mystic Leech — Maze of Shakhrami — (F-9) Map 1 — Dead end. Careful with aggressive Slime on camp.\n• Mystic Leech — Meriphataud Mountains — (E-7)\n• Mystic Leech — Pashhow Marshlands — (I-11)\n• Mystic Leech — Valkurm Dunes — (K-6) & (E-6)\n• Mystic Pugil — North Gustaberg (S) — (F-8) (bottom of ramp)\n• Monster Lvl: 28-32; Name: Mana Leech; Zone: Korroloka Tunnel; Location: (C-7) Map 2; Notes: (Near Survival Guide)\n• Mana Leech — Batallia Downs — (H-8) — Lower left corner\n• Mana Leech — Rolanberry Fields — (K-7) — Lower right corner\n• Mana Leech — Sauromugue Champaign — (F-5)\n• Mana Leech — Qufim Island — (H-6) (H-8) — lower right corner lower left corner\n• Mana Leech — Yuhtunga Jungle — (F-10) — Top of cliff\n• Mana Leech — Wajaom Woodlands — (I-7) — (Nearby Bees are aggressive)\n• Monster Lvl: 38-42; Name: Magic Jar; Zone: Yhoator Jungle; Location: (J-11); Notes: With the adjustments to Pots at manaburn camps, this is now a fine camp.\n• Magic Sludge — Sea Serpent Grotto — (C-6) Map 1\n• Magic Jar — Eastern Altepa Desert — (J-7) — With the adjustments to Pots at manaburn camps, this is now a fine camp.\n• Ascended Jar — Western Altepa Desert — (H-10) — Mistaken Level range? With the adjustments to Pots at manaburn camps, this is now a fine camp.\n• Ember Djinn — Vunkerl Inlet (S) — (F-5) — Bombs - Make a pentagon shape, Shell+Protect on everyone, spaced out. Healers in the middle. Bounce mobs between players.\n• Mana Seedling — Fort Karugo-Narugo (S) — (F-5)\n• Monster Lvl: 39-43; Name: Magic Golem; Zone: The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah; Location: (H-8); Notes: Upper left corner\n• Monster Lvl: 39-40; Name: Mystic Pugil; Zone: Grauberg; Location: (G-6); Notes: Top of the Waterfall, easy access via EXP Guide[S]\n• Monster Lvl: 40-44; Name: Magic Sludge; Zone: Garlaige Citadel; Location: (G-9) Map 1\n• Monster Lvl: 41-45; Name: Magic Berry; Zone: Crawler\'s Nest; Location: (H-9) Map 1; Notes: (Subject to change)\n• Monster Lvl: 45-48; Name: Ascended Leech; Zone: Gustav Tunnel; Location: (H-8) Map 1\n• Ascended Sludge — Toraimarai Canal — (I-6) Map 1\n• Ascended Pugil — Misareaux Coast — (I-6) — Two aggressive Makara at camp\n• Ascended Pugil — East Ronfaure (S) — (H-8) — River\n• Monster Lvl: 48-52; Name: Ascended Sludge; Zone: Labyrinth of Onzozo; Location: (I-7)\n• Monster Lvl: 53-56; Name: Spectral Sludge; Zone: Bostaunieux Oubliette; Location: (H-10) Map 3\n• Spectral Snoll — Uleguerand Range — (J-9)\n• Slippery Sludge — Garlaige Citadel (S) — (I-6) — Basement - Go to B on north part of first map. Do NOT go to Banishing Gate.\n• Monster Lvl: 61-64; Name: Spectral Crab; Zone: Kuftal Tunnel; Location: (F-7) Map 2\n• Spectral Kisser — Wajaom Woodlands — (J-8)\n• Spectral Crab — Rolanberry Fields (S) — (K-10)\n• Monster Lvl: 64-66; Name: Spectral Kisser; Zone: Bhaflau Thickets; Location: (G-7) Map 1\n• Monster Lvl: 65-68; Name: Wizard Leech; Zone: The Boyahda Tree; Location: (G/H-9) Map 3; Notes: By Ancient Goobbue Terrible camp, aggressive mobs everywhere\n• Wizard Leech — Caedarva Mire — (H-10)\n• Wizard Leech — Cape Teriggan — (I-7) — Another bad camp, lots of nearby aggressive mobs\n• Monster Lvl: 66-69; Name: Wizard Golem; Zone: Ro\'Maeve; Location: (D-10)\n• Monster Lvl: 67-70; Name: Wizard Uragnite; Zone: Bibiki Bay; Location: (G-9/10)\n• Monster Lvl: 69-72; Name: Wizard Sludge; Zone: Aydeewa Subterrane; Location: (H-7) Map 6; Notes: Enter from Wajaom Woodlands #10' },
            { title = 'Milestone Rewards: Overview', note = '• Milestone Rewards are available for ACE and WEW characters only.\n• To participate in the Adventurer Milestone Rewards players must complete objectives. These objectives vary for new or existing players.' },
            { title = 'Milestone Rewards: New Player Milestone', note = '• The New Player milestone is a static objective and is always active, and are without any time limit or other conditions.\n• Rewards for the initial new player Milestone are always active.\n    ◦ You may claim this on both ACE characters, unlike existing Milestone campaigns.\n• Rewards for existing player Milestones are active for a limited time.\n• New players must obtain rank 10 in any nation and at least one job leveled to 75.\n• Upon completing the requirement players may receive their reward via the Spatial Anomaly in Castle Zvahl Baileys at (J-8).\n• Reward choices include any one of the following:\n• Any Stage 4 Relic Weapon\n    ◦ ⚠️ Players still need to complete the final upgrade, see Relic Weapons. Consider the fully upgraded relic from Crafting Rewards instead\n• A "Mythos Token" which allows players to complete the HNM trophy rewards stage of a Mythic Weapon.\n    ◦ ⚠️ Players still need to obtain the T4 ZNM trophies, imperial gold pieces, and alexandrite.\n• A Defending Ring\n• An Octave Club\n    ◦ This has been modified to be the exact equivalent of the Kraken Club as a rare/ex reward for Milestones due to it\'s popularity.\n    ◦ The Octave Club can not be equipped at the same time as the Kraken Club.' },
            { title = 'Milestone Rewards: Existing Player Milestone', note = '• Note: There is currently no active Existing Player Milestone campaign.\n• Existing Player milestones are limited time events with a varying objective.\n• You may claim one reward per player per campaign.\n• You may not claim a reward on more than one character.\n    ◦ This means you and your mule—if you have one—can not both receive an item. This is referred to as "double-dipping."\n• Note: Players must be at least 90 days old before claiming this prize.\n    ◦ You may complete the criteria before then and receive credit, but 90 days must have passed.' },
            { title = 'Milestone Rewards: Rewards', note = '• Upon completing the requirement players may receive their reward via the Spatial Anomaly in Castle Zvahl Baileys at (J-8).' },
            { title = 'Login Campaigns: Overview', note = '• Login Campaigns are run year round on CatsEyeXI. Rewarded items are hand picked and regularly rotated.\n• Speak with any Greeter Moogle, located near the Mog House of the following areas:\n• Windurst Walls (C-13)\n• Port San d\'Oria (J-10)\n• Port Bastok (J-13)\n• Each Login Campaign starts the first day of the month and ends the last day of the month with no down time between.\n    ◦ Points are spendable until the last moment, and then lost the first of the month.\n• First login rewards 500 points, each subsequent login 200 points\n• Only 1,500 points will carry over to the next Login Campaign.\n• Crystal Warriors cannot obtain login points.\n• Wings Era Warriors have their own separate login rewards.\n• Items are subject to change in the future.' },
    } },
    { name = 'Crafting and gathering', group = 'Server', desc = 'Custom synthesis recipes and materials, crafting guide, crafting rewards, HELM and digging. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatseyeXI_Crafting_Guide, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Crafting_Rewards, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Synthesis, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/HELM, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Digging', steps = {
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Welcome to the CatsEyeXI crafting guide!', note = '• This guide will review some basics and provide an optimal skill up path for each craft.' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: General Information', note = '• CatsEyeXI uses the following rates, adjusted from retail.\n• Main Craft Level Cap: 110\n• Sub Craft Level Cap: 70\n• Crafting Skillup Rate: 1.5x [ACE] [CW]\n• Crafting Skillup Multiplier: 3.0x [ACE]\n• Fishing Skillup Rate: 3.0x [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Fishing Skillup Multiplier: 1.0x [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Owing to their self-found nature, Crystal Warriors may skill all crafts up to 110.[CW]\n• There are no crafting myths active here. Your cardinal direction, day of the week, or weather active will have ZERO impact on the final results.\n• You can skill up 11 levels over the item\'s natural cap.\n• Adv.Support gives -30% Item loss on break chance.\n• Crafting Levels\n• For every craft skill at level 30 or higher, your rate of material loss on any failed synth is reduced by 1%.\n• For every craft skill at level 50 or higher, your rate of material loss is reduced by another 1%.\n• For every craft skill at level 70 or higher, your rate of material loss is reduced by another 1%, and your overall synthesis success rate increases by 1%.\n    ◦ This means that if you have all craft skills at level 70, you will innately have:\n    ◦ A -24% chance to lose a material after a synth break\n    ◦ A +8% chance to all synth success rates\n• (Note that the the chance to lose each material after a synth break can be no lower than 20%, and success rate can be no higher than 99%.)\n• The /lastsynth command works and can be used such as in the following example macro.\n• Taking your craft to 110 level skill is possible, but you will have challenges as this is a level 75 capped server, and many of the materials post skill cap 100 are not available. Take advantage of skill ups over natural recipe caps.' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Crafting Bonus Items', note = '• In addition to guild point purchased items, the following items are also available.\n• Item: Artificer\'s Ring; Obtained From: Purchased with 1000 Venture Points at Populox in Upper Jeuno.\n• Item: Chocobo Shirt; Obtained From: Adventurer Coupon trade-in\n• Item: Craftkeeper\'s Ring; Obtained From: Purchased with 1000 Venture Points at Populox in Upper Jeuno.\n• Item: Craftmaster\'s Ring; Obtained From: Purchased with 2000 Venture Points at Populox in Upper Jeuno.\n• Item: Kupo Shield; Obtained From: Leveling a craft to 100, purchasing the "Way of the " Guild Point Key Item, and trading the requested item to Nudara in Bastok Markets (I-8), will grant the player with a Kupo Shield.\n• Item: Midras\'s Helm +1; Obtained From: Purchased with 3000 Venture Points at Populox in Upper Jeuno.\n• Item: Bonze Cape (Back, Lv25, All Jobs, DEF:2 MP+3 INT+2, Increases synthesis skill gain rate (+10%), Rare, Ex); Obtained From: Potential reward when trading Silver Shark to Marceo; Notes: Synthesis skill gain rate +10%\n• Item: Shaper\'s Shawl; Obtained From: Potential reward when trading Matsya to Marceo; Notes: Synthesis skill gain rate +25%' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Crafting Bonus Items › Crafting Torques', note = '• These can be found in treasure caskets inside dungeons or purchased from from Domain Officer in Upper Jeuno at (G-9) for 15,000 Domain Invasion Beads.\n• All eight crafting torques can be combined using synergy into Artisan\'s Torque (Lv1, All Jobs, Synthesis skill +2, Decreases likelihood of synthesis material loss +2%)\n• Crafting & Hobbies — Beads — Treasure Casket\n• Alchemist\'s Torque — 15,000 — Ve\'Lugannon Palace\n• Carver\'s Torque — 15,000 — The Boyahda Tree\n• Tanner\'s Torque — 15,000 — Quicksand Caves\n• Smithy\'s Torque — 15,000 — Ifrit\'s Cauldron\n• Goldsmith\'s Torque — 15,000 — Den of Rancor\n• Boneworker\'s Torque — 15,000 — Temple of Uggalepih\n• Weaver\'s Torque — 15,000 — The Shrine of Ru\'Avitau\n• Culinarian\'s Torque — 15,000 — Gustav Tunnel\n• Fisher\'s Torque (Lv. 75) — 15,000 — Outer Horutoto Ruins\n• Field Torque (Lv. 75) — 15,000 — Gusgen Mines\n• Field Rope (Lv. 75) — 15,000 — Dangruf Wadi' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Crafting Bonus Items › Crafting Stalls', note = '• Mega moglification is available after placing a crafting stall in your moghouse. This will give you + 5 skill to your craft. Trade your items to a synergy furnace to receive your crafting stall. This is a custom synergy recipe for CatsEyeXI, and can be found on the Synergy page.' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Crafting Bonus Items › Crafting & Fishing Food', note = '• Food — Effect — Notes\n• Cherry Macaron — Increases rate of synthesis success by 3% Increases synthesis skill gain rate by 3% — Crafted: Cooking 35 (Requires Patissier) <Add Info RE Curio Vendor\n• Coffee Macaron — Increases rate of synthesis success by 5% Increases synthesis skill gain rate by 5% — Crafted: Cooking 55 (Requires Patissier) <Add Info RE Curio Vendor\n• Kitron Macaron — Increases rate of synthesis success by 7% Increases synthesis skill gain rate by 7% — Crafted: Cooking 75 (Requires Patissier)\n• Fisherman\'s Feast — Increases rate of Fishing skill gain by +5% — Crafted: Cooking 102' },
            { title = 'Crafting Guide: Farming Rare Items', note = '• Many synthesis recipes require you to farm the items directly from the monsters. Our website database has a very powerful item lookup tool. Use this to find the best camps and targets to gather rare materials.' },
