            { title = 'Synthesis: Custom Recipes (Jug Pet)', note = '• The following recipes are custom created.\n• Equipment:\n• Item: Fun Dip; Crafts: Cooking 97; Materials: Water Crystal Mand. Sprout x2 G. Sheep Meat Isleracea' },
            { title = 'HELM: Overview', note = '• CatsEyeXI is home to various zones of custom Harvesting, Excavation, Logging, and Mining.\n• Access to a few of these unique HELM zones must be earned by completing a one time quest, detailed on the Quests page.\n    ◦ Excavating Aht Urghan: Clink to the Past\n    ◦ Harvesting The Crawlers\' Nest: Thread Bare\n    ◦ Mining Gustav Tunnel (CW Only): Here be Dragons\n• Below are the CatsEye unique HELM zones and their results.\n    ◦ Rarity information is as follows:\n    ◦ (Guaranteed) - Guaranteed (100% drop rate, 1/1)\n    ◦ (Very Common) - Very common (24%)\n    ◦ (Common) - Common (15%)\n    ◦ (Uncommon) - Uncommon (10%)\n    ◦ (Rare) - Rare (5%)\n    ◦ (Very Rare) - Very Rare (1%)\n    ◦ (Super Rare) - Super Rare (0.5%)\n    ◦ (Ultra Rare) - Ultra Rare (0.1%)\n• There are currently no custom maps for these HELM points.\n    ◦ Anyone who wishes to make and share one is free to do so, and it will be uploaded.' },
            { title = 'HELM: Harvesting › Batallia Downs', note = '• Can also get Thyme and Winter Sage (but we can\'t add them to the table right now...) Location: Bottom of J-7/8\n• Harvesting:\n• Sharug Greens\n• Beaugreens\n• Azouph Greens\n• Frost Turnip\n• San d\'Or. Carrot' },
            { title = 'HELM: Harvesting › Crawlers\' Nest', note = '• Deep in the heart of Derfland lies a labyrinth of twisting tunnels, where many creatures make their nest. The Iron Musketeers in collaboration with the Department of Industry have designated new sites to search for valuable resources in this previously untapped area. This area will become available after completing a quest.\n• (Requires Quest: Thread Bare)\n• Harvesting:\n• Crawler Cocoon (Very Common)\n• Beehive Chip (Common)\n• Silk Thread (Common)\n• Danceshroom (Common)\n• Woozyshroom (Uncommon)\n• Insect Wing (Uncommon)\n• Crawler Egg (Rare)\n• Rolanberry (Rare)\n• Silver Thread (Rare)\n• Agaricus (Rare)\n• Royal Jelly (Very Rare)\n• Rainbow Thread (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Harvesting › Pashhow Marshlands', note = '• The thriving marsh of Derfland is home to a diverse array of creatures. While seeming an unlikely place to strike rich, this area has become of increasing significance to botanists and alchemists who seek fresh materials for their own interests.\n• Harvesting:\n• Insect Wing (Common)\n• Boyahda Moss (Common)\n• Malboro Vine (Common)\n• Beastman Blood (Uncommon)\n• Puffball (Rare)\n• Wijnruit (Rare)\n• Rain Lily (Rare)\n• Dahlia (Very Rare)\n• Copper Frog (Very Rare)\n• Reishi Mushroom (Very Rare)\n• Grain Seeds (Very Rare)\n• Porxie Wing (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Harvesting › Tahrongi Canyon', note = '• Only during Gobbie Gathering. Union Commendation (Very Rare) can also be obtained upon harvesting.\n• Harvesting:\n• Tahrongi Cactus (Very Common)\n• Cactus Stems (Very Common)\n• Saruta Cotton (Common)\n• Crawler Cocoon (Common)\n• Gar. Wildgrass (Common)\n• Dragon Fruit (Uncommon)\n• Kitron (Rare)\n• Persikos (Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Excavation › Arrapago Reef', note = '• Lost at sea, the wrecks of many ruined vessels come to rest upon these rocks. An accumulated trove of abandoned articles turned this once empty ghost yard into a hive for treasure hunters.\n• (Requires Quest: Clink to the Past)\n• ??? Item Appraisers:\n• Ciciroon (J-9) Al Zahbi / Gegeroon (H-8) Nashmau\n• ??? Sword: Scimitar,...\n• ??? Headpiece: Leather Bandana, Jaridah Khud,...\n• ??? Ingot: Silver Ingot, Platinum Ingot,...\n• Excavation:\n• Corsair Bullet (Very Common)\n• Shall Shell (Common)\n• Imp Horn (Common)\n• Firesand (Uncommon)\n• Silica (Uncommon)\n• Old Bullet Box (Rare)\n• Imperial Cermet (Rare)\n• Petrified Log (Rare)\n• Soulflayer Robe (Rare)\n• Soulflayer Staff (Rare)\n• ??? Sword (Very Rare)\n• ??? Headpiece (Very Rare)\n• ??? Ingot (Very Rare)\n• Orobon Lure (Super Rare)\n• Minium (Ultra Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Excavation › Aydeewa Subterrane', note = '• Remnants of the once great Olduum civilization litter the catacombs below Wajaom. Previously only in the purview of Qiqirn archeology, these sites have gained new interest from the Empire’s mercenaries, looking to find their fortunes.\n• (Requires Quest: Clink to the Past)\n• ??? Item Appraisers:\n• Ciciroon (J-9) Al Zahbi / Gegeroon (H-8) Nashmau\n• Excavation:\n• Pebble (Common)\n• Colibri Beak (Common)\n• Blk. Tiger Fang (Uncommon)\n• Silver Leaf (Uncommon)\n• Marid Tusk (Rare)\n• Silica (Rare)\n• Firesand (Rare)\n• Gold Leaf (Rare)\n• ??? Necklace (Very Rare)\n• ??? Earring (Very Rare)\n• ??? Ring (Very Rare)\n• Qiqirn Cape (Super Rare)\n• Platinum Leaf (Super Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Excavation › Fei\'Yin', note = '• Reports of lost Zilart artifacts have recently surfaced from the ruined tower in Fauregandi. Under authority of the Archduke himself, the Armathrwn Society is summoning adventurers from across the land to excavate the ruins and uncover its secrets.\n• Excavation:\n• Pebble (Very Common)\n• Magic Pot Shard (Common)\n• Bat Fang (Uncommon)\n• Golem Shard (Uncommon)\n• Doll Shard (Uncommon)\n• Mercury (Rare)\n• Mythril Ore (Rare)\n• Phil. Stone (Rare)\n• Cermet Chunk (Rare)\n• Fire Ore (Very Rare)\n• Granite (Super Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Excavation › Labyrinth of Onzozo', note = '• Beneath the waves of the Pamtam Straits, winding tunnels lead to the resting place of legendary beasts from another age. Once a well kept secret of the Goblin race, adventurers of Vana\'diel are beginning to unearth the mysteries of this long lost trove of archaeological treasures.\n• (Requires Quest: Broken Bones)\n• Excavation:\n• Bone Chip (Common)\n• Scorpion Claw (Common)\n• Manticore Fang (Uncommon)\n• Manticore Hide (Uncommon)\n• Coral Fragment (Rare)\n• Shall Shell (Rare)\n• Giant Femur (Rare)\n• H.Q. Coeurl Hide (Rare)\n• H.Q. Scp. Shell (Rare)\n• Coeurl Whisker (Rare)\n• Wyvern Scales (Rare)\n• Wyvern Skin (Very Rare)\n• Unicorn Horn (Super Rare)\n• Dragon Bone (Super Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Logging › Bibiki Bay', note = '• The Optistery at Windurst has restored a previously indecipherable text. This mysterious manuscript tells of a land with bountiful fine wood for building staves and bows, in the bay of Gugru Blue off the shores Mindartia. The Sibyl Guards have requested the aid of adventurers to scout the vicinity.\n• Logging:\n• Holly Log (Common)\n• Lauan Log (Common)\n• Rosewood Log (Uncommon)\n• Mahogany Log (Rare)\n• Ebony Log (Rare)\n• Bird Feather (Rare)\n• Bird Egg (Very Rare)\n• Lizard Egg (Very Rare)\n• Phoenix Feather (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Logging › Grauberg (S)', note = '• In the rolling hills of Grauberg lies the Witchfire Glen, home to the Sidhe, a peaceful race of pixies. However, their magical trees recently caught the unwelcome attention of adventurers.\n• Logging:\n• Yew Log (Common)\n• Elm Log (Common)\n• Chestnut Log (Common)\n• Ash Log (Rare)\n• Ebony Log (Rare)\n• Teak Log (Rare)\n• Jacaranda Log (Very Rare)\n• Faerie Apple (Very Rare)\n• Divine Log (Ultra Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Logging › La Theine Plateau', note = '• Only during Gobbie Gathering. Union Commendation (Very Rare) can also be obtained upon logging.\n• Logging:\n• Ash Log (Common)\n• Chestnut Log (Common)\n• Ebony Log (Rare)\n• Mahogany Log (Rare)\n• Petrified Log (Very Rare)\n• Acorn (Very Rare)\n• Lacquer Tree Log (Very Rare)\n• Divine Log (Ultra Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Mining › Garlaige Citadel (S)', note = '• Built into rock, the heavily fortified citadel of Garlaige rests atop caverns, which have now been reinforced to allow miners to commence their activities.\n• Mining:\n• Flint Stone (Very Common)\n• Bomb Ash (Common)\n• Iron Ore (Uncommon)\n• Aluminum Ore (Uncommon)\n• Marble Nugget (Uncommon)\n• Scorpion Shell (Rare)\n• Bomb Arm (Rare)\n• Red Rock (Rare)\n• Adaman Ore (Very Rare)\n• H.Q. Scp. Shell (Very Rare)\n• Orichalcum Ore (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Mining › Grauberg (S)', note = '• Upon the peaks of Skyrend, many a miner has met their end at the clutches of the fearsome Ajattara who prowl to guard their nest from any intruders who would dare take their treasure. Location: C/D-8.\n• Mining:\n• Pebble (Common)\n• Iron Sand (Common)\n• Iron Ore (Uncommon)\n• Wyvern Wing (Uncommon)\n• Adaman Ore (Rare)\n• Wyvern Scales (Rare)\n• Wyvern Skin (Very Rare)\n• Scholar Stone (Very Rare)\n• Wootz Ore (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Mining › Ordelle\'s Caves', note = '• A Mining Expedition sent by San d\'Oria has discovered new mineral deposits in Ordelle\'s Caves. Curilla V Mecru has called on the Temple Knights to secure the surrounding area, now inviting adventurers to investigate.\n• Mining:\n• Copper Ore (Common)\n• Silver Ore (Common)\n• Bomb Ash (Common)\n• Mythril Ore (Uncommon)\n• Silver Beastcoin (Uncommon)\n• Rock Salt (Rare)\n• Gold Beastcoin (Rare)\n• Gold Ore (Rare)\n• Fire Cluster (Rare)\n• Platinum Ore (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Mining › Gustav Tunnel (CW Only)', note = '• Khartes, in Selbina has heard rumours of a wyvern guarding mineral veins in Gustav Tunnel. He has asked adventurers to investigate and report back any sightings.\n• [CW] (Requires Quest: Here Be Dragons)\n• Mining:\n• Flint Stone (Common)\n• Iron Ore (Common)\n• Silver Beastcoin (Common)\n• Darksteel Ore (Uncommon)\n• Mythril Ore (Uncommon)\n• Mtl. Beastcoin (Uncommon)\n• Gold Beastcoin (Rare)\n• Gold Ore (Rare)\n• Heavy Metal (Rare)\n• Orichalcum Ore (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: Mining › Konschtat Highlands', note = '• Only during Gobbie Gathering. Union Commendation (Very Rare) can also be obtained upon mining.\n• Mining:\n• Iron Ore (Very Common)\n• Silver Ore (Very Common)\n• Gold Ore (Common)\n• Darksteel Ore (Common)\n• Adaman Ore (Rare)\n• Platinum Ore (Rare)\n• Orichalcum Ore (Very Rare)' },
            { title = 'HELM: General Changes', note = '• While the above tables are fully custom, there are also a few changes to HELM results of established zones.\n• Only items that have been modified or added to existing zones will be listed below. All other HELM results follow BG Wiki gathering pages.\n    ◦ The exception being that mining in any zone can result in elemental ores (Earth Ore, etc). A table isn\'t needed for that.\n• Zone: East Ronfaure (S); Item: Jacaranda Log; Drop Note: Rarity Decreased from (Super Rare) to (Very Rare).\n• Persikos — (Common), added to zone.\n• Zone: Jugner Forest (S); Item: Jacaranda Log; Drop Note: Rarity Decreased, still (Very Rare), but higher than Ronfaure.\n• Persikos — (Common), added to zone.\n• Zone: Fort K-N; Item: Persikos; Drop Note: (Common), added to zone.\n• Zone: Yuhtunga Jungle; Item: Kitron; Drop Note: (Common), added to zone.\n• Zone: Yhoator Jungle; Item: Kitron; Drop Note: (Common), added to zone.\n• Zone: Bhaflau Thickets; Item: Felicifruit; Drop Note: (Very Rare)~(Rare), added to zone.\n• Zone: Wajaom Woodlands; Item: Felicifruit; Drop Note: (Very Rare)~(Rare), added to zone.\n• Zone: Yhoator Jungle; Item: Agaricus; Drop Note: (Rare), added to zone.\n• Zone: Yuhtunga Jungle; Item: Agaricus; Drop Note: (Rare), added to zone.\n• Zone: Bhaflau Thickets; Item: Kitron; Drop Note: (Rare), added to zone.\n• Zone: Halvung; Item: Khroma Ore; Drop Note: (Super Rare), added to zone.' },
            { title = 'Digging: Chocobo Digging', note = '• Each character has a limit of 300 items from digging per real life day. The digging limit can not be increased. This limit applies to all account types (including Crystal Warriors). This limit resets at JST midnight.\n• Elemental Ore may be dug up during weather in select zones (not RotZ or ToAU) during a 7~21% moon phase.\n• Note: Digging doesn\'t work in Xarcabard and Uleguerand Range, maybe others.' },
    } },
    { name = 'Fishing', group = 'Server', desc = 'Fishing changes and the fishing levelling guide. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatseyeXI/Fishing_Guide, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Fishing', steps = {
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Welcome to the CatsEyeXI Fishing Guide!', note = '• This guide will review some basics and provide a recommended path to work your way to 110.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: General Information', note = '• CatsEyeXI uses the following rates, adjusted from retail.\n• Fishing Skillup Rate: 3.0x [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Fishing Skillup Multiplier: 1.0x [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Fishing may be skilled up to 110 regardless of any other craft progress.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Helpful Gear', note = '• Fisherman\'s (Fsh. Tunica, Fsh. Gloves, Fisherman\'s Hose, Fisherman\'s Boots) or Angler\'s (Angler\'s Tunica, Angler\'s Gloves, Angler\'s Hose, Angler\'s Boots) set should be your starting gear. Crafted or bought from other players.\n• Waders can be obtained from Fishing Guild Points.\n• Fisherman\'s Apron can be obtained from Fishing Guild Points.\n• Fisher\'s Torque can be obtained from golden Treasure Caskets in Outer Horutoto Ruins or through Domain Invasion for 15,000 beads.\n• Fishermn. Stall can be obtained by purchasing an Fishermn. Emblem with Fishing Guild Points then trading it with the following items to a Synergy Furnace: Water Cluster x12, Beech Lumber, Oak Lumber x4,\n• Grass Cloth, and Fastwater F. Rod. This stall provides Mega Moglification: Fishing which gives a +5 bonus to your fishing skill.\n• Mariner\'s Equipment can be obtained through ventures, it will increase your daily fishing fatigue so it is advised to obtain this as soon as you can (boots then chest as a priority). More details on the gear can be found here.\n• Tlahtlamah Glasses can also be obtained through ventures.\n• Trainee\'s Specs. would be an easier to obtain alternative, although it only work up to lv.40 fishing.\n• Lu Shang\'s F. Rod can be obtained through The Rivalry/The Competition or brought from other players.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Fatigue', note = '• You can use the command !fatigue to view your current fatigue. More details on CatsEyeXI\'s fishing fatigue limits can be found here.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Guild Points', note = '• After obtaining Novice rank (Lvl. 28+) you will be able to acquire Fishing Guild Points. Most fish are not stocked (or restocked) in NPC shops so you will either need to rely on purchasing fish from other players or fishing them entirely yourself.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Marceo', note = '• Marceo is a custom CatsEyeXI NPC located in Norg at (H-9) which allows players (Lvl. 15+) to trade fish for rewards. More info on the fish you can trade and the rewards you receive can be found here.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Crooked Jones & Sinister Stash', note = '• Crooked Jones and the Sinister Stash are a custom CatsEyeXI NPCs located in Norg at (H-8) which allows players (Lvl. 20+) to provide a random selection of fish daily in exchanged for a custom currency, "doubloons".\n• More details and a list of rewards can be found here.\n• It is recommended once you hit 5000 total to buy the shovel as you will be able to do an extra daily treasure hunt for more rewards!' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Fish Recommendations', note = '• The ideal range for getting skillups is to catch fish that at 9-13 levels above your natural skill level.\n• The below recommendations assume you do not have a Lu Shang\'s F. Rod, if you do feel free to ignore rod suggestions as Lu works for everything. Some legendary fish will require it and also be able to break it, so level Woodworking to 70 to repair it yourself. Otherwise you will need complete The Immortal Lu Shang to repair it.\n• Fish: Crayfish; Level Cap: 7; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Little Worm; Location(s): West Ronfaure Knightwell (G-10)\n• Fish: Moat Carp; Level Cap: 11; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Insect Ball; Location(s): West Ronfaure Knightwell (G-10)\n• Fish: Quus; Level Cap: 19; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Sabiki Rig; Location(s): Korroloka Tunnel pool (K-6)\n• Fish: Cheval Salmon; Level Cap: 21; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Fly Lure; Location(s): East Ronfaure river\n• Fish: Nebimonite; Level Cap: 27; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): Sea Serpent Grotto pool (J-12)\n• Fish: Pipira; Level Cap: 29; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Minnow; Location(s): Windurst Waters\n• Fish: Ogre Eel; Level Cap: 35; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): South Gustaberg sea, East Sarutabaruta sea, West Sarutabaruta sea\n• Fish: Nosteau Herring; Level Cap: 39; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Sardine Ball; Location(s): Qufim Island (H-6)\n• Fish: Coral Butterfly; Level Cap: 40; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Worm Lure; Location(s): Kazham\n• Fish: Black Eel; Level Cap: 47; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Trout Ball; Location(s): Zeruhn Mines (H-11)\n• Fish: Icefish; Level Cap: 49; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Sabiki Rig; Location(s): Beaucedine Glacier ponds (H-9)\n• Fish: Giant Donko; Level Cap: 50; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Frog Lure; Location(s): Rabao / Eastern Altepa Desert oasis (F-9)\n• Fish: Elshimo Newt; Level Cap: 60; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Frog Lure; Location(s): Yhoator Jungle pool (E-9)\n• Fish: Crescent Fish; Level Cap: 69; Rod: Halcyon Rod; Bait: Fly Lure; Location(s): East Sarutabaruta Lake Tepokalipuka (F/G-9)\n• Fish: Zebra Eel; Level Cap: 70; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): Den of Rancor (E-9)\n• Fish: Bladefish; Level Cap: 71; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Meatball / Slice of Bluetail; Location(s): South Gustaberg sea, East Sarutabaruta sea, West Sarutabaruta sea\n• Fish: Gavial Fish; Level Cap: 81; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Lizard Lure / Meatball; Location(s): North Gustaberg Drachenfall (F-7/8) accessed through Dangruf Wadi\n• Fish: Bastore Bream; Level Cap: 86; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): Port Windurst / Port Bastok\n• Fish: Mercanbaligi; Level Cap: 86; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): Nashmau\n• Fish: Ahtapot; Level Cap: 90; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Shrimp Lure; Location(s): Nashmau\n• Fish: Emperor Fish; Level Cap: 91; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Peeled Crayfish / Trout Ball; Location(s): Beaucedine Glacier ponds / Jugner Forest Lake Mechieume river mouth\n• Fish: Dil; Level Cap: 96; Rod: Halcyon Rod # / Hume Fishing Rod #; Bait: Sliced Cod; Location(s): Talacca Cove\n• Fish: Black Sole; Level Cap: 96; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod # / Halcyon Rod # / Hume Fishing Rod #; Bait: Sinking Minnow / Sliced Cod; Location(s): Port Jeuno / Lower Jeuno / Qufim Island pond (H-7)\n• Fish: Armored Pisces; Level Cap: 108; Rod: Composite Fishing Rod §#; Bait: Frog Lure / Minnow; Location(s): Oldton Movalpolos\n• Fish: Gerrothorax; Level Cap: 110; Rod: May Break: Composite Fishing Rod; Bait: Meatball; Location(s): Pashhow Marshlands (S)\n• §: Fish may be too small #: Line may snap:\n• It is always best to prioritize fish you can both level and obtain venture points on. A list of venture fish can be found here.' },
            { title = 'Fishing Guide: Rank Tests', note = '• Every ten skill levels, you are required to prove to the guild that you "have what it takes" by catching (or buying) a Fishing item of the guild\'s choosing. This item can be turned in once you have reached an "8" in skill (8, 28, 48, etc.) or higher (up to the cap). Once you have the requisite skill, speak with the Guild Master, https://www.bg-wiki.com/ffxi/Thubu Parohren Thubu Parohren\n• Rank: Recruit; Item: Moat Carp; Level: 8-10\n• Rank: Initiate; Item: Cheval Salmon; Level: 18-20\n• Rank: Novice; Item: Giant Catfish; Level: 28-30\n• Rank: Apprentice; Item: Gugru Tuna; Level: 38-40\n• Rank: Journeyman; Item: Monke-Onke; Level: 48-50\n• Rank: Craftsman; Item: Bhefhel Marlin; Level: 58-60\n• Rank: Artisan; Item: Bladefish; Level: 68-70\n• Rank: Adept; Item: Three-eyed Fish; Level: 78-80\n• Rank: Veteran; Item: Gigant Squid; Level: 88-90\n• Rank: Expert; Item: Tiger Shark; Level: 98-100' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Crooked Jones', note = '• Located in Norg at (H-8), Crooked Jones collects fish from the Fishing Ventures system in exchange for a new currency called "doubloons".\n• Each day, one lower tier fish will be selected (max. 60 each), one middle tier fish will be selected (max. 40 each), and one legendary fish will be selected (max. 15).\n• These fish must be traded to a Sinister Stash. Multiple different fish of varying quantities can be traded at once.\n• Players must be at least 20 fishing to interact with Jones and his stash.\n• If you trade the maximum amount of all three fish, you will get a bonus of 100 extra doubloons.\n• Item: Brigand\'s Shovel (Staff, Lv40, All Jobs, DMG:35, Delay:402, HP+10 Water+8, Improves excavation results, Rare, Ex); Doubloons: 5000; Info: Required to participate in Treasure Hunts\n• Item: Crab Cap +1; Doubloons: 8000; Info: Gain various Crab costumes\n• Item: Buccaneer\'s Chart; Doubloons: 10000; Info: Used to spawn a new encounter in Cape Terrigan\n• Item: Brigand\'s Eyepatch (Head, Lv50, All Jobs, DEF:15 MP+15, CHR+3 Water+10, "Expert Angler"+2, Rare, Ex); Doubloons: 12000; Info: Improves rate of gold arrows and increases daily capacity\n• Item: Red Crab Mount; Doubloons: 15000; Info: [ACE] ACE Only\n• Item: Shaper\'s Shawl; Doubloons: 15000; Info: [CW] CW Only\n• Item: Rusty Fishing Hook; Doubloons: 20000; Info: Used in the process of creating the Fishing ultimate weapon' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Crooked Jones › Sinister Stash locations', note = '• Norg at (H-8)\n• Lower Jeuno at (I-8) in the Merry Ministrel Meadhouse' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Crooked Jones › Treasure Hunts', note = '• Once the player has obtained the Brigand\'s Shovel, Crooked Jones will give the option to participate in a Treasure Hunt. This may be done once per day. A Pirate\'s Key must first be obtained from fished up monsters in a specified area. Upon obtaining the key, Jones will reveal the location of the buried treasure. Using the Brigand\'s Shovel, players must find the exact location and open the chest with the Pirate\'s Key, yielding many doubloons and multiple new items.\n• Players may obtain various rewards including legendary fish bait, a mystic key, a Pirate\'s Chart, and the unique Buccaneer\'s Chart.\n    ◦ Trade the Mystic Key to a chest in Sea Serpent Grotto for a large gil reward, see Fishing Guild NM for locations.' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Crooked Jones › Buccaneer\'s Chart', note = '• After obtaining a chart, players may trade it to the Unsettled Sand at (H-9) in Cape Teriggan. The fight is a higher version of the same one for the Pirate\'s Chart fight. You will fight against a Sahagin, a Manta, and a Crab.\n• Level 70 Cap.\n• 3 Players.\n• 30 Minutes.\n• Notable rewards include:\n• Albatross Ring (Guaranteed)\n• Penguin Ring (Guaranteed)\n• Dwarf Pugil x0~2 (Common)\n• Drill Calamary x0~2 (Common)\n• Mercurial kunai (Katana, Lv70, NIN, DMG:17, Delay:190, Occasionally attacks 2-3 times, Rare) (Rare)' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Daily Cap / Fatigue', note = '• New ACE and Wings Era Warrior characters start with a limit of 20 fish per real life day. To increase this limit:\n• ACE characters must complete Limit Break 3 (Whence Blows the Wind) to increase their limit to 300.\n• WeW characters must unlock their subjob (The Old Lady or Elder Memories) to increase their limit to 300.\n• Fishing fatigue can be further increased via equipping the Ebisu Fishing Rod (+1) or Mariner\'s Tunic/Boots (+1/2) obtained from Special Ventures - Fishing.\n    ◦ Every +1 is +10% more fish. For example, the limit would be 330 fish if an Ebisu Rod is owned. This multiplier is additive.\n• Crystal Warriors are exempt from the fishing fatigue limit.\n• This limit resets at JST midnight.' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Guide', note = '• See the Fishing Guide.' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Marceo\'s Guttable Fish', note = '• Marceo is a custom CatsEyeXI NPC located in Norg at (H-9) which allows players (Lvl. 15+) to trade fish for rewards.\n• In addition to the table below, players can also trade Marceo all of the Zaldon fish and receive the usual items and double the gil amount\n    ◦ (14) Greedie — Sardine Ball x1~6 (Very Common) Crayfish Ball x1~6 (Very Common) Silver Beastcoin (Very Common) Peeled Crayfish x1~6 (Uncommon) Remedy (Uncommon) Bronze Moogle Belt (Rare) Moat Carp Creel (Very Rare) Rancid Coffee (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (16) Copper Frog — Insect Wing x1~3 (Very Common) Copper Ore x1~2 (Common) Pebble (Common) Mercury (Uncommon) Tin Ore x1~2 (Rare) Zinc Ore (Rare) Moat Carp Creel (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (20) Forest Carp — Insect Ball x1~6 (Very Common) (70%) Norg Earring (Common) Gold Beastcoin (Uncommon) Scarlet Stone (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (26) Gurnard — Shihei x1~6 (Very Common) Chestnut Log (Common) Elm Log (Common) Oak Log (Common) Beastmen\'s Seal (Uncommon) Wind Arrow x3~9 (Uncommon) Moat Carp Creel (Uncommon) Giant\'s Earring (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (28) Blindfish — Darksteel Nugget (Very Common) Darksteel Nugget x1~2 (Common) Eye Drops (Common) Sairui-Ran x1~6 (Uncommon) Dark Cluster (Uncommon) Dark Card x1~6 (Uncommon) Blinding Potion (Rare) Goblin Mess Tin (Rare) Rebel Earring (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (29) Pipira — Saruta Cotton x1~3 (Common) Clump of Moko Grass x1~3 (Common) Silk Thread x1~2 (Uncommon) Moat Carp Creel x1~3 (Common) Grain Seeds x1~4 (Common) Clear Earring x1 (Super Rare) Papaka Grass x1~3 (Very Common) Crawler Calculus x1 (Common)\n    ◦ (31) Yayinbaligi — Rosewood Log (Very Common) (20%) Ebony Log (Very Common) (20%) Chimera Blood (Common) Nashmau Earring (Uncommon) Imp Horn (Uncommon) Water Card x1~6 (Uncommon) Almond (Rare) Alexandrite (Rare) Imp. Brz. Piece (Rare)\n    ◦ (37) Veydal Wrasse — Moat Carp Creel (Very Common) Ram Horn (Very Common) Ebony Log (Common) Uragnite Shell (Common) Iron Nugget x1~3 (Uncommon) Aht Urhgan Brass (Uncommon) Aileron Mantle (Very Rare) Cocoon Band (Head, Lv71, All Jobs, DEF:65 Element: Wind-10 Slow+5%, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (39) Nosteau Herring — Gelid Aggregate (Very Common) Raptor Skin (Common) Cockatrice Skin (Uncommon) Ice Card x1~6 (Uncommon) Jusatsu x1~6 (Uncommon) Ice Arrow x3~9 (Uncommon) Beastmen\'s Seal (Uncommon) Moat Carp Creel (Rare) Ice Gauntlets (Rare) Prouesse Ring (Ring, Lv65, All Jobs, HP+10 MP+10 Increases combat skill gain rate, Rare) (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (40) Coral Butterfly — Lugworm x1~3 (Very Common) Sheep Wool (Common) Kingdom Earring (Uncommon) Republic Earring (Uncommon) Federation Earring (Uncommon) Duchy Earring (Uncommon) Selbina Earring (Uncommon) Mhaura Earring (Uncommon) Karakul Wool (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (50) Giant Donko — Mythril Ore (Very Common) G. Bird Plume (Common) Manticore Hair (Common) Moat Carp Creel (Uncommon) Beetle Shell (Uncommon) Rabao Earring (Uncommon) Spider Web (Rare) W. Spider\'s Web (Rare) Storm Zucchetto (Rare) Melaco Mittens (Hands, Lv72, WAR MNK RDM THF PLD DRK BST BRD SAM NIN DRG BLU COR DNC RUN, DEF:16 MND+3 Physical damage taken -3%, "Bird Killer"+2, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (53) Vongola Clam — Pearl (Very Common) Auric Sand (Very Common) Coral Fragment (Uncommon) Black Pearl (Uncommon) Bibiki Urchin (Uncommon) Coral Fungus (Uncommon) Vivified Coral (Rare) Storm Loop (Rare) Liminus Earring (Ear, Lv70, All Jobs, MP+10 Increases magic skill gain rate, Rare, Ex) (Very Rare) Southern Pearl (Ultra Rare)\n    ◦ Kaplumbaga (53) — Puk Egg (Very Common) Apkallu Egg (Common) (20%) Turtle Shell (Common) Date (Uncommon) Flan Meat (Uncommon) Demon Blood (Rare) Swamp Ore (Rare) Vampiric Mitts (Rare) Vampiric Boots (Rare) Pigeon\'s Blood Ruby (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (60) Elshimo Newt — Pebble (Very Common) Insect Wing x2~3 (Very Common) Crawler Egg (Uncommon) Giant Stinger (Uncommon) Moat Carp Creel (Uncommon) Kazham Pineapple (Rare) Beehive Chip (Rare) Fruit Seeds (Rare) Agaricus (Very Rare) Kazham Earring (Very Rare)\n    ◦ Kilicbaligi (61) — Silver Ore x1~3 (Very Common) Alexandrite x1~6 (Common) Gold Ore x1~2 (Common) Marid Tusk (Common) Platinum Ore (Uncommon) Luminium Ore (Rare) Gigant Squid (Rare) Imp. Slv. Piece (Rare) Immortal\'s Shotel (Rare) Numen Staff (Staff, Lv75, WAR MNK WHM BLM RDM BST BRD SMN SCH GEO, DMG:51, Delay:366, MP+25 MP recovered while healing +11, Latent effect: Adds "Refresh" effect, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (69) Crescent Fish — T. Whiteshell (Very Common) Beehive Chip (Uncommon) Kaolin (Uncommon) Doll Shard (Uncommon) Platinum Leaf (Uncommon) Fresh Mugwort (Uncommon) W. Spider\'s Web (Uncommon) Dhalmel Hair (Rare) Wild Onion (Rare) Ataractic Solea (Rare) Grapevine Cape (Back, Lv75, WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN BLU PUP SCH GEO, DEF:7 INT+3 MND+3, Enhancing Magic Duration+3%, Rare) (Super Rare) Arachne Web (Super Rare)\n    ◦ Tavnazian Goby (75) — O. Bronzepiece (Very Common) Mythril Nugget x1~3 (Very Common) Moat Carp Creel (Common) Giant Bird Feather (Common) Black C. Feather (Common) Erik\'s Axe (Rare) Tavnazian Salad (Very Rare) Metasoma Katars (Hand-to-Hand, Lv69, WAR MNK RDM DRK PUP, DMG:+17, Delay:+84 Attack+5, Additional effect: Poison, Paralysis, or Bind, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ Silver Shark (76) — Silver Nugget x1~2 (Very Common) Any Crystal (Common) Tiger Hide (Uncommon) Moat Carp Creel x1~3 (Uncommon) Beastman Blood (Rare) Gold Nugget x1~2 (Very Rare) H-P Bayld (Super Rare) Bonze Cape (Back, Lv25, All Jobs, DEF:2 MP+3 INT+2, Increases synthesis skill gain rate (+10%), Rare, Ex) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (80) Jungle Catfish — Moat Carp Creel x2~4 (Very Common) Lacquer Tree Log (Common) Wild Pineapple (Common) Malboro Vine (Common) Crawler Egg (Uncommon) Pamamas (Uncommon) Elshimo Frog (Rare) Thundermelon (Rare) Kitron x2~3 (Very Rare)\n    ◦ Gavial Fish (81) — 1 Byne Bill (Very Common) Ram Horn (Common) Chicken Bone (Common) Moat Carp Creel (Uncommon) Antlion Jaw (Uncommon) Gargouille Horn (Uncommon) Wyvern Scales (Uncommon) Sniper\'s Collar (Rare) Silver Moogle Belt (Very Rare)\n    ◦ (88) Black Ghost — Alexandrite x6~18 (Very Common) Karakul Skin (Common) Platinum Ore (Common) Petrified Log (Common) Moat Carp Creel (Common) Imperial Tea Leaves (Rare) Luminium Ore x1~2 (Rare) Kocco\'s Earring (Rare) Bond Cape (Back, Lv75, WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN BLU PUP SCH GEO, DEF:7 MP+15 MND+3, Latent effect: Bonus to Magic Accuracy, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (91) Morinabaligi — Marid Tusk (Very Common) Date (Common) Moat Carp Creel x2~3 (Common) Lacquer Tree Log (Common) Flan Meat (Uncommon) Imperial Tea Leaves (Rare) Spider Web x1~3 (Rare) Imp. Slv. Piece (Rare) Mana Ampulla (Ammo, Lv70, WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN SCH GEO, MP+15 MND+1 MP recovered while healing +1, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (93) Megalodon — Iron Ore x1~3 (Common) Black Chocobo Feather x1~2 (Common) Black Tiger Fang x1~3 (Uncommon) Smilodon Hide x1~3 (Uncommon) Kopparnickel Ore x1~2 (Uncommon) One Byne Bill (Rare) Tukuku whiteshell (Rare) Ordelle Bronzepiece (Rare) Lycopodium Flower (Rare)\n    ◦ (99) Tiger Shark — Rabbit Hide (Very Common) Fire Crystal (Uncommon) Ice Crystal (Uncommon) Wind Crystal (Uncommon) Earth Crystal (Uncommon) Lightning Crystal (Uncommon) Water Crystal (Uncommon) Light Crystal (Rare) Dark Crystal (Rare) Gold Ore (Rare) Potestas Bomblet (Ammo, Lv72, MNK THF SAM DRG PUP DNC RUN, Fire+10 Attack+5, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (100) Sea Zombie — Drill Calamary (Very Common) Any Cluster x2~4 (Uncommon) Orichalcum Ore (Rare) Rancorous Mantle (Back, Lv72, All Jobs, DEF:7 Attack+8 Critical hit rate+2%, Damage Taken+10%, Rare) (Super Rare)*\n    ◦ (104+) Titanictus — Any Cluster x2~4 (Very Common) Fish Bones (Common) Petrified Log (Common) Phoenix Feather (Rare) Pebble (Rare) 2850 Gil (Rare) Giant Bird Plume (Very Rare) Ancient Sword ??\n    ◦ (108) Armored Pisces — Mythril Ore (Very Common) Moat Carp Creel (Common) Iron Ore x1~2 (Uncommon) Silver Ore (Uncommon) Platinum Ore (Uncommon) Darksteel Ore (Uncommon) Iron Sand (Uncommon) Adaman Ore (Rare) Wizzan Grip (Sub, Lv70, All Jobs, INT+2 Conserve MP+1, Rare) (Super Rare)\n    ◦ (130) Cave Cherax — Dwarf Pugil (Very Common) Any Cluster x1~3 (Uncommon) Luminium Ore (Rare) Dragonkin Earring (Ear, Lv72, WAR PLD DRK BST DRG, Attack+5, Wyvern: Physical damage taken -2%, Rare) (Super Rare)*\n    ◦ (110+) Abaia — Acorn (Very Common) Any Cluster x1~4 (Uncommon) Gnole Claw (Rare) Plumb Boots Aurora Bass\n    ◦ (110+) Mola Mola — Mercurial Spear (Very Rare) ??? Gil\n    ◦ (110+) Gerrothorax — Risky Patch (Very Rare) ??? Gil\n    ◦ (130) Quicksilver Blade — Karakul Meat (Very Common) Any Cluster x1~3 (Uncommon) Imperial Tea Leaves (Rare) Ossa Grip (Sub, Lv72, All Jobs, Latent effect: Enhancing magic duration+5%, (Latent activates while Ice Spikes is active), Rare) (Super Rare)*\n    ◦ (150) Matsya — H-P Bayld (Very Common) Coral Fragment (Uncommon) Any Cluster x2~4 (Rare) Kitron (Rare) Thokcha Ore (Rare) Palladian Brass Ore (Rare) Phrygian Ore (Rare) Shaper\'s Shawl (Rare)* (5%)\n• Players will receive a random elemental cluster (or listed item below for higher-level fish) when rolling a Rare/Ex item they already have.\n    ◦ Sea Zombie (100): Rancorous Mantle -> Blank Key\n    ◦ Cave Cherax (130): Dragonkin Earring -> Aether Key\n    ◦ Quicksilver Blade (130): Ossa Grip -> Elementium Ingot\n    ◦ Matsaya (150): Shaper\'s Shawl -> Prismatic Key' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Sahagin', note = '• Several fishing related quests are available from the friendly Sahagin at (I-10) in Sea Serpent Grotto (Behind the Gold Beastcoin door). Each Sahagin Quest has a Fishing skill requirement of 30.' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Sahagin › Crafty Collie', note = '• Crafty Collie asks for Eastern Gem x12\n• All twelve gems must be traded at once\n• Players are awarded 75-100 Sahagin Silver\n• This quest has no cooldown' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Sahagin › Hungry Horace', note = '• Hungry Horace asks for three different randomly selected large fish\n• Trade all three fish at the same for a bonus\n• Players are awarded a total of Sahagin Silver based on the table below\n• The request can be rerolled by trading Horace 50,000 gil (10,000 gil for CW)\n• This quest has no cooldown\n• Fish: Abaia; Silver: 100\n• Fish: Ahtapot; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Armored Pisces; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Bhefhel Marlin; Silver: 50\n• Fish: Bladefish; Silver: 60\n• Fish: Cave Cherax; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Emperor Fish; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Gavial Fish; Silver: 60\n• Fish: Gerrothorax; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Giant Catfish; Silver: 30\n• Fish: Giant Chirai; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Giant Donko; Silver: 40\n• Fish: Gigant Octopus; Silver: 40\n• Fish: Gigant Squid; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Grimmonite; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Gugru Tuna; Silver: 50\n• Fish: Gugrusaurus; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Istavrit; Silver: 40\n• Fish: Jungle Catfish; Silver: 60\n• Fish: Kalkanbaligi; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Kilicbaligi; Silver: 50\n• Fish: Lakerda; Silver: 50\n• Fish: Lik; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Matsya; Silver: 100\n• Fish: Megalodon; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Mola Mola; Silver: 90\n• Fish: Monke-Onke; Silver: 40\n• Fish: Morinabaligi; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Pirarucu; Silver: 70\n• Fish: Pterygotus; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Rhinochimera; Silver: 60\n• Fish: Ryugu Titan; Silver: 100\n• Fish: Sea Zombie; Silver: 100\n• Fish: Takitaro; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Three-eyed Fish; Silver: 60\n• Fish: Titanictus; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Turnabaligi; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Veydal Wrasse; Silver: 50\n• Fish: Yayinbaligi; Silver: 30\n• Fish: Tiger Shark; Silver: 80\n• Fish: Quick. Blade; Silver: 90' },
            { title = 'Fishing: Sahagin › Slippery Sam', note = '• Slippery Sam allows players to spend their Sahagin Silver to spawn various NMs\n• Each NM costs 600 Sahagin Silver to spawn and drops Benthic Ore (Very Common) and Fine Fishing Line (Rare)\n• Each NM also has a chance to drop a unique rusty item (Uncommon)\n• Rusty items can be upgraded by trading the required items to Slippery Sam\n• Notorious Monster: Pelagic Crab Pelagic Seal (G-7) (Behind Silver Door); Base: Rusty Earring (Uncommon); Additional items: Merman\'s Earring Benthic Ore x25; Completed: Highwind (Ear, Lv70, DRG, Accuracy+5 "Store TP"+2, Wyvern: HP+40 "Regen"+1, Rare, Ex)\n• Notorious Monster: Pelagic Hog Pelagic Seal (D-9) (Behind Mythril Door); Base: Rusty Knife (Uncommon); Additional items: Cermet Kukri +1 Benthic Ore x25; Completed: Nightingale (Dagger, Lv70, BRD, DMG:36, Delay:200, CHR+5 Accuracy+12, Haste+1% "Iridescence", Rare, Ex)\n• Notorious Monster: Pelagic Manta Pelagic Seal (G-8) (Behind Gold Door); Base: Rusty Axe (Uncommon); Additional items: Dst. Tabar +1 Benthic Ore x25; Completed: Berserker (Axe, Lv70, WAR/BST, DMG:44, Delay:276, STR+5, Occasionally attacks twice, (Hidden effect: Piercing damage), Rare, Ex)' },
    } },
    { name = 'Gear and drops', group = 'Server', desc = 'Monster drops changed on the server, and augments. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Content/Drops, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Augments', steps = {
            { title = 'Drops: Overview', note = '• Certain foes have had their drops altered on the server.' },
            { title = 'Drops: Alexandrite', note = '• The mobs below all drop the following items:\n• Alexandrite (100%)\n• Alexandrite (50%)\n• Alexandrite (25%)\n• Ctn. Purse (Alx.) (10%)\n• Monster: Qiqirn Archaeologist Qiqirn Enterpriser Qiqirn Lieuter Qiqirn Mosstrooper; Zone: Aydeewa Subterrane\n• Monster: Lamia Bellydancer Lamia Dancer Lamia Dartist Lamia Deathdancer Lamia Fatedealer Lamia Graverobber Lamia Necromancer Lamia Toxophilite Lamie Bellydancer Lamie Deathdancer Lamie Necromancer Lamie Toxophilite Merrow Bladedancer Merrow Chantress Merrow Icedancer Merrow Kabukidancer Merrow Shadowdancer Merrow Songstress Merrow Typhoondancer Merrow Wavedancer Nix Bladedancer Nix Songstress Nix Typhoondancer Nix Wavedancer Qiqirn Trailer Qiqirn Treasure Hunter Soulflayer; Zone: Arrapago Reef\n• Monster: Mamool Ja Blusterer Mamool Ja Infiltrator Mamool Ja Lurker Mamool Ja Mimer Mamool Ja Philosopher Mamool Ja Pikeman Mamool Ja Stabler Troll Sabreur Troll Shieldbearer Troll Surveillant; Zone: Bhaflau Thickets\n• Monster: Lamia Chaukidar Lamia Fatedealer Lamia Necromancer Lamia Toxophilite Qiqirn Mireguide Qiqirn Rock Hound Soulflayer; Zone: Caedarva Mire\n• Monster: Moblin Billionaire Moblin Millionaire Qiqirn Diamantaire Qiqirn Mercenary Troll Artilleryman Troll Cameist Troll Combatant Troll Cuirasser Troll Engraver Troll Gemologist Troll Ironworker Troll Lapidarist Troll Machinist Troll Scrimer Troll Smelter Troll Stoneworker Troll Targeteer; Zone: Halvung\n• Monster: Mamool Ja Blusterer Mamool Ja Bounder Mamool Ja Diver Mamool Ja Frogman Mamool Ja Infiltrator Mamool Ja Lurker Mamool Ja Mimer Mamool Ja Mimicker Mamool Ja Philosopher Mamool Ja Pikeman Mamool Ja Savant Mamool Ja Sophist Mamool Ja Spearman Mamool Ja Stabler Mamool Ja Strapper Mamool Ja Zenist Poroggo Qiqirn Goldsmith Qiqirn Poulterer; Zone: Mamook\n• Monster: Hilltroll Dark Knight Hilltroll Monk Hilltroll Paladin Hilltroll Puppetmaster Hilltroll Ranger Hilltroll Red Mage Hilltroll Warrior; Zone: Mount Zhayolm\n• Monster: Mamool Ja Bounder Mamool Ja Mimicker Mamool Ja Savant Mamool Ja Sophist Mamool Ja Zenist Woodtroll Dark Knight Woodtroll Monk Woodtroll Ranger Woodtroll Warrior; Zone: Wajaom Woodlands' },
            { title = 'Drops: BCNMs', note = '• BCNM: Copycat; Drops: Infinity Core (100%)\n• BCNM: Early Bird Catches the Wyrm; Drops: Sweet Tea (100%) Ridill (5%)\n• BCNM: Horns of War; Drops: Defending Ring (5%) Savory Shank (100%)\n• BCNM: Operation Desert Swarm; Drops: Antares Harness (5%) Infinity Core (100%)\n• BCNM: The Hills Are Alive; Drops: Hauteclaire (5%) Red Pondweed (100%)\n• BCNM: Today\'s Horoscope; Drops: Infinity Core (100%)' },
            { title = 'Drops: Dynamis', note = '• See Dynamis 2.0 Drops.' },
            { title = 'Drops: HNMs', note = '• See HNMs Custom Drops.' },
            { title = 'Drops: Lesser NMs', note = '• Name: Ash Dragon; Drops: Dragon Staff (30%)\n• Name: Bune; Drops: Dragon Scales (25%)\n• Name: Charybdis; Drops: Angel Skin (7%)\n• Name: Guivre; Drops: Dragon Scales (25%)\n• Name: Novv the Whitehearted; Drops: Siren\'s Hair (10%)\n• Name: Ocean Sahagin; Drops: Siren\'s Hair (33%)\n• Name: Oupire; Drops: Hagun (15%)\n• Name: Roc; Drops: Shining Cloth (25%)\n• Name: Ungur; Drops: Dragon Scales (25%)\n• Name: Zuug the Shoreleaper; Drops: Siren\'s Hair (10%)' },
            { title = 'Drops: Normal Monsters', note = '• Name: Eschan Porxie (Escha - Ru\'Aun); Drops: Bead Pouch (22%) Porxie Pork (4%)\n• Name: Nostokulshedra (Escha - Ru\'Aun); Drops: Angel Skin (4%)' },
            { title = 'Drops: Treasure Caskets', note = '• The following items are scaled down rewards from Grounds of Valor caskets.\n• Item: Dagda\'s Shield [Rare] WAR PLD DRK; Level: 70; Stats: DEF:20 Enmity+2 Cure Potency+5%; Notes: Fei\'Yin\n• Item: Potestas Bomblet [Rare] MNK THF SAM DRG PUP DNC RUN; Level: 70; Stats: Fire+10 Attack+5; Notes: Upper Delkfutt\'s Tower\n• Item: Grapevine Cape [Rare] WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN BLU PUP SCH GEO; Level: 75; Stats: DEF:7 INT+3 MND+3 Enhancing Magic Duration+3%; Notes: Ranguemont Pass\n• Item: Melaco Mittens [Rare] WAR MNK RDM THF PLD DRK BST BRD SAM NIN DRG BLU COR DNC RUN; Level: 72; Stats: DEF:16 MND+3 Physical damage taken -3% "Bird Killer"+2; Notes: Bostaunieux Oubliette\n• Item: Bond Cape [Rare] WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN BLU PUP SCH GEO; Level: 75; Stats: DEF:7 MP+15 MND+3 Latent effect: Bonus to Magic Accuracy; Notes: Toraimarai Canal Latent unchanged\n• Item: Prouesse Ring [Rare] [Ex] All Jobs; Level: 65; Stats: HP+10 MP+10 Increases combat skill gain rate; Notes: Zeruhn Mines\n• Item: Numen Staff [Rare] WAR MNK WHM BLM RDM BST BRD SMN SCH GEO; Level: 75; Stats: DMG:51 Delay:366 MP+25 MP recovered while healing +11 Latent effect: Adds "Refresh" effect; Notes: Inner Horutoto Ruins Latent unchanged\n• Item: Ossa Grip [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 75; Stats: Latent effect: Enhancing magic duration+5%; Notes: The Eldieme Necropolis Latent: Ice Spikes active\n• Item: Cocoon Band [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 71; Stats: DEF:65 Wind-10 Slow+5%; Notes: Crawlers\' Nest\n• Item: Metasoma Katars [Rare] WAR MNK RDM DRK PUP; Level: 69; Stats: DMG+17 Delay+84 Attack+5 Additional effect: Poison, Paralysis, or Bind; Notes: Garlaige Citadel\n• Item: Dragonkin Earring [Rare] WAR PLD DRK BST DRG; Level: 72; Stats: Attack+5 Wyvern: Physical damage taken -2%; Notes: The Boyahda Tree\n• Item: Brachyura Earring [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 70; Stats: MP+15 Enhances effect of Protect and Shell spells cast on wearer; Notes: Korroloka Tunnel\n• Item: Wizzan Grip [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 70; Stats: INT+2 Conserve MP+1; Notes: Kuftal Tunnel\n• Item: Terminus Earring [Rare] [Ex] All Jobs; Level: 70; Stats: HP+10 Increases combat skill gain rate; Notes: The Shrine of Ru\'Avitau\n• Item: Liminus Earring [Rare] [Ex] All Jobs; Level: 70; Stats: MP+10 Increases magic skill gain rate; Notes: Gustav Tunnel\n• Item: Furtive Grip [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 75; Stats: Subtle Blow+5; Notes: Labyrinth of Onzozo\n• Item: Rancorous Mantle [Rare] All Jobs; Level: 72; Stats: DEF:7 Attack+8 Critical hit rate+2%, Damage Taken+10%; Notes: Den of Rancor\n• Item: Mana Ampulla [Rare] WHM BLM RDM BRD SMN SCH GEO; Level: 70; Stats: MP+15 MND+1 MP recovered while healing +1; Notes: Sea Serpent Grotto Ammo' },
            { title = 'Augments: Overview', note = '• CatsEye is home to various custom augment systems.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Adept Reforging', note = '• Adept Reforging is a system of trials to upgrade certain ENM material crafted armor sets.\n• See: the Adept Reforging page.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Artifact +1', note = '• See the dedicated CatsEyeXI Systems/Artifact %2B1 Augments page.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Synergy Augments', note = '• See CatsEyeXI Systems/Synergy § Weapons.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Abjuration Augments', note = '• See CatsEyeXI Systems/Synergy § Abjurations.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Novice Trials', note = '• Novice Trials are an augment system which allows players to enhance various pieces of equipment up to around level 50. There are all sorts of trials of varying difficulty for players to improve existing or old equipment and make it shine.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Grand Trials', note = '• Grand Trials is a continuation of the Novice Trials system encompassing high-end gear intended for level 50+. These trials are more intense and require a lot more dedication!' },
            { title = 'Augments: Relic +1', note = '• See the CatsEyeXI Content/Dynamis Augments page.' },
            { title = 'Augments: Salvage Augments', note = '• See dedicated CatsEyeXI Systems/Salvage Augments page.' },
    } },
    { name = 'Quests and missions', group = 'Server', desc = 'Mission availability, quest notes, the custom quest system and the Novice Trials. Individual custom quests are in quest_guides.lua. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Content/Missions, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Quests, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Loxley_Quest_System_(LQS), https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Novice_Trials', steps = {
            { title = 'Missions: City Missions › Bastok', note = '• Retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s Bastok Missions walkthrough.' },
            { title = 'Missions: City Missions › San d\'Oria', note = '• Retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s San d\'Oria Missions walkthrough, with the exception of Mission 9-2,\n• the fight can be skipped by talking to Nantoto in Lower Jeuno H-8 (Trion is too squishy and it\'s almost impossible to win).' },
            { title = 'Missions: City Missions › Windurst', note = '• Retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s Windurst Missions walkthrough.\n• Players do not need to possess the Key item Portal charm to open the 3-mage gate on CEXI.' },
            { title = 'Missions: Rise of the Zilart', note = '• Retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s Zilart Missions walkthrough.\n• If you accidentally warped out of the device chamber after Zilart Mission 6 but before completing ZM7, you can now click a sparkle next to the battlefield entrance in the Chamber of Oracles to be transported back to that room.' },
            { title = 'Missions: Chains of Promathia', note = '• Retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s Promathia Missions walkthrough.\n• [CW] Crystal Warriors are under level caps for all BCNM, Promyvions, Phominua, Riverne, Sacrarium.' },
            { title = 'Missions: Treasures of Aht Urhgan', note = '• Missions are retail accurate, and follow the wiki\'s Aht Urhgan Missions walkthrough.\n• However, since assaults are not fully implemented, your Assault rank on CatsEyeXI will be directly connected to your Aht Urhgan Missions progress.\n• Mission: 3; Name: President Salaheem; Rank Reward: Private Second Class; Currency Required: N/A\n• Mission: 10; Name: Astral Waves; Rank Reward: Private First Class; Currency Required: Imp. Brz. Piece x10\n• Mission: 15; Name: The Black Coffin; Rank Reward: Superior Private; Currency Required: Imp. Brz. Piece x20\n• Mission: 20; Name: Teahouse Tumult; Rank Reward: Lance Corporal; Currency Required: Imp. Brz. Piece x30\n• Mission: 24; Name: Foiled Ambition; Rank Reward: Corporal; Currency Required: Imp. Slv. Piece x10\n• Mission: 28; Name: Bastion of Knowledge; Rank Reward: Sergeant; Currency Required: Imp. Slv. Piece x20\n• Mission: 32; Name: In the Blood; Rank Reward: Sergeant Major; Currency Required: Imp. Slv. Piece x30\n• Mission: 36; Name: Gaze of the Saboteur; Rank Reward: Chief Sergeant; Currency Required: Imp. Mtl. Piece x10\n• Mission: 40; Name: Unraveling Reason; Rank Reward: Second Lieutenant; Currency Required: Imp. Mtl. Piece x20\n• Mission: 44; Name: Nashmeira\'s Plea; Rank Reward: First Lieutenant; Currency Required: Imp. Mtl. Piece x30\n• Mission: 48; Name: Eternal Mercenary; Rank Reward: Captain; Currency Required: Imp. Gold Piece x30\n• Players must speak to the Wildcat Captain at the Commissions Agency (K-10) in Aht Urhgan Whitegate. After completing the required missions and being offered a promotion, players can trade the requested currency to receive their new rank and accompanying Key Item.\n• You will not be rewarded the currencies from the rank update, despite the logs saying so.\n• Note: Rank promotions also makes purchasing items from the guards in Whitegate for Imperial Standing possible.' },
            { title = 'Missions: Wings of the Goddess', note = '• Players can advance in Wings of the Goddess Missions up until In the Name of the Father. At that point, the different nation questlines send players to WotG instanced zones (Ghoyu\'s Reverie or Ruhotz Silvermines) which are not available yet on CatsEyeXI, and so we cannot advance past that point yet.' },
            { title = 'Missions: Seekers of Adoulin', note = '• Not implemented' },
            { title = 'Missions: A Crystalline Prophecy', note = '• Not implemented' },
            { title = 'Missions: A Moogle Kupo d\'Etat', note = '• Not implemented' },
            { title = 'Missions: A Shantotto Ascension', note = '• Not implemented' },
            { title = 'Missions: Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel', note = '• Rhapsodies has been partially implemented in order to grant ACE accounts Trusts without needing a custom system. As the two corresponding key items (White/Crimson) are tied to them. Thus, certain rewards (mostly key items) have been removed and others added.\n• Trust ciphers, and Rhapsodies KIs are only received by ACE/CW accounts while the other rewards are received by all account types.\n• In order to progress through the Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel without interruption, your character must have progressed to the following missions below in other expansions:\n• Obtain Rank 6 in your home nation by completing Rank Mission 5-2.\n• Progress in Rise of the Zilart until your current mission is Headstone Pilgrimage.\n• Progress in Chains of Promathia until your current mission is The Road Forks.\n    ◦ Note: Once you are on The Warrior\'s Path, you will be required to complete all remaining missions through Dawn, the final cutscenes in Lufaise Meadows, and Apocalypse Nigh for Tenzen to be available.\n• Progress in Treasures of Aht Urhgan until your current mission is Royal Puppeteer.\n• Progress in Wings of the Goddess until your current mission is In the Name of the Father.\n• If you get stuck, compare your mission to the relevant character in the story at the moment to the official list of when the NPC is unavailable.\n• Creation and Rebirth:\n• Chapter 1:\n• 1-1 — Rhapsodies of Vanadiel — Cutscene\n• 1-2 — Resonance — Cutscene\n• 1-3 — Emissary from the Seas — Cutscene\n• 1-4 — Set Free — Quest — Anniversary Ring\n• 1-5 — The Beginning — Cutscene — Key item Reisenjima Sanctorium orb\n• 1-6 — Flames of Prayer — Cutscene — Key item "Rhapsody in White"[ACE]\n• ▼ Obtain Rank 3 in your home nation by completing Journey Abroad The Emissary The Three Kingdoms ▼\n• 1-7 — The Path Untraveled — Cutscene — Unlocks access to Cipher Of Semih\'s Alter Ego [ACE] [CW] and Cipher Of Halver\'s Alter Ego[ACE]\n• 1-8 — At the Heavens\' Door — Cutscene\n• 1-9 — The Lion\'s Roar — Fight - Popped NM — Super Reraiser Tank\n• Note: Level 50 cap, encounter status applied and is removed upon zoning. CFH, and trusts are not allowed and despawn upon clicking the vortex. The NM can take no more than 50 damage at a time, but is extra susceptible to damage-over-time such as Dia and Poison.\n• 1-10 — Eddies of Despair — Cutscene — Access to Escha - Zi\'Tah 1,000 Silt(Currency of Escha, allows warping from teleports in the zone)\n• 1-11 — A Land After Time — Cutscene — Cipher of Lion\'s alter ego II[ACE] [CW]\n• ▼ Obtain Rank 6 in your home nation by completing The Shadow Lord Xarcabard, Land of Truths The Shadow Awaits ▼\n• 1-12 — Fate\'s Call — Cutscene — Miratete\'s Memoirs\n• 1-13 — What Lies Beyond — Cutscene\n• 1-14 — The Ties That Bind — Cutscene\n• 1-15 — Impurity — Cutscene\n• 1-16 — The Lost Avatar — Fight - Popped NM — Beastmen\'s Seal x30\n• Uncapped, no encounter status applied, trusts allowed. LV75 recommended. Beware of charm.\n• 1-17 — Volto Oscuro — Cutscene — Cipher of Zeid\'s Alter Ego II[ACE] [CW]\n• 1-18 — Ring My Bell — Cutscene\n• ▼ Progress in Chains of Promathia until your current mission is The Last Verse if you are past 7-5 The Warrior\'s Path ▼\n• Revitalization:\n• Chapter 2:\n• 2-1 — Spirits Awoken — Cutscene\n• ▼ Progress in Chains of Promathia until your current mission is The Road Forks ▼\n• 2-2 — Crashing Waves — Cutscene — Cipher Of Tenzen\'s Alter Ego II[ACE] [CW] Kindred\'s Seal x30\n• 2-3 — Call to Serve — Cutscene — Cipher Of Prishe\'s Alter Ego II[ACE] [CW]\n• 2-4 — Numbering Days — Cutscene\n• 2-5 — Inescapable Binds — Cutscene\n• 2-6 — Desert Winds — Quest\n• ▼ Progress in Treasures of Aht Urhgan until your current mission is Royal Puppeteer ▼\n• 2-7 — Ever Forward — Cutscene\n• 2-8 — The Endless Sky — Quest\n• 2-9 — Aphmau\'s Light — Quest — Cipher Of Nashmeira\'s Alter Ego II[ACE] [CW]\n• 2-10 — Reunited — Cutscene\n• 2-11 — Take Wing — Cutscene\n• 2-12 — Prime Number — Cutscene — Rebirth Feather\n• 2-13 — From the Ruins — Cutscene — Key item "Rhapsody in Crimson"[ACE] Far East Hearth\n• ▼ Progress in Wings of the Goddess until your current mission is In the Name of the Father ▼\n• 2-14 — Cauterize — Cutscene\n• 2-15 — Uncertain Destinations — Cutscene\n• 2-16 — Ganged Up On — Cutscene — Cipher Of Lilisette\'s Alter Ego II [ACE] [CW]\n• 2-17 — Sacrifice — Cutscene\n• 2-18 — Somber Dreams — Fight - Popped NM\n• Note: Uncapped, difficult fight. Alliance recommended. Uses many AoE moves so keeping some distance is recommended, or good "magic damage taken -%" and magic defense gear. Uses a conal death move at low health, but will not use any conal moves if tanking to the side. Will rage after 1hr, gaining an evasion boost and damage reduction.\n• 2-19 — Of Light and Darkness — Cutscene\n• 2-20 — Temporary Farewells — Cutscene\n• 2-21 — Brushing Up — Cutscene\n• 2-22 — Keep On Giving — Quest\n• Note: It is highly recommended that [CW] Crystal Warriors pick the 2nd option - "Style" - as it has the easiest crafting requirement (Spicy Cracker - Cooking 59).\n• 2-23 — Past Imperfect — Cutscene\n• ▼ Progress in Rise of the Zilart until your current mission is Headstone Pilgrimage ▼\n• 2-24 — The Cursed Temple — Cutscene\n• 2-25 — Wisdom of Our Forefathers — Cutscene\n• 2-26 — Where Divinities Collide — Cutscene\n• 2-27 — Visions of Dread — Cutscene\n• 2-28 — To the Skies — Cutscene\n• 2-29 — Escha - Ru\'Aun — Cutscene — Access to Escha - Ru\'Aun (if not already unlocked by defeating Dynamis Lord)\n• 2-30 — The Decisive Heroine — Cutscene — Summoned Trusts: gain a bonus to attack, defense, and magic accuracy (level * 2/3), and receive Refresh+1 Campaign Battles: Promotion credit gain +20%, rank-up cooldown reduced to 24 hours\n• Progress in Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Missions is not available beyond this point on CatsEyeXI.\n• Cutscene: A mission that is entirely or almost entirely cutscenes.\n• Quest: A mission that involves a lot of running around and cutscenes.\n• Dungeon: A mission that takes place mostly in a dungeon, such as Promyvion or Sacrarium.\n• Fight: A mission that mostly involves one or many NM fights.\n• BCNM: A mision that is either solely a BCNM, or culminates in a BCNM fight. Usually referenced along with Dungeon-type missions.' },
            { title = 'Quests: Overview', note = '• CatsEyeXI is home to various custom quests. This began in earnest with the creation of the Crystal Warrior mode. To find quests available to your game mode, search with your browser for the following terms: ACE, CW, WEW\n• As a note and warning to all players, make sure when accepting any quest, you make sure to talk to the NPC multiple times to exhaust all dialogue, the following command !quest can also be used to check Custom Quests!' },
            { title = 'Quests: Limit Breaks', note = '• The ???s for the Level 50 (In Defiant Challenge) and 55 (Atop the Highest Mountains) limit breaks are functional.\n• All Limit Breaks related to Maat work as expected, and are three tries per testimony. Keep in mind that because Rhapsody in Umber is not available on CEXI, you will not be able to summon trusts for the Maat fight.\n    ◦ Custom quests and fights were created for the limit breaks for BLU, PUP, COR, DNC, SCH.\n    ◦ Since players need to reach level 75 for GEO and RUN, they do not have a limit break.' },
            { title = 'Loxley Quest System (LQS): Overview', note = '• Catseye provides custom content for its players using Loxley\'s Quest System (https://github.com/LoxleyXI/LQS).\n• The Quest System includes:\n• Custom quests\n• Novice/grand/adept trials\n• Goblin brew\n• Dragonslaying\n• Allied incursion\n• Allied skirmish\n• Crystal Warrior Battle Content, including: Yagudo arena, Goblin\'s gambit, Tonberry trouble, Moblin mayhem\n• The quest system uses an alternative method for loot drops, which is unaffected by Treasure Hunter.' },
            { title = 'Novice Trials: Novice Trials', note = '• Novice Trials to upgrade your existing equipment can be undertaken from the following NPCs:\n    ◦ Mellie (H-7) in Selbina\n    ◦ Huebald (H-7) Port San d\'Oria\n    ◦ Bobortimer (H-6) Port Bastok\n    ◦ Sadoc (L-6) Port Windurst\n• This quest is available for all character types and there is no cooldown.\n• Players are assigned a list of enemies to defeat and messages track their objectives.\n• Some new encounters will require items to spawn and may be level capped.\n    ◦ All party members who have flagged the trial will receive completion when the Notorious Monster is defeated, requiring only one player to obtain the pop items.\n• HQ versions of crafted items can be traded to any of the Novice Trial NPCs as listed above alongside an augmented normal quality version, transferring these augments to the HQ version.\n    ◦ (The current trial must first be completed)\n    ◦ The NQ version will be consumed.\n• Unlike Adept Reforging, players may complete Novice Trials on any job.\n• Augmented items can be stored at the Squire Guard in Ru\'Lude Gardens (I-10).\n• Item: Beestinger; Level: 7; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Critical hit rate+1%; Requirements: Maneating Hornet x15 (North Gustaberg) Maneating Hornet x15 (South Gustaberg)\n• Item: Rabbit Charm; Level: 7; [Augmented] Augments: DEX+1 AGI+1 Evasion+1; Requirements: Forest Hare x15 (West Ronfaure) Steppe Hare x10 (La Theine Plateau)\n• Item: Pelte; Level: 8; [Augmented] Augments: INT+1 MND+1 MP recovered while healing+2; Requirements: River Crab x15 (East Sarutabaruta) River Crab x15 (West Sarutabaruta)\n• Item: Mist Silk Cape; Level: 8; [Augmented] Augments: Cure spellcasting time -1% Cure Potency+1%; Requirements: Crawler x15 (West Sarutabaruta) Canyon Crawler x15 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Clipeus; Level: 9; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 Shield Skill+3; Requirements: Scarab Beetle x15 (East Ronfaure) Copper Beetle x10 (Palborough Mines)\n• Item: Armiger\'s Lace; Level: 9; [Augmented] Augments: HP+2 Accuracy+1; Requirements: Vulture x10 (South Gustaberg) Vulture x10 (North Gustaberg)\n• Item: Pilgrim\'s Wand; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: MP+5 Conserve MP+2 MP Recovered while healing +1; Requirements: Carrion Crow x 15 (West Sarutabaruta) Akbaba x 10 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Tropical Punches; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Counter+2; Requirements: Mandragora x15 (East Sarutabaruta) Pygmaioi x10 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Katayama; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Zanshin+2; Requirements: Ornery Sheep x15 (North Gustaberg) Mad Sheep x10 (Konschtat Highlands)\n• Item: Optical Earring; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: HP+2 DEX+1; Requirements: Strolling Sapling x15 (Konschtat Highlands) Wandering Sapling x15 (Jugner Forest)\n• Item: Scale Mail; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 HP+10; Requirements: Goblin Armorer (Konschtat Highlands) (Level Sync 15) Trade: Bronze Ingot x3 to Lost Tongs (G-7)\n• Item: Scale Cuisses; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 HP+8; Requirements: Goblin Armorer (Konschtat Highlands) (Level Sync 15) Trade: Bronze Ingot x3 to Lost Tongs (G-7)\n• Item: Gelong Staff; Level: 10; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 Regen+1; Requirements: Pugil x15 (East Ronfaure (S)) Beach Pugil x15 (Valkurm Dunes)\n• Item: Light Axe; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 CHR+2; Requirements: Forest Hare x15 (East Ronfaure) Forest Hare x15 (West Ronfaure)\n• Item: Entrancing Ribbon; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: Fast Cast+1% Pet: Accuracy+2 Ranged Accuracy+2; Requirements: Steppe Hare x15 (La Theine Plateau) Canyon Rarab x15 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Doublet; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 HP+10; Requirements: Goblin Burglar (La Theine Plateau) (Level Sync 15) Trade: Sheep Leather x3 to Lost Lockpick (C-5)\n• Item: Brais; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: Evasion+2 Accuracy+1; Requirements: Goblin Burglar (La Theine Plateau) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Sheep Leather x3 to Lost Lockpick (C-5)\n• Item: Pike; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Pet: Breath+2; Requirements: Digger Wasp x15 (Giddeus) Killer Bee x10 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Wild Cudgel; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+7 HP+5 Counter+2; Requirements: Orcish Stonechucker x10 (Fort Ghelsba) Orcish Neckchopper x10 (Fort Ghelsba) Orcish Grunt x10 (Fort Ghelsba) Sentry Lizard x10 (Fort Ghelsba)\n• Item: Bee Spatha; Level: 11; [Augmented] Augments: MP+15 DEF+4; Requirements: Huge Wasp x15 (Konschtat Highlands) Huge Wasp x15 (La Theine Plateau)\n• Item: Linen Robe; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 MP+10; Requirements: Goblin Tailor (Tahrongi Canyon) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Cotton Thread x3 to Lost Needle (G-9)\n• Item: Linen Slops; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: MP+5 Magic Accuracy+1; Requirements: Goblin Tailor (Tahrongi Canyon) (Level Sync 15, no trusts) Trade: Cotton Thread x3 to Lost Needle (G-9)\n• Item: Brass Hammer; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 MND+2; Requirements: Skeleton Warrior x7 (Konschtat Highlands) Skeleton Warrior x7 (La Theine Plateau) Skeleton Warrior x7 (Tahrongi Canyon)\n• Item: Great Axe; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 DEF+5; Requirements: Young Quadav x15 (North Gustaberg) Young Quadav x15 (South Gustaberg)\n• Item: Serpette; Level: 12; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 STR+1 INT+1; Requirements: Rambling Ram (East Ronfaure) (Level Sync 15) Trade: Baked Apple x3 to Large Hoofprint (I-9)\n• Item: Felling Axe; Level: 13; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 STR+1 Pet: STR/DEX/VIT+1; Requirements: Grave Bat x25 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb) Tomb Bat x10 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb)\n• Item: Guerilla Gloves; Level: 13; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 MP+4 Attack+2 Pet: STR+1; Requirements: Greater Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines) Veteran Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines) Onyx Quadav x15 (Palborough Mines)\n• Item: Battle Gloves; Level: 14; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 HP+3 MP+3 Store TP+1 Potency of Cure received+1%; Requirements: Rock Eater x15 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb) Plague Bats x10 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb) Nachzehrer x5 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb) Spook x1 (King Ranperre\'s Tomb)\n• Item: Fungus Hat; Level: 14; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 INT+1 MND+1 CHR+1 Haste+1%; Requirements: Marsh Funguar x15 (Carpenters\' Landing) Marsh Funguar x15 (Pashhow Marshlands)\n• Item: Gassan; Level: 15; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Enmity+2; Requirements: Thread Leech x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Forest Leech x15 (Jugner Forest)\n• Item: Rogetsurin; Level: 15; [Augmented] Augments: HP+3 MP+3 VIT+1 Throwing Skill+3; Requirements: Skeleton Warrior x20 (Gusgen Mines) Sand Hare x15 (Valkurm Dunes) Sand Bats x5 (Valkurm Dunes) Poltergeist x5 (Konschtat Highlands)\n• Item: Mettle Leggings Note: Also equipable as PUP; Level: 17; [Augmented] Augments: HP+4 DEX+1 Pet:Attack+2 Ranged Attack+2; Requirements: Wild Sheep x25 (East Ronfaure (S)) Brutal Sheep x20 (Jugner Forest)\n• Item: Decurion\'s Hammer; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Enhancing Magic Skill+2 Healing Magic Skill+2; Requirements: Wolf Zombie x20 (Konschtat Highlands) Ghost x5 (Konschtat Highlands) Skeleton Warrior x10 (Gusgen Mines)\n• Item: Ryl.Spr. Spear; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Conserve TP+1 Resist Blind+3; Requirements: Orcish Wallbreacher x1 (Ghelsba Outpost) Orcish Barricader x1 (Ghelsba Outpost) Orcish Flamethrower x5 (Fort Ghelsba)\n• Item: Mercenary\'s Pole; Level: 18; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 Magic Defense Bonus+2; Requirements: Four of Batons x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Coins x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Cups x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins) Four of Swords x10 (Outer Horutoto Ruins)\n• Item: Decurion\'s Dagger; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+2 Accuracy+2 Resist Silence+3; Requirements: Greater Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Veteran Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Onyx Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands)\n• Item: Decurion\'s Shield; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 AGI+1 Magic Defense Bonus+2; Requirements: Greater Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Veteran Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands) Onyx Quadav x15 (Pashhow Marshlands)\n• Item: Ryl.Spr. Horn; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: Song Recast Delay-1 Attack+2; Requirements: Orcish Grunt x15 (Jugner Forest) Orcish Neckchopper x15 (Jugner Forest) Orcish Stonechucker x15 (Jugner Forest)\n• Item: Mercenary\'s Knife; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Ranged Accuracy+2; Requirements: Yagudo Mendicant x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Persecutor x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Piper x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Item: Mrc. Greatsword; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 MP+5 Resist Sleep+3; Requirements: Yagudo Mendicant x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Persecutor x15 (Meriphataud Mountains) Yagudo Piper x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Item: Carbuncle Mitts; Level: 20; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 MP+5 Enmity-1 Pet: DEF+10; Requirements: Air Elemental x3 (Tahrongi Canyon) Water Elemental x3 (La Theine Plateau) Thunder Elemental x3 (Konschtat Highlands)\n• Item: Beetle Mask; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: AGI+2; Requirements: Copper Beetle x15 (Palborough Mines) Beady Beetle x15 (Carpenters\' Landing)\n• Item: Beetle Harness; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+4 AGI+2; Requirements: Giant Beetle (Sauromugue Champaign) (Level Sync 20) Trade: Beetle Shell x12 to Disturbed Mound (G-5)\n• Item: Beetle Mittens; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: Attack+2; Requirements: Stag Beetle x15 (Jugner Forest) Stag Beetle x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Item: Beetle Subligar; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: Attack+2; Requirements: Stag Beetle x15 (Jugner Forest) Stag Beetle x15 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Item: Beetle Leggings; Level: 21; [Augmented] Augments: AGI+2; Requirements: Copper Beetle x15 (Palborough Mines) Beady Beetle x15 (Carpenters\' Landing)\n• Item: Cotton Doublet; Level: 23; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 HP+7 MP+7 Attack+1; Requirements: Cottontail (Batallia Downs) (Level Sync 25) Trade: Cotton Cloth x12 to Bunny Trail (H-5)\n• Item: Winged Boots; Level: 24; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 Evasion+2 Haste+1%; Requirements: Rock Lizard x35 (North Gustaberg (S)) Hill Lizard x25 (Sauromugue Champaign) Ivory Lizard x15 (Yuhtunga Jungle)\n• Item: Nomad\'s Mantle; Level: 24; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 Dual Wield+1; Requirements: Seeker Bats x35 (Korroloka Tunnel) Bogy x25 (Gusgen Mines)\n• Item: Barbarian\'s Sword; Level: 24; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+6 VIT+2 Parrying rate+2%; Requirements: Yagudo Votary x20 (Castle Oztroja) Yagudo Priest x10 (Castle Oztroja) Yagudo Theologist x10 (Castle Oztroja) Boggart x20 (Meriphataud Mountains)\n• Item: Ranging Knife; Level: 24; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 DEX+1 Ranged Attack+2; Requirements: Clipper x25 (Rolanberry Fields) Clipper x 35 (Korroloka Tunnel)\n• Item: Nadrs; Level: 24; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 Double Attack+1% Critical hit rate+1%; Requirements: Clipper x25 (Batallia Downs) Clipper x35 (Qufim Island)\n• Item: Anthos Xiphos; Level: 25; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 DEX+1 Attack+3; Requirements: Soniashnyk (West Sarutabaruta (S)) (Level Sync 25) Trade: Lycopodium Flower x36 to Black Soil (E-6)\n• Item: Herder\'s Subligar; Level: 25; [Augmented] Augments: HP+10 DEX+3 Pet: Attack+3 Rng.Atk.+3; Requirements: Sauromugue Skink x15 (Sauromugue Champaign) Champaign Coeurl x15 (Sauromugue Champaign) Sabertooth Tiger x10 (Sauromugue Champaign)\n• Item: Parrying Knife; Level: 25; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 STR+1 CHR+1 Enmity+2 Parrying Rate+1; Requirements: Malboro x10 (Pashhow Marshlands) Ornery Sheep x30 (North Gustaberg (S)) Ge\'Dha Evileye x1 (Beadeaux)\n• Item: Astaroth Cane; Level: 27; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 MP+9 INT+1 Accuracy+5; Requirements: Bandersnatch x20 (Gusgen Mines) Ghoul x20 (Gusgen Mines) Ore Eater x15 (Gusgen Mines)\n• Item: Steam Scale Mail; Level: 27; [Augmented] Augments: HP+10 MP+10 STR+1 VIT+1 Parrying Skill+3; Requirements: Steam Lizard x25 (Dangruf Wadi) Hill Lizard x15 (Sauromugue Champaign)\n• Item: Faerie Tunic; Level: 27; [Augmented] Augments: MP+15 STR+2 AGI+2 Magic Defense Bonus+2 Cure Potency+2%; Requirements: Schildkrote (Pashhow Marshlands) (Level Sync 30) Trade: Holy Phial x2 to Seltsam Loch (L-6)\n• Item: Eremite\'s Wand; Level: 28; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+5 MP+10 INT+3 MND+3 Magic burst dmg.+2%; Requirements: Orcish Cursemaker x20 (Davoi) Orcish Fighter x20 (Davoi) Orcish Cursemaker x5 (Batallia Downs) Orcish Fighter x5 (Batallia Downs)\n• Item: Griot Belt; Level: 28; [Augmented] Augments: HP+5 MP+5 Haste+2%; Requirements: Copper Quadav x20 (Beadeaux) Brass Quadav x20 (Beadeaux) Old Quadav x20 (Beadeaux) Copper Quadav x5 (Rolanberry Fields) Brass Quadav x5 (Rolanberry Fields) Old Quadav x5 (Rolanberry Fields)\n• Item: Brass Grip; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: Staff Skill+2 Parry Skill+2 Divine Magic Skill+2; Requirements: Boggart x35 (Inner Horutoto Ruins) x35\n• Item: Circe\'s Hat; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: MP+9 MND+1 Healing magic skill+3; Requirements: Goblin Leecher x15 (Buburimu Peninsula) Goblin Leecher x15 (Valkurm Dunes)\n• Item: Fidelity Mantle; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+3 HP+6 MP+6 Attack+3; Requirements: Bulwark Bat x10 (Castle Oztroja) Bastion Bats x15 (Castle Oztroja) Stirge x15 (Oldton Movalpolos) Dark Bats x10 (Oldton Movalpolos) Goblin\'s Bat x10 (Oldton Movalpolos)\n• Item: Fleuret; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 HP+7 MP+7 Accuracy+3 INT+2 MND+2; Requirements: Dancing Weapon x20 (Qufim Island) Lycopodium x20 (Sauromugue Champaign (S)) Chaos Idol x15 (Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower)\n• Item: Steel Kilij; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 STR+1 INT+1 Accuracy+3 Attack+3 Fast Cast+1%; Requirements: Hollohaza Liba (Bhaflau Thickets) (Level Sync 30) Trade: Karakul Leather x4 Colored Egg x12 to Clay Cast Nest (F-9)\n• Item: Hawker\'s Knife; Level: 30; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+3 Store TP+1 Recycle+5; Requirements: Orcish Nightraider x30 (Davoi) Orcish Nightraider x5 (Batallia Downs) Orcish Nightraider x5 (Lufaise Meadows) (Orcish Serjeant) x5 (Carpenters\' Landing)\n• Item: Aega\'s Doublet; Level: 32; [Augmented] Augments: HP+15 Evasion+3 Pet: Attack +3; Requirements: Yuhtunga Mandragora x30 (Yuhtunga Jungle) Yhoator Mandragora x30 (Yhoator Jungle)\n• Item: Pigeon Earring; Level: 33; [Augmented] Augments: MP+15 STR+1 Attack+2; Requirements: Thread Leech x30 (Korroloka Tunnel) Acrophies x30 (Qufim Island) Acrophies x15 (Lufaise Meadows)\n• Item: Jaeger Ring; Level: 35; [Augmented] Augments: AGI+3 Store TP+1; Requirements: Sadfly x30 (Gusgen Mines) Gallinipper x40 (Attohwa Chasm) Elusive Edwin x1 (The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah)\n• Item: Jujitsu Sitabaki; Level: 37; [Augmented] Augments: HP+10 STR+2 DEX+2 Store TP+1; Requirements: Orcish Brawler x20 (Batallia Downs) Orcish Brawler x20 (Lufaise Meadows)\n• Item: Cvl. Mantle; Level: 37; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+2 Enmity+2 Counter+2; Requirements: Orcish Impaler x20 (Davoi) Orcish Beastrider x20 (Davoi) Orcish Impaler x10 (Lufaise Meadows) Orcish Beastrider x10 (Lufaise Meadows)\n• Item: Passaddhi Staff; Level: 39; [Augmented] Augments: DMG+5 MP+15 MND+2 Conserve MP+4; Requirements: Ooze x15 (Sea Serpent Grotto) Spring Sahagin x15 (Sea Serpent Grotto) Lake Sahagin x15 (Sea Serpent Grotto) Pond Sahagin x15 (Sea Serpent Grotto)\n• Item: Dobson Bandana; Level: 39; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+15 Enmity+2 Magic Evasion+1; Requirements: Prince Ogrefly (Attohwa Chasm) Trade: Attohwa Ginseng x1 to Ogrefly Nest (G-8)\n• Item: Jujitsu Gi; Level: 40; [Augmented] Augments: HP+15 STR+2 AGI+2 Store TP+1; Requirements: Orcish Brawler x20 (Batallia Downs) Orcish Brawler x20 (Lufaise Meadows)\n• Item: Salutary Robe; Level: 40; [Augmented] Augments: INT+2 Conserve MP+3 Enmity-6; Requirements: Magic Urn x10 (Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower) Goblin Shaman x15 (Maze of Shakhrami) Backoo x1 (Buburimu Peninsula)\n• Item: Voyager Sallet; Level: 40; [Augmented] Augments: DEF+16 VIT+4 Attack+2; Requirements: Hawker x30 (Riverne - Site A01) Ogrefly x40 (The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah) Guardian Crawler x6 (Crawlers\' Nest)\n• Item: Brigandine; Level: 45; [Augmented] Augments: HP+10 MP+10 STR+2 AGI+2 Attack+4; Requirements: Battering Ram x15 (La Theine Plateau) Tremor Ram x15 (Konschtat Highlands) Tundra Tiger x30 (Beaucedine Glacier) Smilodon x10 (Batallia Downs (S))\n• Item: Hornetneedle; Level: 47; [Augmented] Augments: DMG:+4 Delay:-10 DEX+2; Requirements: Yhoator Wasp x20 (Yhoator Jungle) Volcano Wasp x20 (Ifrit\'s Cauldron) Temple Bee x30 (Temple of Uggalepih)' },
    } },
    { name = 'Combat and jobs', group = 'Server', desc = 'Job adjustments and trusts on CatsEyeXI. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Jobs, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Trusts', steps = {
            { title = 'Jobs: Overview', note = '• This page lists custom changes to jobs compared to retail.\n• Note: for advanced job quests, many of these quests require you to be on a lvl 30+ job for each step of them, please plan accordingly.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Warrior › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Shield Mastery acquired at level 40.\n• Retaliation is now considered a "stance" and lasts 2 hours with a 1-minute recast.\n• Blood Rage acquired at level 75.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Monk › Abilities and Traits', note = '• The duration of the Focus and Dodge job abilities has been extended from 30 seconds to 75 seconds\n• The duration of Footwork has been extended from 60 seconds to 120 seconds\n• Attack Bonus I acquired at level 30, II at level 55, and III at level 70.\n• Smite acquired at level 37\n• Counterstance is now considered a "stance" and lasts 2 hours with a 1-minute recast.\n• Smite II acquired at level 75\n• Perfect Counter acquired at level 75\n• Impetus acquired at level 75\n• Tactical Guard acquired at level 75' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Monk › Adjustments', note = '• The penalty to TP gained on hand-to-hand auto-attacks from Martial Arts delay reduction has been reduced by half.\n• [CW] Crystal Warriors with a Black Belt may re-obtain their Brown Belt via a quest from Raving Fist in Mhaura.\n    ◦ This is for using it in level cap content.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: White Mage › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Gains access to Baramnesra at level 65.\n• Gains access to Enlight at level 75.\n    ◦ Enlight is now a White Mage only spell.\n• Gains access to Arise at level 75.\n    ◦ Cost reduced to 150 Mp and cast time reduced to 10sec.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: White Mage › Adjustments', note = '• Bar-status spells scale with enhancing magic skill.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Black Mage › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Occult Acumen I acquired at Lv60\n• Occult Acumen II acquired at Lv75\n• Enmity Douse acquired at Lv75\n• Gains access to Tier V elemental spells at Lv75.\n    ◦ Obtainable from Higher VNMs\n    ◦ Each spell is equal in power level and MP cost' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Black Mage › Adjustments', note = '• Scythe skill Increased from E to C+, and can learn the weaponskill Entropy' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Red Mage', note = '• Magic Burst Bonus I acquired at Lv70\n• Magic Atk. Bonus III acquired at Lv75\n• Gains access to Baramnesia at level 65\n• inundation is not currently learnable, and there are currently no plans to implement it.\n• Bar-status spells scale with enhancing magic skill.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Abilities and Traits', note = '• The Trick Attack ability transfers a portion of the thief\'s total enmity to the Trick Attack partner (not just the enmity from the attack itself).\n• Accomplice and Collaborator acquired at level 40.\n• Assassin at level 50.\n• Bully at level 60.\n• Conspirator at level 75.\n• Despoil at level 75.\n• As of the 10-10-2024 update.\n• Dual Wield I at level 20\n• Dual Wield II at level 40' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Merits', note = '• In addition to granting an accuracy bonus, Ambush merits also reduce the cooldown of Sneak Attack and Trick Attack.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Weaponskills', note = '• Viper Bite is obtained at 40 Dagger Skill (Level 13)\n• Wasp Sting and Viper Bite have increased damage' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Treasure Hunter › Max Attainable', note = '• On CatsEyeXI, there is a hard cap on how much Treasure Hunter can be obtained by players, from all sources: gear, traits, server bonuses, etc. as follows.\n• To Thief main:\n• [ACE] ACE is 6\n• [CW] CW is 6\n• [WEW] WEW is 8\n• TH: +2; ITEM: Native Treasure Hunter II trait at level 45; Type: All\n• TH: +2; ITEM: Prestige (see below); Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Thief\'s Knife or Vajra (do not stack); Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Assassin\'s Armlets or augmented Rogue\'s Armlets +1; Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: White Rarab Cap +1 (from Exp Ventures) or augmented Dragon Cap +1; Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Tarutaru Sash [Augmented] (from Abyssea - La Theine Sturdy Pyxis); Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Tartarus Platemail; Type: [WEW]\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Talaria; Type: [WEW]\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Summit of the Stars Bonus; Type: All\n• To non-Thief main:\n• [ACE] ACE is 4\n• [CW] CW is 4\n• [WEW] WEW is 4\n• TH: +4; ITEM: THF prestige level 5; Type: All\n• TH: +2; ITEM: Avarice (from Venture Battles); Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: White Rarab Cap +1; Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Tarutaru Sash [Augmented] (from Abyssea - La Theine Sturdy Pyxis); Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Native Treasure Hunter trait at level 15 /THF; Type: All\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Tartarus Platemail; Type: [WEW]\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Talaria; Type: [WEW]\n• TH: +1; ITEM: Summit of the Stars Bonus; Type: All' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Treasure Hunter › Prestige', note = '• To earn a Treasure Hunter +1 Prestige bonus as Thief main job, you must:\n• Have THF prestige at level 4 or higher\n• Trade either a Rogue\'s Armlets+1 that has been augmented with Treasure Hunter, or a Dragon Cap +1 that has been augmented with Treasure Hunter, to Prestix in Upper Jeuno. You still keep the item and the augments. Prestix will not take it from your inventory.\n• To earn a Treasure Hunter +2 prestige bonus as THF main job, you must:\n• Have THF prestige at level 5\n• Trade both of the above augmented items to Prestix. Again, he will return the items after he inspects them.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Thief › Treasure Hunter › Proc System', note = '• As of January 2025, the Treasure Hunter "proc" system has been implemented on CatsEyeXI. The following table shows the chance to proc the next tier of TH on a mob.\n• This table assumes your character\'s treasure hunter is 5, and you are attacking the mob with that TH gear equipped. If your TH level is lower or higher, adjust the number in the first column accordingly.\n• "Feint" in this table indicates that you are either attacking the mob with max-merited Feint on the attack, or that the mob already has the evasion-down effect of a max-merited Feint applied from a previous attack.\n• "SA" and "TA" refers to Sneak Attack and Trick Attack.\n• The maximum TH tier you can proc to on CEXI is 12.\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 5 → 6; Base Proc Chance: 4%; With Feint: 8%; SA or TA: 40%; SA and TA: 80%; Feint + (SA or TA): 80%; Feint + SA + TA: 100%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 6 → 7; Base Proc Chance: 2%; With Feint: 4%; SA or TA: 20%; SA and TA: 40%; Feint + (SA or TA): 40%; Feint + SA + TA: 80%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 7 → 8; Base Proc Chance: 1%; With Feint: 2%; SA or TA: 10%; SA and TA: 20%; Feint + (SA or TA): 20%; Feint + SA + TA: 40%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 8 → 9; Base Proc Chance: 0.5%; With Feint: 1%; SA or TA: 5%; SA and TA: 10%; Feint + (SA or TA): 10%; Feint + SA + TA: 20%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 9 → 10; Base Proc Chance: 0.25%; With Feint: 0.5%; SA or TA: 2.5%; SA and TA: 5%; Feint + (SA or TA): 5%; Feint + SA + TA: 10%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 10 → 11; Base Proc Chance: 0.125%; With Feint: 0.25%; SA or TA: 1.25%; SA and TA: 2.5%; Feint + (SA or TA): 2.5%; Feint + SA + TA: 5%\n• Mob\'s TH Tier: 11 → 12; Base Proc Chance: 0.0625%; With Feint: 0.125%; SA or TA: 0.625%; SA and TA: 1.25%; Feint + (SA or TA): 1.25%; Feint + SA + TA: 2.5%' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Paladin', note = '• No changes.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dark Knight › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Nether Void acquired at level 75.\n• Scarlet Delirium acquired at level 75.\n• Occult Acumen I acquired at level 37 (down from 45).\n• Gains access to Absorb-Attri at level 75.\n• Job Ability Haste, e.g. from Desperate Blows, Hasso, and Haste Samba, caps at 30% instead of 25% on CatsEyeXI. It is noted in this section due to Dark Knight\'s unique ability to cap Job Ability Haste while Last Resort is active. With this change, players can get 25% from Desperate Blows and still benefit from job ability haste from other sources.\n    ◦ Equipment-based haste still caps at 25% as normal.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dark Knight › Weaponskills', note = '• Frostbite and Freezebite have increased damage and apply Frost for a short duration\n• Shadow of Death has increased damage' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Call Beast acquired at level 10\n    ◦ See all Custom Jugs\n• Fencer I acquired at level 60, and II acquired at level 75.\n• Stout Servant acquired at level 75.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Adjustments', note = '• Beastmaster Jug Pets were adjusted in order to address some lacking attributes.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Adjustments › Charisma Bonuses', note = '• Your CHR improves your jug pet in two separate ways, snapshotted at different times. Only CHR from gear, food, merits, and buffs counts, not your base CHR. Charisma from merits counts double. These bonuses are always positive, never negative.\n• Pet Stats:\n• Your +CHR ÷ 2, capped at 100, is added to your pet\'s Attack%, Accuracy, Magic Attack, Magic Accuracy, Defense% and Skillchain Damage; and your +CHR ÷ 8 is added to your pet\'s Counter rate. You must have your CHR gear equipped when you use Call Beast or Bestial Loyalty to lock in this bonus.\n• Ready Strength:\n• A second bonus is applied when you use damage-dealing Ready moves. The bonus is: 1 + (+CHR ÷ 400). Swap in to your CHR gear before using a Ready move to gain this bonus. Allow a after swapping in your gear to make sure it registers.\n• Again, these bonuses do NOT include base CHR, only your +CHR. If BST is your subjob, this bonus is scaled down by sub level / main level.\n• +CHR: +40; Summon Bonus: +20; Ready Bonus: 1.10×\n• +CHR: +80; Summon Bonus: +40; Ready Bonus: 1.20×\n• +CHR: +100; Summon Bonus: +50; Ready Bonus: 1.25×\n• +CHR: +200; Summon Bonus: +100 (cap); Ready Bonus: 1.50×' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Adjustments › Pet TP', note = '• Your pets\' TP (and TP Bonus) now affects your Ready damage to a much greater degree, even when your pet has less than 1000 TP.\n• Most damage-dealing pet skills scale in damage according to this formula: 1 + pet TP ÷ 3000, capped at 2x at full TP.\n• If the pet skill can critical (usually indicated by "Chance of critical hit varies with TP"), a bonus crit chance is applied to that pet skill, scaling from +0% at 0 TP, to +100% at 3000 TP. These pet skills have also been given +15% crit damage.\n• This is in addition to the CHR bonus to damage as described in the section above, and the level-scaling bonus multiplier applied to the damage of all Ready moves (except for ??? Needles) as mentioned in the section below.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Adjustments › Pet Stat Bonuses', note = '• ALL jug pets have had their DEF increased by a flat 10%.\n• ALL jug pets have a level-scaling bonus damage multiplier on Ready skills (except for ??? Needles).\n• The following jug pets have been granted additional enmity for tanking purposes:\n• Jug Pet: Crab Familiar; Enmity+: 10\n• Jug Pet: Courier Carrie; Enmity+: 15\n• Jug Pet: Beetle Familiar; Enmity+: 10\n• Jug Pet: Panzer Galahad; Enmity+: 15\n• In addition, these stats have added to the following jug pets:\n• Jug Pet: Sheep Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Hare Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Crab Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 25\n• DEF — 105\n• Jug Pet: Courier Carrie; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 35\n• DEF — 105\n• Jug Pet: Homunculus; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• EVA — 45\n• Jug Pet: Flytrap Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Tiger Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Flowerpot Bill; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• EVA — 45\n• Jug Pet: Eft Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Lizard Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Mayfly Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Funguar Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Beetle Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 35\n• DEF — 105\n• Jug Pet: Antlion Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Mite Familiar; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 113\n• DEF — 0\n• Jug Pet: Lullaby Melodia; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Keeneared Steffi; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Flowerpot Ben; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• EVA — 45\n• Jug Pet: Saber Siravarde; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Coldblood Como; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Shellbuster Orob; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Voracious Audrey; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Ambusher Allie; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Lifedrinker Lars; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 113\n• DEF — 0\n• Jug Pet: Panzer Galahad; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 35\n• DEF — 105\n• Jug Pet: Chopsuey Chucky; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Amigo Sabotender; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Turbid Toloi; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Slippery Silas; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 88\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Lucky Lulush; Stat: ACC; Value+: 25\n• ATT — 100\n• EVA — 25\n• DEF — 45\n• Jug Pet: Faithful Falcorr; Stat: ACC; Value+: 45\n• ATT — 96\n• EVA — 55\n• DEF — 25\n• MDEF — 4\n• Jug Pet: Dapper Mac; Stat: ACC; Value+: 30\n• ATT — 96\n• DEF — 80\n• MDEF — 10\n• Level Cap:\n• The level cap for the following high-quality pets has been raised to 75\n• Lullaby Melodia (Sheep)\n• Keeneared Steffi (Rabbit)\n• Flowerpot Ben (Mandragora)\n• Saber Siravarde (Tiger)\n• Coldblood Como (Lizard)\n• Shellbuster Orob (Fly)\n• Funguar Familiar (Funguar, no HQ version)' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Beastmaster › Beast Raising', note = '• Beastmaster has access to a new Beast Raising System that is exclusive to CatsEyeXI using the Bestiary Book (G-12) inside the Lower Jeuno Chocobo Stables.\n• Bonuses from this system apply to High-quality Jug Pets. Fully leveled pets provide aura effects for the whole party. The range of this aura is 12 yalms.\n    ◦ Bonuses are only applied when summoned by Call Beast, they will NOT apply when called via Bestial Loyalty.\n• NOTE: Bestiary Book will NOT respond if you have not acquired at least one pet.\n• How to Unlock Beast Raising:\n• There is no level requirement.\n• As BST, kill the requisite source mobs in the below table.\n• After the kill, you have a random chance to obtain it as a pet. If you do not see a message, you need to keep trying.\n• Killing NMs yield a higher chance of success, but can be tedious.\n• Activities and Feeding\n• Players can participate in one, randomly selected, pet activity per day and one pet can be fed per day, each granting pet experience and levels.\n• Feeding: Trade the Bestiary Book the Food item listed below to feed your pet. 100xp\n• Rest: Pet wants to take the day off to rest. 200xp\n• Kill targets: Find the specific target in the zone. 400xp\n• Hot and Cold: /think in the given zone to find the buried treasure. 500xp\n• Pet: LullabyMelodia; Source: Stray Mary (Very Common) (Konschtat Highlands) Mad Sheep (Very Rare) (La Theine Plateau); Food: Boyahda Moss 100 exp.; Activities: 15 Huge Wasp (La Theine Plateau / Konschtat Highlands) 400 exp. Hot and Cold /think (La Theine Plateau / Tahrongi Canyon) 500 exp.; Lv1: Att+10 Def+10; Lv2: Att+15 Def+15; Lv3: Att+20 Def+20; Lv4: Att+25 Def+25; Lv5: Att+30 Def+30; Aura (12\'): Attack +15%\n• Pet: KeenearedSteffi; Source: Ratatoskr (Very Common) (Fort Karugo-Narugo (S)) Beach Bunny (Very Rare) (Cape Teriggan); Food: San d\'Or. Carrot 100 exp.; Activities: 15 Akbaba (La Theine Plateau/Tahrongi Canyon) 400 exp.; Lv1: Acc+10 Eva+10; Lv2: Acc+15 Eva+15; Lv3: Acc+20 Eva+20; Lv4: Acc+25 Eva+25; Lv5: Acc+30 Eva+30; Aura (12\'): Evasion +15%\n• Pet: FlowerpotBen; Source: Backoo (Very Common) (Buburimu Peninsula) Mourioche (Very Rare) (The Boyahda Tree); Food: Yuhtunga Sulfur 100 exp.; Activities: 15 Canyon Crawler (Tahrongi Canyon) / 15 Carnivorous Crawler (Buburimu Peninsula) 400 exp.; Lv1: VIT+5 Att+5; Lv2: VIT+8 Att+8; Lv3: VIT+10 Att+10; Lv4: VIT+12 Att+12; Lv5: VIT+15 Att+15; Aura (12\'): Counter +15%\n• Pet: SaberSiravarde; Source: Tempest Tigon (Very Common) (Carpenters\' Landing) Wajaom Tiger (Very Rare) (Wajaom Woodlands); Food: G. Sheep Meat 100 exp.; Activities: 10 Goblin Butcher (Jugner Forest) / 10 Orcish Impaler (Batallia Downs) 400 exp.; Lv1: DEX+5 Acc+10; Lv2: DEX+8 Acc+15; Lv3: DEX+10 Acc+20; Lv4: DEX+12 Acc+25; Lv5: DEX+15 Acc+30; Aura (12\'): Critical Hit Rate +10%\n• Pet: ColdbloodComo; Source: Geyser Lizard (Very Common) (Dangruf Wadi) Maze Lizard (Very Rare) (Crawlers\' Nest); Food: Crawler Egg 100 exp.; Activities: 15 Raptor (Meriphataud Mountains) 10 Goblin Ambusher (Konschtat Highlands) 400 exp. Hot and Cold /think (Tahrongi Canyon, ???) 500 exp.; Lv1: INT+5 Acc+10; Lv2: INT+8 Acc+15; Lv3: INT+10 Acc+20; Lv4: INT+12 Acc+25; Lv5: INT+15 Acc+30; Aura (12\'): Accuracy +30\n• Pet: ShellbusterOrob; Source: Elusive Edwin (Very Common) (The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah) Monarch Ogrefly (Very Rare) (Attohwa Chasm); Food: Honey 100 exp.; Activities: 15 Coeurl (Meriphataud Mountains) 10 Yagudo Votary (Meriphataud Mountains) 400 exp.; Lv1: DEX+5 MND+5; Lv2: DEX+8 MND+8; Lv3: DEX+10 MND+10; Lv4: DEX+12 MND+12; Lv5: DEX+15 MND+15; Aura (12\'): MND +15%\n• Pet: VoraciousAudrey; Source: Lizardtrap (Very Common) (Aydeewa Subterrane) Hawkertrap (Rare) (Riverne - Site A01); Food: Skull Locust; Activities: 15 Forest Tiger (Carpenters\' Landing) (Jugner Forest Entrance), 10 Land Pugil (Carpenters\' Landing)(San d\'Oria Entrance) 400 exp. Hot and Cold Tahrongi Canyon; Lv1: AGI+5 INT+5; Lv2: AGI+8 INT+8; Lv3: AGI+10 INT+10; Lv4: AGI+12 INT+12; Lv5: AGI+15 INT+15; Aura (12\'): Magic Attack +15%' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Bard', note = '• Fencer I acquired at level 75.\n• Can access Requiescat, see Aeonic WS' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Ranger › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Bounty Shot acquired at level 55.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Ranger › Weaponskills', note = '• Flaming Arrow and Hot Shot will apply Burn for a short duration\n• Wasp Sting and Viper Bite have increased damage' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Ranger › Ranged Distance Penalty', note = '• Ranger, as with all jobs on CatsEyeXI, does not use the ranged distance system. This means that you may use ranged weapons at point-blank range with no penalty.\n• You may see attack messages (your ranged attack "strikes true"), but rest assured, the distance penalty is not in effect on CatsEyeXI.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Samurai › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Hasso and Seigan are now considered a "stances" and last 2 hours with a 1-minute recast.\n• Skillchain Bonus trait at level 75' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Ninja', note = '• All ninjutsu cast on enemies gains +15 magic accuracy.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Ninja › Abilities & Traits', note = '• Futae acquired at level 75.\n• Magic Burst Bonus I acquired at level 75.\n• Tactical Parry I acquired at level 75.\n• Mijin Gakure has been modified to give 3 shadows, and reduces the character to 1hp.\n• Elemental Ninjutsu San level spells are available to buy from Solby-Maholby in Norg, rather than merited catagory. Warning, they are not cheap, the price on the npc\'s page is not reflective of CatsEyeXI pricing.\n    ◦ Casting elemental ninjutsu can now grant TP similar to the Occult Acumen trait. When you cast elemental ninjutsu on an enemy and deal at least 1 damage, you will now gain TP equal your Ninja Tool Expertise (max 100). The TP gained can be further increased with Store TP.\n    ◦ Casting elemental Ninjutsu also is buffed to gain enmity while casting the wheel. The amount of enmity, how much of the wheel to go through, or effect to gain to start it is unknown at this time.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dragoon › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Fly High acquired at level 75.\n• Dragon Breaker and the ability to use fjoturangons acquired via a quest at Sigmund in Mhaura. To unlock Dragon Breaker and the ability to use fjoturangons, players must speak with Sigmund in Mhaura after completing the Dragonslayer intro quest. Players will need: to have defeated at least 5 different "DKP" dragons, be Level 75 Dragoon, have 1,000 DKP, have 200 Stored Merits (ACE)/75 Stored Merits (CW/WEW), and trade a dragon heart, dragon talon, wyrm scale, and wyrm tooth. Use of a fjoturangon with the Angon ability will force a flying Wyrm to the ground (additionally, it will proc a Dragonslaying foe). In addition, the "defense down" status effect of a fjoturangon lasts for 15 more seconds than a standard angon.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dragoon › Merits', note = '• Dragoon\'s Call Wyvern recast is now reduced by 3 minutes per tier of Empathy as of the 10-10-2024 update.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Summoner', note = '• Odin, Cait Sith, Siren, and Atomos are not available at this time.\n    ◦ However, Wings-Era Warriors that merged in from the WingsXI server with it are capable of calling Cait Sith.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Summoner › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Mana Cede acquired at level 75.\n• Fleet Wind acquired at level 75.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Summoner › Adjustments', note = '• Summoners may teleport to Cloisters after completing "Trial-Size" Mini-fork trials, without the use of a Mini-fork.\n    ◦ To initiate the teleport, Summoners must trade a nominal 100 gil to the respective NPC.\n• Light Spirit was adjusted to cast its protect and shell spells, enhanced similarly to how a scholar can make them AoE.\n• All magical Blood Pacts now gain +15 magic accuracy.\n• Group 2 Merit Blood Pacts now deal +25% damage.' },
