            { title = 'Jobs: Blue Mage › Adjustments', note = '• Blue Mage gets Unbridled Learning at 75 after the 9-12-2024 update.\n    ◦ This ability must be active to use Harden Shell, Pyric Bulwark, and Carcharian Verve.\n    ◦ There is no need to set these spells - they will become available when the Unbridled Learning effect is active.\n• Blue Magic affected by Diffusion gets the bonus from gear that increases Enhancing Magic Duration after the 8-22-2024 update.\n• Blue Mage now gets an extra set point per tier of Assimilation for a total of +10 at rank 5 after the 8-8-2024 update.\n• Boruko (J-10) in Aht Urghan Whitegate (Near Waoud) provides players with additional Blue Magic Points as of the 9-19-2024 update.\n    ◦ Players earn points based on how many Blue Magic Spells they have learned, up to a maximum of 25 points.\n    ◦ Players with Lv.75 Blue Mage with access to merits is required to receive these bonuses.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Blue Mage › Spells', note = '• Some spells that are normally higher than Lv.75 have been added to Blue Mage. Although some of these spells are normally learned from monsters that are found in areas not currently available on the CatsEyeXI server, customizations have been made to find them in other areas as noted below.\n• The spells listed are found in the same areas/mobs as retail unless noted.\n• Spell: Acrid Stream; Level: 75; Notes: Clionid, Escha - Ru\'Aun on Seiryu\'s island\n• Spell: Demoralizing Roar; Level: 75; Notes: Wivre\n• Spell: Empty Thrash; Level: 75; Notes: Craver\n• Spell: Heavy Strike; Level: 75; Notes: Golem\n• Spell: Blazing Bound; Level: 75; Notes: Limule, Escha - Ru\'Aun on Suzaku\'s island\n• Spell: Quadratic Continuum; Level: 75; Notes: Gorger\n• Spell: Barbed Crescent; Level: 75; Notes: Fomor\n• Spell: Plenilune Embrace; Level: 75; Notes: Gnole\n• Spell: Osmosis; Level: 75; Notes: Amoeban, Escha - Ru\'Aun on Genbu\'s Island\n• Spell: Occultation; Level: 75; Notes: Seether\n• Spell: Barrier Tusk; Level: 75; Notes: Marid\n• Spell: Magic Barrier; Level: 75; Notes: Ahriman\n• Spell: Orcish Counterstance; Level: 75; Notes: Any Orcs in the past [S] zones.\n• Spell: Harden Shell; Level: 75; Notes: Pygmytoise in Gustav Tunnel lower level. Must be under the effect of Unbridled Learning to use.\n• Spell: Pyric Bulwark; Level: 75; Notes: Tinnin hydra mobs. Must be under the effect of Unbridled Learning to use.\n• Spell: Carcharian Verve; Level: 75; Notes: Tchakka in Domain Invasion.\n• Spell: Animating Wail; Level: 75; Notes: Qutrub\n• Spell: Battery Charge; Level: 75; Notes: Magic Pot\n• Spell: Anvil Lightning; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Ungeweder\n• Spell: Blinding Fulgor; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Baelfyr\n• Spell: Silent Storm; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Ungeweder\n• Spell: Entomb; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Byrgen\n• Spell: Glutinous Dart; Level: 75; Notes: Velkk Intruder\n• Spell: Searing Tempest; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Baelfyr\n• Spell: Scouring Spate; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Gefyrst\n• Spell: Spectral Floe; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Gefyrst\n• Spell: Tenebral Crush; Level: 75; Notes: Wild Byrgen' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Blue Mage › Limit Break', note = '• See the Custom LB5 quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Corsair', note = '• Marksmanship skill increased from B to A\n• Club skill added at E.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Corsair › Extra Rolls', note = '• Corsair has been given rolls beyond level 75 on the server:\n• Caster\'s Roll (Fast Cast) - Complete the custom quest X Marks the Spot.\n• Bolter\'s Roll (Movement Speed) - Complete the custom quest X Marks the Spot.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Corsair › Artifact Armor', note = '• The AF quest Against All Odds does not function correctly, and has a work-around.\n• Start the quest then speak to Mnejing in Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-10) to receive your Corsair\'s Tricorne.\n• The Hydrogauge for Navigating the Unfriendly Seas can be found by clicking the ??? on the Aht Urhgan Whitegate Docks at I-11/12. It can also be fished up from Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Al Zahbi, Nashmau, and Silver Sea route to Al Zahbi, with any rod and any bait.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Corsair › Limit Break', note = '• See the Custom LB5 quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Adjustments', note = '• The penalty to TP gained on hand-to-hand auto-attacks from Martial Arts delay reduction has been reduced by half.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Important note', note = '• Due to balancing and server stability /pup is not usable, whilst you can set PUP as a subjob summoning the Automaton will not function!' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Frames', note = '• Frames are obtained via Ghatsad, as per retail.\n• Crystal Warriors can obtain the required materials via a custom quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Oils', note = '• Gavrie does sell oil\'s off in Aht Urhgan Whitegate for the normal retail prices of 50/250/500 gil a piece, buyable in stacks of 12. The crafting recipe is working also.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Attachments', note = '• Most Attachments work.\n• See Mnejing\'s Puppetmaster Shop for attachments that aren\'t otherwise sold from Yoyoroon in Nashmau at (G-6)\n    ◦ Rararoon is disabled on the server. Some of Rararoon\'s inventory is sold by Mnejing\'s.\n    ◦ Note: Crystal Warrior\'s cannot use Mnejing\'s Puppetmaster Shop. Attachments he sells are obtained from Goblin\'s Gambit, Ob, Hilltroll Puppetmasters or Troll Machinists.\n    ◦ Some previously obtained attachments were given the wrong version and are not able to be equipped. Permitted attachments can be exchanged for the correct version free of charge at Geppetto (I-6) in Aht Urhgan Whitegate.\n• All methods to obtain attachments include: AH, Crafting, Mnejing\'s Shop, Yoyoroon, drops from Ob Zeni NM, Goblin\'s Gambit, Hilltroll Puppetmasters, Troll Machinists, random world treasure caskets, and finally the random item Gobbie Mystery Box. Not every attachment possible from the Gobbie Box is confirmed working though, as the loot pool for it is too massive to audit. See the table below for the confirmed working Attachments with methods of obtaining being possible unless otherwise stated.\n    ◦ The Amplifier II is confirmed coded and working, only way of obtainment is Gobbie box at this time. The crafting recipe is not enabled yet, further testing on the effect and power of the Amp I is wanted to be seen before enabling the recipe. -Haruuc 4-30-2026\n    ◦ The Optic Fiber II is in the client, but is only obtainable via the gobbie box.\n• The only Softly confirmed attachment NOT wanted in the game is the Coiler II attachment. -Runham 6/28/2025\n    ◦ Truesights has been implented into LSB, but not enabled on CEXI. No Data available if possible Gobbie box chance.\n• Automatons may be equipped with attachments which boost and augment their capabilities. Initially received as items, they must be traded to equip in the automaton equipment menu. Once traded they can not be turned back into items.\n• While your main job is Puppetmaster speak with Tateeya in the Automaton Workshop at (I-7) in Aht Urhgan Whitegate then trade her the attachments. She won\'t take an attachment that you have already traded before.\n• After the initial dialogue you may trade attachments on any job.\n• Available Attachments: Note: Not all of these attachments may function correctly, but these are all the permitted ones for use. This note was updated last very long ago about the "permitted" ones for use, if the Attachment is in the game and obtainable, and you are able to trade it Tateeya to equip it, then it is allowed. There is no banning for using attachments unless game-breaking. Whether or not they are fully coded to work as Retail is a different story, the following table should all be working as intended, and obtainable in some way.\n    ◦ Name: Attuner; Description: Enhances attack against powerful enemies.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Flame Holder; Description: Converts the energy of a Fire Maneuver into attack power during weapon skills.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Heat Capacitor; Description: Erases all Fire Maneuver effects to restore TP.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Heat Capacitor II; Description: Erases all Fire Maneuver effects to restore TP.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Inhibitor; Description: Store TP Improves TP usage efficiency.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Inhibitor II; Description: Store TP Improves TP usage efficiency.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Magniplug; Description: Enhances weapon damage.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Magniplug II; Description: Enhances weapon damage.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Reactive Shield; Description: Use Blaze Spikes.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Speedloader; Description: Focuses on taking advantage of skillchains and grants a skillchain bonus.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Speedloader II; Description: Focuses on taking advantage of skillchains and grants a skillchain bonus.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Strobe; Description: Increases enmity Occasionally use Provoke.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Strobe II; Description: Increases enmity Occasionally use Provoke.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Tension Spring; Description: Enhances attack.; Capacity: Fire\n    ◦ Name: Tension Spring II; Description: Enhances attack.; Capacity: Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Tension Spring III; Description: Enhances attack.; Capacity: Fire Fire Fire\n    ◦ Name: Amplifier; Description: Increases magic burst damage. Attempts to use magic bursts more.; Capacity: Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Amplifier II; Description: Increases magic burst damage. Attempts to use magic bursts more.; Capacity: Ice Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Arcanoclutch; Description: Enhances magic Damage.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Ice Maker; Description: Converts the energy of an Ice Maneuver into magic attack when casting magic spells.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Loudspeaker; Description: Enhances magic attack.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Loudspeaker II; Description: Enhances magic attack.; Capacity: Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Loudspeaker III; Description: Enhances magic attack.; Capacity: Ice Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Mana Booster; Description: Shortens spellcasting time.; Capacity: Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Power Cooler; Description: Reduces MP cost.; Capacity: Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Scanner; Description: Occasionally scans target\'s magic resistances.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Tactical Processor; Description: Decreases decision-making time.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Tranquilizer; Description: Enhances magic accuracy.; Capacity: Ice\n    ◦ Name: Tranquilizer II; Description: Enhances magic accuracy.; Capacity: Ice Ice\n    ◦ Name: Accelerator; Description: Enhances evasion.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Accelerator II; Description: Enhances evasion.; Capacity: Wind Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Accelerator III; Description: Enhances evasion.; Capacity: Wind Wind Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Barrage Turbine; Description: Erases all Wind Maneuver effects to occasionally grant a Barrage effect.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Drum Magazine; Description: Sacrifices accuracy for speed in ranged attacks.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Pattern Reader; Description: Analyzes enemy attack patterns and gradually enhances evasion.; Capacity: Wind\n    ◦ Name: Repeater; Description: Occasionally executes multiple ranged attacks.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Replicator; Description: When HP is low, converts all Wind Maneuvers into shadow images.; Capacity: Wind\n    ◦ Name: Scope; Description: Enhances ranged accuracy.; Capacity: Wind\n    ◦ Name: Scope II; Description: Enhances ranged accuracy.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Scope III; Description: Enhances ranged accuracy.; Capacity: Wind Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Turbo Charger; Description: Adds Haste effect.; Capacity: Wind Wind\n    ◦ Name: Analyzer; Description: Increases chance of mitigating the effects of special attacks previously used by the enemy.; Capacity: Earth\n    ◦ Name: Armor Plate; Description: Reduces Physical Damage Taken.; Capacity: Earth Earth\n    ◦ Name: Armor Plate II; Description: Reduces Physical Damage Taken.; Capacity: Earth Earth Earth\n    ◦ Name: Armor Plate III; Description: Reduces Physical Damage Taken.; Capacity: Earth Earth Earth Earth\n    ◦ Name: Barrier Module; Description: Increases chance of blocking with shield. Earth Maneuver: Adds Shield Mastery and shortens Shield Bash recast time.; Capacity: Earth\n    ◦ Name: Barrier Module II; Description: Increases chance of blocking with shield. Earth Maneuver: Adds Shield Mastery and shortens Shield Bash recast time.; Capacity: Earth Earth\n    ◦ Name: Equalizer; Description: Reduces damage received according to damage taken.; Capacity: Earth Earth\n    ◦ Name: Hammermill; Description: Increases the damage inflicted by Shield Bash May also induce Slow effect.; Capacity: Earth\n    ◦ Name: Schurzen; Description: May erase an Earth Maneuver effect to reduce severe physical damage.; Capacity: Earth\n    ◦ Name: Shock Absorber; Description: Use Stoneskin.; Capacity: Earth\n    ◦ Name: Coiler; Description: Occasionally grants the automaton bonus melee attacks.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Dynamo; Description: Increases critical hit rate.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Galvanizer; Description: Increases chance of countering.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Heat Seeker; Description: Analyzes enemy evasion patterns and gradually enhances accuracy.; Capacity: Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Stabilizer; Description: Enhances accuracy.; Capacity: Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Stabilizer II; Description: Enhances accuracy.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Stabilizer III; Description: Enhances accuracy.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Target Marker; Description: Enhances accuracy against powerful enemies.; Capacity: Lightning Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Volt Gun; Description: Adds lightning damage to attacks.; Capacity: Lightning\n    ◦ Name: Condenser; Description: May erase a Water Maneuver effect to prevent an overload.; Capacity: Water\n    ◦ Name: Heatsink; Description: Reduces Overload rate.; Capacity: Water\n    ◦ Name: Mana Channeler; Description: Increases magic recast time in exchange for increased magic attack.; Capacity: Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Mana Jammer; Description: Enhances magic defense.; Capacity: Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Mana Jammer II; Description: Enhances magic defense.; Capacity: Water Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Mana Jammer III; Description: Enhances magic defense.; Capacity: Water Water Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Percolator; Description: Increases skill gain rate.; Capacity: Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Resister; Description: Increases status ailment resistance.; Capacity: Water\n    ◦ Name: Resister II; Description: Increases status ailment resistance.; Capacity: Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Stealth Screen; Description: Reduces enmity.; Capacity: Water\n    ◦ Name: Stealth Screen II; Description: Reduces enmity.; Capacity: Water Water\n    ◦ Name: Steam Jacket; Description: Reduces damage taken from successive attacks of the same type.; Capacity: Water\n    ◦ Name: Arcanic Cell; Description: Enhances Occult Acumen.; Capacity: Light\n    ◦ Name: Arcanic Cell II; Description: Enhances Occult Acumen.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Auto-Repair Kit; Description: Increases HP Adds "Regen" effect to Light Maneuver.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Auto-Repair Kit II; Description: Increases HP Adds "Regen" effect to Light Maneuver.; Capacity: Light Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Auto-Repair Kit III; Description: Increases HP Adds "Regen" effect to Light Maneuver.; Capacity: Light Light Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Damage Gauge; Description: Prioritizes curing.; Capacity: Light\n    ◦ Name: Eraser; Description: Erase enfeebling and all maneuver effects.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Flashbulb; Description: Use Flash.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Optic Fiber; Description: Increases the performance of other attachments.; Capacity: Light\n    ◦ Name: Optic Fiber II; Description: Increases the performance of other attachments.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Vivi-Valve; Description: Increases "Cure" potency.; Capacity: Light Light\n    ◦ Name: Disruptor; Description: Use Dispel.; Capacity: Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Economizer; Description: When MP is low, may erase all Dark Maneuver effects to restore MP.; Capacity: Dark\n    ◦ Name: Mana Conserver; Description: Conserve MP.; Capacity: Dark\n    ◦ Name: Mana Converter; Description: Consumes HP to gradually restore MP.; Capacity: Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Mana Tank; Description: Increases MP Adds "Refresh" effect to Dark Maneuver.; Capacity: Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Mana Tank II; Description: Increases MP Adds "Refresh" effect to Dark Maneuver.; Capacity: Dark Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Mana Tank III; Description: Increases MP Adds "Refresh" effect to Dark Maneuver.; Capacity: Dark Dark Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Regulator; Description: Enables automaton to absorb a foe\'s beneficial status effect.; Capacity: Dark Dark Dark\n    ◦ Name: Smoke Screen; Description: Decreases accuracy, increases evasion.; Capacity: Dark Dark' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Artifact Armor', note = '• The quest Puppetmaster Blues is not functional.\n• To unlock the Puppetry Taj, you must complete the quest Operation Teatime and then speak to Mnejing in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at (G-10) to receive it.\n• The other Artifact Armor pieces are commissioned by Mnejing, instead of Dhima Polevhia.\n    ◦ You need to trade Mnejing the materials and currency at the same time\n    ◦ You do not need to wait a game day or zone between commissions, simply trade the items and currency and you will receive the piece\n• Armor: Puppetry Babouches; Ingredients:; Ruby; Wamoura Cloth; Marid Leather; Platinum Sheet; Coin Cost: Imperial Mythril Piece x2\n• Armor: Puppetry Dastanas; Ingredients:; Rainbow Thread; Wamoura Cloth; Marid Leather; Platinum Sheet; Coin Cost: Imperial Mythril Piece\n• Armor: Puppetry Tobe; Ingredients:; Ruby; Wamoura Cloth; Moblinweave; Scarlet Linen; Coin Cost: Imperial Gold Piece' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Limit Break', note = '• See the Custom LB5 quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Puppetmaster › Specific Changes', note = '• As of the 1/2/2026 update, Automatons now have a 95% resistance to instant-death spells and mob abilities (Haruuc).' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dancer', note = '• Club skill added at E.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dancer › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Divine Waltz II acquired at level 60.\n• Feather Step acquired at level 65.\n• Presto acquired at level 75.\n• Tactical Parry I acquired at level 75.\n• Critical Attack Bonus I acquired at level 75.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Dancer › Limit Break', note = '• See the Custom LB5 quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Scholar › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Gains Immanence at 75.\n• Gains Perpetuance at 75.\n• Gains Occult Acumen I at level 60.\n• Gains Occult Acumen II at level 75.\n• Level: 10; # of Charges: 1; Time to Regain One Charge: 4 min.\n• Level: 30; # of Charges: 2; Time to Regain One Charge: 2 min.\n• Level: 50; # of Charges: 3; Time to Regain One Charge: 1 min. 20 sec.\n• Level: 65; # of Charges: 4; Time to Regain One Charge: 1 min.\n• Level: 75; # of Charges: 5*; Time to Regain One Charge: 48 sec.\n• The FFXI Client will only show 4 charges but you have 5 available when maxed' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Scholar › Limit Break', note = '• See the Custom LB5 quest.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Scholar › Artifact Armor', note = '• The SCH AF3 quest doesn\'t work as normal, but has a work around. Next to Erlene is a box labeled "SCH AF3"; click on that to start the Seeing Blood-red quest. Then, travel to Pashhow Marshlands (S) (E-11) but instead of clicking Indescript Markings, click the box labled SCH AF Hat to receive Unaddressed sealed letter. Once you have the key item, return to The Eldieme Necropolis (S) and click the SCH AF3 box labeled SCH AF3 to obtain your Scholar\'s M.board and complete the quest.\n• The remaining pieces from Loussaire work as intended.\n    ◦ The Indescript Markings for Scholar\'s Pants appeared around 10:00 game time for me. Outside the suggested 16:00-6:00 window.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Unlock', note = '• To unlock Geomancer you must first complete one job to level 75, then complete the quest The Unnamed Way from Master Lao in Windurst Waters (South) (K-8).' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Lvl.: 10; Name: Conserve MP\n• Lvl.: 20; Name: Clear Mind\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Cardinal Chant♦\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Conserve MP II\n• Lvl.: 30; Name: Max MP Boost I\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Clear Mind II\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Conserve MP III\n• Lvl.: 45; Name: Cardinal Chant II♦\n• Lvl.: 55; Name: Elemental Celerity\n• Lvl.: 55; Name: Conserve MP IV\n• Lvl.: 60; Name: Clear Mind III\n• Lvl.: 60; Name: Max MP Boost II\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Cardinal Chant III♦\n• Lvl.: 70; Name: Conserve MP V\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Curative Recantation\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Primordial Zeal\n• Lvl.: 1; Name: Bolster\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Full Circle\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Lasting Emanation\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Ecliptic Attrition\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Collimated Fervor\n• Lvl.: 50; Name: Life Cycle\n• Lvl.: 60; Name: Blaze of Glory\n• Lvl.: 70; Name: Dematerialize\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Entrust\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Mending Halation\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Radial Arcana' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Adjustments', note = '• ♦ Cardinal Chant was altered to provide an affinity boost to magic, determined by where the target is located relative to the caster when the elemental magic spell actually lands on the target, instead of the retail bonuses.\n• Affinity is a separate Magic Damage multiplier for a particular element. It sits at a 1.0 in the equation, and increases when affinity is added.\n• For refence below, an NQ elemental staff adds 0.05 to the multiplier. An HQ adds 0.1.\n    ◦ Those staves also add magical accuracy based on this of +10 and +20.\n• Collimated Fervor enhances the bonuses of Cardinal Chant by 50%.\n• N Dark\n• NW Fire — NE Light\n• W Water — E Ice\n• SW Thunder — SE Wind\n• S Earth\n• Tier I — Level 25 — +0.05 Affinity — +5 Magic Accuracy\n• Tier II — Level 45 — +0.1 Affinity — +10 Magic Accuracy\n• Tier III — Level 65 — +0.15 Affinity — +15 Magic Accuracy' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Geomancy', note = '• Geomancy: Geocolure spells are learned through use of Geomantic Reservoirs after learning the corresponding Indicolure spell. While they may be available at the appropriate level of Geomancer as a sub-job, only main job Geomancers may cast Geocolure spells.\n    ◦ Lvl.: 1; Name: Indi-Poison; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 4; Name: Indi-Voidance; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 4; Name: Stone; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 5; Name: Geo-Poison; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 8; Name: Geo-Voidance; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 9; Name: Water; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 10; Name: Indi-Precision; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 14; Name: Aero; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 14; Name: Geo-Precision; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 15; Name: Drain; Acquisition: Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 15; Name: Indi-Regen; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 16; Name: Indi-Attunement; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 19; Name: Fire; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 19; Name: Geo-Regen; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 20; Name: Geo-Attunement; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 22; Name: Indi-Focus; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 24; Name: Blizzard; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 25; Name: Stonera; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 26; Name: Geo-Focus; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 28; Name: Indi-Barrier; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 29; Name: Thunder; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 30; Name: Indi-Refresh; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 30; Name: Aspir; Acquisition: Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 30; Name: Indi-CHR; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 30; Name: Watera; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 32; Name: Geo-Barrier; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 33; Name: Indi-MND; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 34; Name: Indi-Fury; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 34; Name: Geo-Refresh; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 34; Name: Geo-CHR; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 34; Name: Stone II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 35; Name: Aera; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 35; Name: Sleep; Acquisition: Various\n    ◦ Lvl.: 36; Name: Indi-INT; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 37; Name: Geo-MND; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 38; Name: Geo-Fury; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 38; Name: Water II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 39; Name: Indi-AGI; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 40; Name: Indi-Fend; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 40; Name: Geo-INT; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 40; Name: Fira; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 42; Name: Aero II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 42; Name: Indi-VIT; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 43; Name: Geo-AGI; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 44; Name: Geo-Fend; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 45; Name: Indi-DEX; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 45; Name: Blizzara; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 46; Name: Fire II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 46; Name: Indi-Acumen; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 46; Name: Geo-VIT; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 48; Name: Indi-STR; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 48; Name: Indi-Slow; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 49; Name: Geo-DEX; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 50; Name: Blizzard II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 50; Name: Geo-Acumen; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 50; Name: Thundara; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 52; Name: Indi-Torpor; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 52; Name: Geo-STR; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 52; Name: Geo-Slow; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 54; Name: Thunder II; Acquisition: Chutarmire\n    ◦ Lvl.: 56; Name: Geo-Torpor; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 58; Name: Indi-Slip; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 58; Name: Stone III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 61; Name: Water III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 62; Name: Geo-Slip; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 64; Name: Aero III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 64; Name: Indi-Languor; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 67; Name: Fire III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 68; Name: Indi-Paralysis; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 68; Name: Geo-Languor; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 70; Name: Blizzard III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 70; Name: Indi-Vex; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 70; Name: Sleep II; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 70; Name: Stonera II; Acquisition: Sylvie\n    ◦ Lvl.: 72; Name: Geo-Paralysis; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 73; Name: Thunder III; Acquisition: Susu\n    ◦ Lvl.: 74; Name: Geo-Vex; Acquisition: Reservoir\n    ◦ Lvl.: 74; Name: Indi-Haste; Acquisition: AF Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 74; Name: Geo-Haste; Acquisition: AF Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 74; Name: Indi-Frailty; Acquisition: AF Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 74; Name: Geo-Frailty; Acquisition: AF Quest\n    ◦ Lvl.: 75; Name: Watera II; Acquisition: Sylvie' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Artifact Armor', note = '• Geomancer Artifact Weapons may be obtained through the custom questThe Earth Holds Its Breath:\n• Dowser\'s Wand (Club, Lv40, GEO, DMG:15, Delay:216, INT+2 Magic Accuracy+2, Rare, Ex)\n• Filiae Bell (Handbell, Lv40, GEO, MP+15 MND+1, Rare, Ex)\n• Geomancer Artifact Armor may be obtained through the custom process below once reaching level 75.\n• Artifact #1\n• Talk to Drunk Taru in Bibiki Bay (G-10).\n• He will ask for a, obtained through Domain Invasion point exchange NPC, Domain Officer, Near Upper Jeuno Auction House (G-9).\n• Trade the Pearlscale and you will obtain the Geomancy Sandals.\n• Artifact #2\n• Talk to Drunk Taru in Bibiki Bay (G-10).\n• He will ask for a Seal of Byakko.\n• Trade him the Seal of Byakko and you will obtain the Geomancy Mitaines.\n• Artifact #3\n• Talk to Drunk Taru in Bibiki Bay (G-10).\n• He will ask for a Siren\'s Tear.\n• Touch the ??? by the river at the (J-8/9) in North Gustaberg with no main or sub equipped.\n• Trade him the Siren\'s Tear to obtain the Geomancy Galero.\n• Artifact #4\n• Talk to Drunk Taru in Bibiki Bay (G-10).\n• He will ask for a Oil-Soaked Cloth.\n• Trade him the Oil-Soaked Cloth to obtain the Geomancy Pants.\n• Artifact #5\n• Talk to Drunk Taru in Bibiki Bay (G-10).\n• He requests you return to him with the title received from killing the notorious monster Sandworm.\n• Return to him with the title "Sandworm Wrangler" to complete the quest.\n• You will obtain the Geomancy Tunic.\n    ◦ Additionally, speak to Drunk Taru one more time to have the following spells added directly to your spell list:\n• Geo-Frailty / Indi-Frailty\n• Geo-Haste / Indi-Haste\n• Item: Geomancy Galero; Stats: DEF: 25 MP +25 INT +5 Elemental Skill +15 Enhances Cardinal Chant\n• Item: Geomancy Tunic; Stats: DEF: 40 MP +35 Dark Skill +12 Enhances Life Cycle\n• Item: Geomancy Mitaines; Stats: DEF: 15 MP +16 INT +3 MND +4 Geomancy Skill +15 Luopan: Damage Taken -6%\n• Item: Geomancy Pants; Stats: DEF: 30 MP +20 Fast Cast +10% Spell Interruption Rate -15%\n• Item: Geomancy Sandals; Stats: DEF: 12 MP +15 AGI +5 CHR +5 Movement Speed +12%' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Relic Armor', note = '• Details on which zones to obtain Relic Armor and its upgrade process can be found here.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Relic Weapon', note = '• Geomancer has access to Mjollnir (Level 75)' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Geomancer › Ergon Weapon', note = '• Idris has been added as of the 9-12-2024 update.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Unlock', note = '• To unlock Rune Fencer you must first complete one job to level 75, then complete the quest Runic Insurrection from Octavien in Bastok Markets (F-10).' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Abilities and Traits', note = '• Lvl.: 5; Name: Tenacity\n• Lvl.: 10; Name: Magic Defense Bonus\n• Lvl.: 15; Name: Inquartata\n• Lvl.: 20; Name: Max HP Boost I\n• Lvl.: 30; Name: Magic Defense Bonus II\n• Lvl.: 35; Name: Auto Regen\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Tactical Parry\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Max HP Boost II\n• Lvl.: 45; Name: Inquartata II\n• Lvl.: 50; Name: Magic Defense Bonus III\n• Lvl.: 50; Name: Accuracy Bonus I\n• Lvl.: 60; Name: Max HP Boost III\n• Lvl.: 65; Name: Auto Regen II\n• Lvl.: 70; Name: Magic Defense Bonus IV\n• Lvl.: 70; Name: Accuracy Bonus II\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Magic Defense Bonus V\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Inquartata III\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Inspiration\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Sleight of Sword\n• Lvl.: 1; Name: Elemental Sforzo\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Ignis\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Gelus\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Flabra\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Tellus\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Sulpor\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Unda\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Lux\n• Lvl.: 5; Name: Tenebrae\n• Lvl.: 10; Name: Vallation\n• Lvl.: 20; Name: Swordplay\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Swipe\n• Lvl.: 25; Name: Lunge\n• Lvl.: 40; Name: Pflug\n• Lvl.: 50; Name: Valiance\n• Lvl.: 60; Name: Embolden\n• Lvl.: 65; Name: Vivacious Pulse\n• Lvl.: 70; Name: Gambit\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: One for All\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Battuta\n• Lvl.: 75; Name: Rayke\n• Level: 1; # of Runes: 1\n• Level: 35; # of Runes: 2\n• Level: 65; # of Runes: 3' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Magic', note = '• Gains access to Flash at level 38.\n• Gains access to Crusade at level 56.\n• Gains access to Baramnesia at level 63.\n• Bar-status spells scale with enhancing magic skill.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Artifact Armor', note = '• Runefencer Artifact Weapon may be obtained through the custom quest Forged in Frost and Flame:\n• Beorc Sword (Great Sword, Lv40, RUN, DMG:56, Delay:480, Magic Attack Bonus +2, Parrying Skill +3, Rare, Ex)\n• Rune Fencer Artifact Armor may be obtained through the custom process below once reaching level 75.\n• Artifact #1\n• Talk to West Minstrel in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-9) just down the stairs from HP #1.\n• Talk to Varado in South Gustaberg (J-8, Southwest corner), at the top of the mountain.\n• Examine the Stranger Flower at Blueblade Fell in Lufaise Meadows (J-6) to obtain the Key item Yahse wildflower petal.\n• Talk to Varado in South Gustaberg again (J-8).\n• Zone (logging out works) and talk to Varado once again.\n• You will obtain the Runeist Mitons and may now start AF #2/3/4.\n• Artifact #2/3/4\n• Talk to Caida in East Ronfaure (H-10, Northeast corner)\n• Talk to Caida in East Ronfaure (H-10) again and ask about all three runes\n    ◦ Rune of Power\n    ◦ Go to Rolanberry Fields (K-10), click the ??? for an NM battle.\n    ◦ After defeating the NM click the ??? again for a Key item Vivid Rainbow Extract.\n    ◦ Rune of Wisdom\n    ◦ Solve the cipher. (Examine the ??? at the Aged Arbor, E-5 in Batillia Downs from Beaucedine Glacier entrance)\n    ◦ Rune of Courage\n    ◦ Go to Monastic Cavern (J-7), examine the ??? for a Key item Runic Kinegraver.\n• Return to Caida in East Ronfaure (H-10) and turn in your key items.\n• You will obtain the Runeist Bottes, Runeist Trousers, and Runeist Coat\n• After obtaining the gear, talk to Caida again and make sure he tells you to go to the desert.\n• Artifact #5\n• Go to Eastern Altepa Desert and speak to Babus at (F-10).\n• Inquire about the trial.\n• Trade Babus (F-10) a seal of Byakko, Genbu, Seiryu, and Suzaku, they will be returned.\n• You will obtain the Runeist Bandeau.\n• Item: Runeist Bandeau; Stats: DEF: 27 HP +27 DEX +5 Physical Damage Taken -3% Increases Regen Duration +3\n• Item: Runeist Coat; Stats: DEF: 50 HP +20 MP +20 STR +5 VIT +5 Resist All Elements +10 Enhances Valiance and Vallation\n• Item: Runeist Mitons; Stats: DEF: 21 MP +22 DEX +3 VIT +3 Refresh +1 Enhances Gambit\n• Item: Runeist Trousers; Stats: DEF: 40 HP +15 MP +15 STR +7 Enmity +5 Damage Taken -3%\n• Item: Runeist Bottes; Stats: DEF: 18 MP +18 VIT +6 Magic Defense Bonus +2 "Pflug" +10' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Relic Armor', note = '• Details on which zones to obtain Relic Armor and its upgrade process can be found here.' },
            { title = 'Jobs: Rune Fencer › Ergon Weapon', note = '• Epeolatry has been added as of the 9-12-2024 update.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Unlocking', note = '• [ACE] ACE players can call up to 5 trusts. They unlock 3 trust "slots" at level 5, then 1 additional from completing each of RoV Missions 1-6 and 2-13.\n• [CW] CW players can call up to 2 trusts. They unlock their first trust "slot" by completing any Matter of Trust 1 quest, and another "slot" by completing any Matter of Trust 3 quest (see CatsEyeXI Systems/Quests). Usage is then restricted to 1 trust from lv.10, and 2 trusts from lv.40.\n• [WEW] WEW players can not call trusts.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Notes', note = '• Completing RoV mission 2-30, instead of Rhapsody in Emerald, grants the following bonuses to all game modes:\n• All summoned Trusts gain bonuses to attack, defense, and magic accuracy, and also receive Refresh+1' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Healers', note = '• Name (Job): Apururu (UC) (WHM/RDM); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Apururu Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Every conquest tally you must earn 5000 accolades to keep Apururu (UC).\n• Name (Job): Cherukiki (WHM/BLM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete CoP 6-4. Speak with Taillegeas in Ru\'Lude Gardens (I-7).; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Kupipi (WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: Windurst [CW] via A Matter of Trust III (Windurst); Customized: No; Notes: Has Bonus to Magic Accuracry. Prioritises tanks for healing <75% HP. Others <50% HP. Modified to lower priority for Paralyze and Slow.\n• Name (Job): Mihli Aliapoh (WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] RoE Tutorial [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Pieuje (UC) (WHM/PLD); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Pieuje Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Yoran-Oran (UC) (WHM/BLM); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Yoran-Oran Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: Yes; Notes: Does not use Nott. Casts Cursna on party members afflicted with Doom.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Magic DPS', note = '• Name (Job): Adelheid (SCH/BLM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] RoE Tutorial [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Ajido-Marujido (BLM/RDM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: Windurst + Rank 6 [CW] via A Matter of Trust I (Windurst); Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Shantotto (BLM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete Quests: Trust: San d\'Oria, Trust: Bastok, and Trust: Windurst. Obtain trusts: Ajido-Marujido, Kupipi, Nanaa Mihgo, Curilla, Excenmille, Trion, Volker, Naji, & Ayame. Complete Quest: Curses, Foiled A-Golem!?; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Shantotto II (BLM/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: See Summit of the Stars: Trust Access for unlock and usage restrictions.; Customized: No; Notes: Tier-1 single target elemental spells only.\n• Name (Job): Ullegore (BLM/DRK); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Obtained in Halloween Event; Customized: No' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Melee DPS', note = '• Name (Job): Abenzio (MNK/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Purchased from Chiliad the Snoll in Ru\'Lude Gardens for 1000 Grand Tokens during the Chiliad the Snoll server event when CEXI reaches 1000 concurrent players.; Customized: Yes; Notes: Slight accuracy bonus, buff to magic accuracy to help his status effect abilities, and he has an auto-regen which increases in potency at higher levels (38 at lvl75).\n• Name (Job): Abquhbah (WAR/MNK); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete President Salaheem (AU3) and Ever Forward (RoV 2-7).; Notes: Holds up to 1500 TP to try to close skillchains.\n• Name (Job): Aldo (THF/NIN); Available: [CW]; Obtainment: Tonberry Trouble; Customized: Yes; Notes: Uses Despoil, Sneak Attack and has Dual Wield. Gains Treasure Hunter II at 45. Uses Dancing Edge and Evisceration. Will open Skillchains when you have 1000+ TP.\n• Name (Job): Areuhat (WAR/PLD); Available: [CW]; Obtainment: Sold by Allied Incursion Quartermaster in Al Zahbi.; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Ayame (SAM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Trust: Bastok + Rank 3; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Ayame (UC) (SAM/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Ayame Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Flaviria (UC) (DRG/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Flaviria Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Ingrid II (WHM/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Domain Invasion Greater Domain NMs; Customized: Yes; Notes: Does not cast cure, will periodically heal the party with a special move when multiple members are injured, will cast Cursna on Doom-afflicted party members. Will magic burst with powerful Banish spells. Holds up to 2500 TP to try to close skillchains. Against undead, gains a large bonus to physical and magical damage.\n• Name (Job): Invincible Shield (UC) (WAR/COR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Invincible Shield Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Iron Eater (WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete Trust: Bastok Collect trusts: Volker, Naji, & Ayame.; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Jakoh Wahcondalo (UC) (THF/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Jakoh Wahcondalo Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Lehko Habhoka (THF/BLM); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Lilisette II (DNC/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: RoV Mission 2-16; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Lion II (THF/NIN); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: RoV Mission 1-7; Customized: No; Notes: Casts Utsusemi. Gains Treasure Hunter II at 45. Holds up to 1500 TP to try to close skillchains.\n• Name (Job): Luzaf (COR/NIN); Available: [CW]; Obtainment: Sold by Allied Incursion Quartermaster in Al Zahbi.; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Maat (MNK/THF); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete Shattering Stars for six or more jobs. Speak with Maat in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-5).; Customized: Yes; Notes: Attack Bonus, Accuracy Bonus & Double Attack bonus.\n• Name (Job): Maat (UC) (THF/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Maat Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Matsui-P (NIN/BLM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: The Wyrmking Descends; Customized: Yes; Notes: Double Attack & MP bonus. Uses Innin, and will Magic Burst.\n• Name (Job): Maximilian (THF/NIN); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Purchase at Cumetouflaix; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus & Double Attack bonus. Casts Utsusemi. Uses Collaborator at 40 on the player with the highest enmity who is not a RUN, PLD, or NIN. Uses Bully at 60. TH2 at 45.\n• Name (Job): Mayakov (DNC/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Purchased from Domain Officer for 50,000 Domain Shards; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus, Double Attack, and Store TP bonus. Uses Haste Samba, Waltz, Saber Dance and Feather Step.\n• Name (Job): Morimar (BST/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Lesser Domain Invasion NM; Customized: Yes; Notes: Increased dmg and Store TP. At level 75, when he takes enough damage, he enters a rage that unlocks his ultimate weaponskill: 12 Blades of Remorse, and increases his STR and Accuracy. Attempts to close the highest skillchain available\n• Name (Job): Naja Salaheem (MNK/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus and Store TP bonus. Uses MNK Job Ability.\n• Name (Job): Naja Salaheem (UC) (THF/WAR); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Naja Salaheem Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Not fully implemented, may not work as expected.\n• Name (Job): Naji (WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: Bastok [CW] via A Matter of Trust III (Bastok); Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Nanaa Mihgo (THF); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Trust: Windurst + Rank 3; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus and Store TP bonus. Uses Despoil. Gains Treasure Hunter II at 45.\n• Name (Job): Nashmeira II (WHM/PUP); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: After RoV Mission 2-9; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Prishe (MNK/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: CoP 8-4. Examine Walnut Door in Tavnazian Safehold (K-7, Top floor); Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Prishe II (WHM/MNK); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: After RoV Mission 2-3; Customized: Yes; Notes: Uses Curaga at 75% HP instead of 25% when Ulmia is in the party.\n• Name (Job): Rainemard (RDM/PLD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Obtain trusts Shantotto and Iron Eater. Obtain Bundle of scrolls Key item Speak with Shanene in Batallia Downs (S) (J/I-7).; Customized: Yes; Notes: Only casts enhancing magic player and himself. Haste and Phalanx II. Uses convert when under 10% Mp instead of 5%.\n• Name (Job): Shikaree Z (DRG/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete Three Paths. Speak to Perih Vashai in Windurst Woods (K-7).; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Tenzen (SAM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] RoE Tutorial [CW] via Tonberry Trouble; Customized: Yes; Notes: [CW] version has been significantly buffed, will open the highest skillchain available based on the last weaponskill the player used. Haste bonus.\n• Name (Job): Uka Totlihn (DNC/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus and Store TP bonus. Uses Waltz, Haste Samba, and Quickstep. Stuns TP moves with Violent Flourish.\n• Name (Job): Volker (WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: Bastok + Rank 6 [CW] via A Matter of Trust I (Bastok); Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus and Enmity bonus. Uses WAR Job Ability.\n• Name (Job): Zeid II (DRK/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in White" Key item or after RoV Mission 1-17; Customized: Yes; Notes: Accuracy Bonus. Casts Stun.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Ranged DPS', note = '• Name (Job): Elivira (COR/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: Yes; Notes: Only uses Evoker\'s Roll and Warlock\'s Roll.\n• Name (Job): Semih Lafihna (RNG/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) Speak to Kupipi during mission 2-3 or after RoV Mission 1-7; Customized: Yes; Notes: Ranged Accuracy Bonus and Store TP bonus. Uses RNG Job Ability.\n• Name (Job): Tenzen II (SAM/RNG); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: After RoV Mission 2-2; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Qultada (COR/RNG); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item [CW] with Incursion Points; Customized: Yes; Notes: Only uses Samurai Roll and Fighter\'s Roll, and doesn\'t use Double-Up.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Special', note = '• Name (Job): Cornelia (GEO/BRD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Daily Quest Rewards; Customized: Yes; Notes: Uses Indi-Haste (12%)\n• Name (Job): Kupofried (GEO/BRD); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) "Rhapsody in Crimson" Key item; Customized: Yes; Notes: Uses Corsair\'s Roll (20%)\n• Name (Job): Moogle (GEO/BRD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Daily Quest Rewards; Customized: No; Notes: Indi-Refresh (~3)\n• Name (Job): Sakura (GEO/BRD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Daily Quest Rewards; Customized: No; Notes: Indi-Regen (~3)' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Support', note = '• Name (Job): Joachim (BRD/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] RoE Tutorial [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: Yes; Notes: Only uses 1x March and 1x Ballad song.\n• Name (Job): Koru-Moru (RDM/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Curio Vendor Moogle (Scrolls) [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Sylvie (UC) (GEO/WHM); Available: [ACE]; Obtainment: Join Sylvie Unity and earn 5000 accolades to unlock. Players can exchange 5 Copper Vouchers for Unity Accolades to instantly unlock.; Customized: No; Notes: Every conquest tally you must earn 5000 accolades to keep Sylvie (UC).\n• Name (Job): Ulmia (BRD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: CoP 8-4. Examine the Dilapidated Gate in Misareaux Coast (I-11).; Customized: Yes; Notes: Only uses 1x Minuet and 1x Madrigal song.' },
            { title = 'Trusts: Tanks', note = '• Name (Job): Ark Angel Ev (PLD/WHM); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Purchase at Cumetouflaix; Customized: Yes; Notes: Enmity++ bonus. Hp +10% Uses the spells Phalanx at level 68, Enlight at level 75, and uses Holy to Magic Burst at level 55. Uses Shield Strike, and will use it to stun enemies when they attempt abilities or to cast spells. Gains increased enmity from her weaponskills.\n• Name (Job): August (PLD/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: See Summit of the Stars: Trust Access for unlock and usage restrictions.; Customized: Yes; Notes: Damage of No Quarter has been buffed\n• Name (Job): Curilla (PLD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: San d\'Oria + Rank 3 [CW] via A Matter of Trust I (San d\'Oria); Customized: Yes; Notes: Bonus Cure Potency, Cure Cast Time, and Enmity Loss Reduction, and small bonus to Enmity. +20% MP, and gains increased enmity from her weaponskills. When Rainemard is in the party, Curilla now has bonuses to Accuracy, Magic Accuracy, Defense, and Magic Defense, and a much larger bonus to Enmity. Bonus enmity whenever she uses any weaponskill.\n• Name (Job): Excenmille (PLD); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] Trust: San d\'Oria [CW] via A Matter of Trust III (San d\'Oria)\n• Name (Job): Gessho (NIN/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Complete Passing Glory. Examine the cushion in Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12).; Customized: Yes; Notes: Will prioritize Provoke over casting Kurayami and Hojo\n• Name (Job): Halver (PLD/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Speak to Halver during mission 2-3 or after RoV Mission 1-7; Customized: Yes; Notes: [ACE] Enmity bonus. [CW] Only builds TP and performs Weaponskills.\n• Name (Job): Trion (PLD/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: Trust: San d\'Oria + Rank 6; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Rughadjeen (PLD/PLD); Available: [CW]; Obtainment: Sold by Allied Incursion Quartermaster in Al Zahbi.; Customized: No\n• Name (Job): Valaineral (PLD/WAR); Available: [ACE] [CW]; Obtainment: [ACE] RoE Tutorial [CW] via Goblin\'s Gambit; Customized: No' },
    } },
    { name = 'Travel and quality of life', group = 'Server', desc = 'Getting around, and the Mog Vault storage system. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Navigation, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Mog_Vault', steps = {
            { title = 'Navigation: Aht Urhgan Whitegate', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing the quest Lure of the Wildcat (Jeuno), you\'ll be able to teleport to Aht Urhgan Whitegate by trading 300 gils to Ajithaam in Upper Jeuno (F-5).\n• If you also have completed Up, Up and Away, you\'ll be able to teleport from Emilia / Emilio / Emiliu as well.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: BCNM Teleportation / Domenic', note = '• Game modes: [CW] CW\n• After completing the quest Digging Up Dirt, you\'ll be able to teleport to Ghelsba Outpost, Horlais Peak, Waughroon Shrine, Balga\'s Dais and Qu\'Bia Arena by speaking to Domenic in Lower Jeuno (J-7).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Beastmen Strongholds Teleportation', note = '• Game modes: [CW] CW\n• After completing the quest Gobbie Travels, you\'ll be able to teleport to Beadeaux, Davoi and Castle Oztroja by talking to Portalix located at Lower Jeuno (H-9).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Castle Zvahl Keep / Throne Room', note = '• Game modes: [CW] CW\n• With the Shadow Lord Shirt purchase for 50 Helper Points.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: EXP Book › Present', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing the quest Near Death Experience, you\'ll be able to teleport to many locations from the present by talking to the EXP Book located at Lower Jeuno (I-7).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: EXP Book › Past', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing the quest Blast to the Past, you\'ll be able to teleport to many locations from the past by talking to the EXP Book located at Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-9).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Jeuno~ish from Al Zahbi', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• Talk to Shihu-Danhu at Al Zahbi (J-10) to be teleported back to somewhere around Jeuno (random, see NPC page for details).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Home Points Teleportation', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE\n• After clicking a home point, you\'ll be able to teleport back to it. Doing so will also restore your HPs & MPs in Towns/Cities - Crystals in outside areas do not restore HP & MP.\n• Otherwise, see retail\'s Home Point Teleportation for general functionalities.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Items Teleport to Various Cities', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• Teleport Ring: Dem, Teleport Ring: Holla and Teleport Ring: Mea can be purchased with Domain Shards.\n• Duchy Earring, Federation Earring, Kazham Earring, Kingdom Earring, Mhaura Earring, Nashmau Earring, Norg Earring, Rabao Earring, Republic Earring and Selbina Earring can be obtained via Marceo\'s Guttable Fish.\n• Tavnazian Ring is obtained by completing CoP 8-1.\n• Tidal Talisman can be purchased with Obsidian Fragments ([ACE] ACE and [CW] CW only)' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Mini Tuning Fork Warps', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing the mini-tuning fork fight, SMNs may trade 100 gil to the corresponding avatar trial NPC in order to warp to the cloister. This means mini-tuning forks do not need to be held on to just to warp.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Norg', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-4, you\'ll be able to teleport to Norg by talking to Pacomart in Selbina (H-10) or Tonasav in Mhaura (H-9).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Outpost Teleportation', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing a Supply Run to a given outpost, you\'ll be able to teleport back to it from a Nation Teleporter, or from Emilia / Emilio / Emiliu after completing the quest Up, Up and Away.\n• Outpost Warps have the same retail restrictions in place, which can be found here.\n• Outpost Warps also unlock after clearing the region\'s Garrison.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Past Teleportation', note = '• After completing the Nation Initiation quest of, you can use a Scroll of Retrace to teleport back to your nation, and then use one of the Campaign Teleport NPC to travel elsewhere in the past:\n• Scarlette, C.A. in Southern San d\'Oria (S) at H-9\n• Waldemar, I.M. in Bastok Markets (S) at G-4\n• Mindala-Andola, C.C. in Windurst Waters (S) at G-5' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Ru\'Aun Gardens', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• After completing Zilart Mission 13 and Promathia Mission 8-3, complete the quest Teleport into Tu\'Lia. You\'ll then be able to teleport to Ru\'Aun Gardens from any Hall of Transference (crag).' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Unity Warps', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE\n• Warp to various locations from a for Unity Accolades.\n• You can teleport to certain Wanted areas. Some of the warps have been disabled on this server.\n• Available Unity Warps are:\n• 99 & Below\n• East Ronfaure\n• South Gustaberg\n• East Sarutabaruta\n• La Theine Plateau\n• Konschtat Highlands\n• Tahrongi Canyon\n• Content Level 119\n• Valkurm Dunes\n• Buburimu Peninsula\n• Qufim Island\n• Content Level 122\n• Jugner Forest\n• Pashhow Marshlands\n• Meriphataud Mountains\n• Content Level 125\n• Rolanberry Fields\n• Batallia Downs (A nice shortcut to Jeuno!)\n• Sauromugue Champaign\n• Beaucedine Glacier\n• Xarcabard\n• Garlaige Citadel\n• Content Level 128\n• Fei\'Yin\n• Content Level 135\n• Behemoth\'s Dominion' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Wajaom Woodlands', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• The Olduum Ring (obtained via quest Olduum) will teleport you to the Leypoint at (G-8) Wajaom Woodlands.' },
            { title = 'Navigation: Within Windurst', note = '• Game modes: [ACE] ACE, [CW] CW, [WEW] WEW\n• Machu-Kuchu at Port Windurst (E-7) will teleport you to Windurst Walls (J-11)\n• Komulili at Windurst Walls (J-11) will teleport you to Port Windurst (E-7)\n• Pattsu-Yabittsu at Windurst Woods (K-12) will teleport you to Windurst Waters North (G-8)\n• Tonana at Windurst Waters North (G-8) will teleport you to Windurst Woods (K-12)' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Mog Vault', note = '• Inventory woes, begone! CatsEyeXI is proud to introduce a brand-new storage system that will change how you manage your gear and items: the Mog Vault.\n• Kept secret since the days of the ancient Moogle kingdom of Kupalika, the Mog Vault is an extradimensional pocket of Quantum Moogle space. Items placed inside the Vault completely vanish from this plane of existence... until you choose to swap them back into reality.\n• In practical terms:\n• The Mog Vault lets you swap the entire contents of a storage container with a container inside the Vault.\n• By putting items in the Mog Vault, you can free up a Wardrobe, Mog Satchel, Mog Sack, or Mog Case to hold more items.\n• Anything inside the Mog Vault is completely inaccessible while stored (but it is searchable with /find).\n• With the Mog Vault, your storage just got much less cramped. No more tough choices about which jobs to gear or which craft items to toss; just stash them in the Vault, and bring them back when you\'re ready!' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Mog Vault › Unlocking Vaults › Base Vaults', note = '• Completing the initial quest will unlock:\n• 1 Vault Deposit Box (for Satchel/Sack/Case)\n• 1 Vault Wardrobe (for equipment wardrobes)\n• Requirements:\n• Level 75\n• Access to Escha - Ru\'Aun\n    ◦ Rank 10, in any nation.\n    ◦ Having defeated Dynamis Lord in Dynamis Xarcabard to be able to access\n    ◦ Complete Chains of Promathia Mission 1-3\n• Walkthrough:\n• Begin the quest by speaking to Moggy in Kazham H-9.\n    ◦ Moggy will ask for your help tracking down his missing big bro, Mogster. You will be tasked with delivering letters from moogle to moogle in order to solve the mystery.\n• Talk to Serino in Airship, Jeuno - Kazham\n• Talk to Mochos in Newton Movalpolos G-8\n    ◦ You can get there by warping to the mine shaft for 2,000 gil from Twinkbrix and then working your way west\n• Talk to Atla in Pso\'Xja H-8 Map 14, near Golden-Tongued Culberry\n    ◦ Enter from Beaucedine Glacier F-7, Nue\'s tower\n    ◦ You get to Atla by dropping down the holes while aiming for the center-south (can drop left and take the first hole you see on the next two floors, twice, then go south past the scary tile floor up the stairs to the center platform)\n• Talk to Mozme in Escha - Ru\'Aun H-9\n• Trade an X-Potion to Mozme\n    ◦ An X-Potion +1, +2, or +3 will also work.\n• Travel to Mount Zhayolm F-9 Map 1\n    ◦ Access via Halvung C/D-11, you will need Bracelet of verve\n• Talk to Mogster, then talk to him again and select "Bring it on" to start a fight\n    ◦ Important! Make sure everyone in your group who is at this stage of the quest speaks with Mogster once before the fight begins, or else they will not get credit, and you\'ll have to repeat the fight.\n    ◦ He has a strong Regen, extremely high DEF, and hits like a brick. Plus some nice small AOE damage & amnesia or stun moves.\n    ◦ Seems to use Washtub (AoE amnesia, stun, damage) more often when hate changes.\n    ◦ Uses Draw in followed by an Stun + AoE at 50% and again at 25%. After each, his attack speed increases slightly and his double/triple attack rate seems to increase.\n• After the fight, talk to Mogster.\n• Return to Moggy in Kazham to unlock 1 vault deposit box and 1 vault wardrobe.\n• Tip: If you lose track of your progress, you can use the !vault command to see where you are at!' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Mog Vault › Unlocking Vaults › More Vaults', note = '• You can unlock more Vault containers via Moggy\'s Mogshop.\n• In future updates, you\'ll be able to earn additional Vault containers by doing favors for moogles.' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Mog Vault › Using Vaults', note = '• Once unlocked, you can use the !vault command while in town to view your Mog Vault.\n• For 10,000 gil, you may swap one of your containers with its Vault counterpart:\n• Vault Deposit Box ↔ Satchel, Sack, or Case\n• Vault Wardrobe ↔ any Wardrobe 1-8\n• Unlocking more vault containers will also reduce the cost when swapping containers (amount TBD).\n• Unlocked Tier: Box/Wardrobe A; Cost (Gils) Prices lower per Deposit Box/Wardrobe unlock: 10,000; Kupo Kudo unlock Cost*: N/A\n• Unlocked Tier: Box/Wardrobe B; Cost (Gils) Prices lower per Deposit Box/Wardrobe unlock: 8,500; Kupo Kudo unlock Cost*: 50\n• Unlocked Tier: Box/Wardrobe C; Cost (Gils) Prices lower per Deposit Box/Wardrobe unlock: 7,000; Kupo Kudo unlock Cost*: 60\n• Unlocked Tier: Box/Wardrobe D; Cost (Gils) Prices lower per Deposit Box/Wardrobe unlock: 6,000; Kupo Kudo unlock Cost*: 75\n• Unlocked Tier: Box/Wardrobe E; Kupo Kudo unlock Cost*: 95\n• *Kupo Kudo price scales with total upgrades purchased, regardless of option chosen.\n• The swap always exchanges the entire contents of both containers. (No single-item transfers!)\n• If your Vault container is empty, swapping will leave you with an empty container to refill as you like. Next time you swap, you\'ll trade the full container for whatever\'s in the Vault.\n• Heads Up! You won\'t be able to swap out items that are currently equipped, or swap in items that would cause you to have multiple copies of a Rare item.' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Mogster Rematch', note = '• Every week, players can challenge Mogster in Mount Zhayolm to a rematch! Defeating Mogster will earn each participant 4 Kupo Kudos; speak to Mogster after the fight to obtain this reward. Helping other players with their initial Mog Vault quest fight counts as that week\'s rematch, so you don\'t have to fight Mogster again that week!\n• Players cannot challenge Mogster to a rematch the same week that they complete the Mog Vault quest.' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Moggy\'s Mogshop', note = '• After unlocking the Mog Vault, Moggy opens his Mogshop, which includes cosmetic and useful items as well as expansions for the Vault. To purchase these items, players must spend Kupo Kudos, which are earned through various moogle errands and favors.\n• Trade Kupo Kudos to Moggy to add them to your balance. You can also withdraw Kudos, but this is currently only used for the Ancestry Moogle\'s Race Change.\n• Item: Unlock Vault Dep. Box; Kupo Kudos: 50*\n• Item: Unlock Vault Wardrobe; Kupo Kudos: 50*\n• Item: Mog Missile x15; Kupo Kudos: 1\n• Item: Moogle Guard +1; Kupo Kudos: 25\n• Item: Kupofried\'s Ring; Kupo Kudos: 50**\n• Item: Moogle Cap; Kupo Kudos: 50\n• Item: N. Moogle Statue; Kupo Kudos: 50\n• Item: Moogle Mount; Kupo Kudos: 250\n• Item: Kupo Masque; Kupo Kudos: 500\n• Item: Kupo Rod; Kupo Kudos: 500\n• * The Kudo cost for both the Deposit Box/Wardrobes goes up with each expansion of either. 50>60>75 and so on. You can reduce the Kudo cost of upgrades by obtaining the Viridian abyssite of guerdon, Vermillion abyssite of guerdon (not yet available), and Ivory abyssite of guerdon (not yet available). If you have already unlocked Mog Vault containers at the higher price, the excess Kupo Kudos you paid will be refunded to your balance.\n• ** Can be recharged for 4 kudos per charge (44 kudos for 11/11) by trading the ring to Moggy. Can only purchase or recharge one ring per month. Can be used while under Prestige.' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Moggy\'s Mogshop › Ways to Earn Kupo Kudos', note = '• Weekly Letter Quest\n    ◦ Each week, three moogles are selected across Vana\'diel for Moggy\'s letter delivery chain.\n    ◦ Deliver all three letters to earn Kudos along the way (1 kudo from each moogle), plus a bonus (4 kudos) when you return to Moggy, for a total of 7.\n    ◦ Your progress on this weekly quest can be tracked with the !vault command.\n• Kupo Nuts\n    ◦ Trade a Kupo Nut to any "letter moogle," or any moogle from the original Mog Vault quest, once per moogle per week.\n    ◦ Rewards include Kupo Kudos, a Scroll of Instant Escape (new!), moogle-themed consumables, and sometimes flowerpots!\n    ◦ Obtain Kupo Nuts with points from a variety of other CatsEyeXI content.\n• Stiltzkin the Traveling Merchant Moogle\n    ◦ Each day, Stiltzkin appears near another moogle, where he sells players a package deal: one medicine, one gemstone, and one or more Kupo Kudos.\n    ◦ Stiltzkin\'s prices increase each time you purchase from him, with higher prices bringing better rewards; his price resets after you purchase from him 9 times.\n    ◦ Moggy will reveal Stiltzkin\'s current location each day once you\'ve completed that week\'s letter quest.\n• 11,111Gil — 1 Kupo Kudo 2 random items, including: Light Opal Pearl Potion Eye Drops Silent Oil\n• 22,222 Gil — 1 Kupo Kudo 2 random items, including: Hi-Ether Lapis Lazuli Sardonyx Tomato Juice Elixir Vitae\n• 33,333 Gil — 1 Kupo Kudo 2 random items, including: Amethyst Ametrine Garnet Super Ether Tomato Juice\n• 44,444 Gil — 1 Kupo Kudo 2 random items, including: Sphene Peridot Chrysoberyl Echo Drops Grape Juice Prism Powder\n• 55,555 Gil — 2 Kupo Kudos 2 random items, including: Black Pearl Fluorite Reraiser X-Potion\n• 66,666 Gil — 2 Kupo Kudos 2 random items, including:\n• 77,777 Gil — 3 Kupo Kudos 2 random items, including:\n• 88,888 Gil — 3 Kupo Kudos 2 random items, including: Antacid Fluorite Hermes Quencher Ruby\n• 99,999 Gil — 4 Kupo Kudos 2 random items, including: Ruby Sapphire Strange Milk Vile Elixir\n• [WIP]' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Moggy\'s Mogshop › Moogle Locations', note = '• Only 3 Letter-Moogles spawn each week alongside the quest Moogles, allowing for a maximum of 8 \'Kupo Nut\' trades per week.\n• Moogle: Grimo; Location: Whitegate >> Nashmau Ship; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Gumo; Location: Ceizak Battlegrounds; Notes: Back of the DI Arena\n• Moogle: Kumool; Location: The Garden of Ru\'Hmet; Notes: 2nd floor, go counter-clockwise following Ix\'Aern DRG locations, at southmost tip at (H-10)\n• Moogle: Kumop; Location: Rolanberry Fields; Notes: By Fountain of Partings\n• Moogle: Mimoza; Location: Ve\'Lugannon Palace; Notes: Enter from #2 Ru\'Aun, then to basement via "F". Mimoza is in the first cells in front of you at (H-7)\n• Moogle: Mocchi; Location: Toraimarai Canal; Notes: Map 2, Corner of the circular room intersecting (G-8)/(H-9)\n• Moogle: Mogki; Location: Bastok >> Jeuno Airship; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Mogmatt; Location: Escha - Zi\'Tah; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Mogmi; Location: Sea Serpent Grotto; Notes: (G-10) Map #3. Through Mythril Door.\n• Moogle: Mogret; Location: Yuhtunga Jungle; Notes: (K-7) - Ash Dragon exit from Ifrit\'s Cauldron.\n• Moogle: Mogrich; Location: The Eldieme Necropolis; Notes: Bottom right of (E-6) Map2. Entrance #7 via Beauc. Glacier side.\n• Moogle: Mogrika; Location: Kamihr Drifts; Notes: Back of the DI Arena\n• Moogle: Mogryo; Location: Stellar Fulcrum; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Mogsam; Location: Quicksand Caves; Notes: Enter from the Altepa Gate, bottom right of (I-10).\n• Moogle: Mogsy; Location: Riverne - Site B01; Notes: Near the Monument at (C-10)\n• Moogle: Mogtaka; Location: The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah; Notes: (I-10) After Exiting via Dragon\'s Aery\n• Moogle: Moguel; Location: Caedarva Mire; Notes: (K-6) Map #1, near the rams, access via Arrapago Reef exit 6\n• Moogle: Mogwin; Location: Morimar Basalt Fields; Notes: Back of the DI Arena\n• Moogle: Mois; Location: Uleguerand Range; Notes: Slide off the north side of the western ramp, landing on the first cave.\n• Moogle: Mojito; Location: Batallia Downs; Notes: (J-11) On the Island.\n• Moogle: Molulu; Location: La Theine Plateau\n• Moogle: Monev\n• Moogle: Monty; Location: Jugner Forest; Notes: In King Arthro area\n• Moogle: Moodon; Location: San d\'Oria >> Jeuno Airship; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Mooel; Location: The Shrine of Ru\'Avitau; Notes: Just before Mother Globe room.\n• Moogle: Moonte; Location: Bostaunieux Oubliette; Notes: In the vampire room Map #2 (K-7)\n• Moogle: Moorock; Location: Aydeewa Subterrane; Notes: Map#2 (J-10) Must enter via Wajoam #9 entrance then follow path "I" to reach him.\n• Moogle: Mopli; Location: Hall of the Gods; Notes: Past the Cerulean Gate at the bottom of the teleporter room\n• Moogle: Mosco; Location: Windurst >> Jeuno Airship; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Mosh; Location: Manaclipper from Bibiki Bay; Notes: Appears to work for any destination\n• Moogle: Mugmug; Location: Yorcia Weald; Notes: Back of the DI Arena\n• Moogle: Nazna; Location: Nashmau >> Whitegate Ship; Notes: - - -\n• Moogle: Noggy; Location: North Gustaberg; Notes: Down at F-7. Must enter North Gustaberg from the northern exit in Dangruf Wadi\n• Moogle: Suzuna; Location: Marjami Ravine; Notes: Back of Hurkan\'s Arena\n• Moogle: Atla; Location: Pso\'Xja; Notes: H-8 Map 14, near Golden-Tongued Culberry; enter from Nue tower\n• Moogle: Mochos; Location: Newton Movalpolos; Notes: G-8\n• Moogle: Moggy; Location: Kazham\n• Moogle: Mozme; Location: Escha - Ru\'Aun; Notes: North of where Despot would be, near the shrine entrance.\n• Moogle: Serino; Location: Kazham >> Jeuno Airship; Notes: - - -' },
            { title = 'Mog Vault: Ancestry Moogle\'s Race Change', note = '• Ancestry Moogle, located near the Greeter and Curio Moogles in the 3 nations, can perform an appearance change on the player, allowing Race, Gender, Face, Hair, and Size to be changed.\n• Availability\n• Everyone gets one free Race Change per character.\n• After that, in order to be eligible for a Race Change, players must trade an Ancestry Moogle either:\n    ◦ 20x Kupo Kudo or,\n    ◦ 2,000,000 gil ([ACE]), or 1,000,000 gil ([WEW] [CW])\n• Alternatively, players can purchase eligibility for the Race Change service from Ygnas in Ru\'Lude Gardens or Ruspix in Leafallia\n    ◦ for 70,000 Activity Points.\n• Eligibility for the Race Change service lasts for 14 days before it expires. Players may only make use of this service once per 14 days.\n• Armor Swap\n• After changing Race or Gender Ancestry Moogle can change certain items that you can no longer use.\n• Dancer Artifact Armour.\n• Eventually, other items such as lvl 30 RSE and Purgonurgo Island teleport equipment e.g. Wonder Maillot +1.' },
    } },
    { name = 'Commands', group = 'Server', desc = 'Custom ! commands typed in /say. Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Commands', steps = {
            { title = 'Overview', note = '• Custom commands to type in /say.\n• All custom commands start with ! and may have sub-commands (in lowercase in the table below) and/or VARIABLES (in uppercase in the table below).\n• Command: !artifacts; Notes: Get information about Stronghold artifacts; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !box...; Notes: Disclaimer: The Ephemeral box will not prevent players from withdrawing more items than they have inventory space for. Items that do not fit in the inventory will be permanently lost. See the Ephemeral Box page for more info.; Game Modes: [CW]\n    ◦ Command: !box ITEM_NAME !box ITEM_ID; Notes: Anywhere in the world: Check your stock for the given item. Within 5 yalms of an Ephemeral Box: Withdraw the item via a menu For example: !box Wool Cloth or !box 4401\n    ◦ Command: !box QUANTITY ITEM_NAME !box QUANTITY ITEM_ID; Notes: Within 5 yalms of an Ephemeral Box: Withdraw the given quantity/item For example: !box 12 Wool Cloth\n    ◦ Command: !box ammo; Notes: Within 5 yalms of an Ephemeral Box: Withdraw ammo as quivers, cases & boxes. You do not need to specify the element with this command, a menu will appear.\n    ◦ Command: !box cluster; Notes: Within 5 yalms of an Ephemeral Box: Withdraw crystals as clusters, or Prismatic Cluster You do not need to specify the element with this command, a menu will appear.\n    ◦ Command: !box store; Notes: Within 5 yalms of an Ephemeral Box: Instantly store every storable item in their inventory. Re-run the command for large numbers of items. Tip: move to your Mog Case the items you don\'t want to store, or see the corresponding config command above to customize the behavior of this command.\n• !campaign — Shows you how close you are to your next promotion, as well as the status of any currently active campaign battles.\n• Command: !chef; Notes: Grants the player a food item of their choosing in exchange for gil. You may also NPC items with it.; Game Modes: [ACE] [WEW]\n    ◦ Antacid — 8,000G\n    ◦ Meat Jerky — 2,000G\n    ◦ Meat Mithkabob — 5,000G\n    ◦ Coeurl Sub — 7,000G\n    ◦ Boiled Crab — 2,000G\n    ◦ Fish Mithkabob — 5,000G\n    ◦ Jack-o\'-Lantern — 2,000G\n    ◦ Tuna Sushi — 8,000G\n    ◦ Dorado Sushi — 8,000G\n    ◦ Apple Pie — 2,000G\n    ◦ Melon Pie — 2,000G\n    ◦ Cream Puff — 7,000G\n    ◦ Orange Juice — 2,000G\n    ◦ Melon Juice — 5,000G\n    ◦ Yagudo Drink — 7,000G\n• Command: !config NAME VALUE; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n    ◦ Ephemeral Box:\n    ◦ Name: ebox_store_food; Value: true or false; Notes: Whether to store corresponding type of items in the Ephemeral Box when using !box store\n    ◦ ebox_store_ammo — true or false\n    ◦ ebox_store_tools — true or false\n    ◦ ebox_store_potion — true or false\n    ◦ ebox_store_pet — true or false\n    ◦ Misc:\n    ◦ Name: emilia_signet; Value: true or false; Notes: Enables / disables the automatic application of Signet upon teleporting with Emilia\n    ◦ Name: no_afterglow; Value: on or off; Notes: Configure whether suppress Relic/Mysthic weapon afterglow effect. Note: You must unlock the Aeonic weaponskill associated with your weapon type in order to enable afterglow.\n    ◦ Name: no_equip_messages; Value: true or false; Notes: Configure whether show on equip messages for traits and bonuses\n    ◦ Name: prestige_hidden; Value: true or false; Notes: Configure whether to show or hide your Prestige stars Make sure to zone after using the command for it to fully take effect\n    ◦ Name: skip_furnace_rp; Value: true or false; Notes: Configure whether to block the message you see when you use the synergy furnace to augment equipment (i.e. "Yourname has given up X pieces of their soul to the furnace")\n    ◦ Name: venture_list_full; Value: true or false; Notes: Configure whether to show all venture types when omitting the sub-category (if set to true), or only show exp (if set to false)\n    ◦ Name: no_gil_messages; Value: on or off; Notes: Enables / disables the gil obtained messages from "EXP to Gil" Corsair prestige levels.\n    ◦ Name: warp_scrolls; Value: true or false; Notes: Enables / disables the automatic purchase of a Scroll of Instant Warp for 10 Conquest Points upon teleporting with Emilia, Domenic or via Runic Portal in Whitegate\n• Command: !currency; Notes: List how much Dynamis Currencies, Alexandrite, H-P Bayld and Incursion Currencies you have, and where they are stored (Inventory or E.Box); Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !dailies; Notes: View your Goblin and Sea dailies.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !dailykills; Notes: View your daily quest progress for Murdox.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !dawnunstuck; Notes: Releases the player from the stuck event at CoP 8-4 Dawn. Try using it for other missions too, should you get stuck.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !delexp; Notes: Removes the players dedication buff.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !essences; Notes: Verifies which Dynamis 2.0 wins you have obtained.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !fatigue; Notes: Displays one\'s fishing fatigue for the day.; Game Modes: [ACE] [WEW]\n• Command: !help; Notes: Displays all commands available to your character.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !hunter; Notes: Display your current weekly hunt objective.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !incursion; Notes: Check the currently occupied Incursion areas the time remaining; Game Modes: [CW]\n• Command: !keys; Notes: Displays chest/coffer keys stored with Picklox.; Game Modes: [CW]\n• Command: !lsstats NUMBER; Notes: Display the top NUMBER contributors in a player\'s Linkshell for Summit of the Stars.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !maat; Notes: Display which jobs you have used to defeat Maat in Shattering Stars.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !mog; Notes: Allows access to the mog house menu anywhere in a city. ⚠️ This command may only be used in cities.; Game Modes: [ACE] [WEW]\n• Command: !newadventurer; Notes: Removes the ? from the heads of new players.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !pass; Notes: Displays garrison pop items stored with Picklox.; Game Modes: [CW]\n• Command: !pf; Notes: Displays those seeking with the Party Finder addon.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !points; Notes: Lists all of the various point amounts: Currencies: Obsidian Fragments, Escha Beads, Dynamis RP, DKP Ventures: EXP, Fishing, Mining, Gathering, Logging CW: Arena Points, Gobbie Grandeur Points, Helper Points; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !pops; Notes: Shows you which Domain Invasion NMs, Goblin Brew NMs, Sky 2.0 Bosses, or Guild NMs you can currently spawn.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !prestige JOB; Notes: Without JOB, shows your currently active Prestige bonuses. Displays gil collected in the current area from COR Prestige Bonus and Wings-Era Warrior combined. With JOB (eg. !prestige war), shows prestige bonuses for this job.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !quest; Notes: Displays your progress on CatsEye Custom Quests.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !re; Notes: Refreshes the party status, if it doesn\'t show players in the current zone or other similar issues.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !rubyweather; Notes: Display which weathers you have unlocked for the SMN quest I Can Hear a Rainbow.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !sanction !sigil !signet; Notes: Applies the bonuses of either Sanction, Sigil, or Signet anywhere in the game.; Game Modes: [ACE]\n• Command: !scroll SCROLL_NAME; Notes: Check if a scroll is stored in the Ephemeral Box or Gramateus; Game Modes: [CW]\n• Command: !skills; Notes: Displays custom skill such as Garbagio; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !skipfloor; Notes: Allow to skip lamp floors in Nyzul Isle Investigation every 30 minutes via the command !skipfloor. The lockout applies to all party members!; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !squire ITEM_NAME; Notes: Checks items stores at the Squires; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !rifts; Notes: Allows players to see when and where a Rift has opened if they missed the Unity channel announcement.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !summit !summit VALUE; Notes: With no parameter, returns whether earning points for your linkshell for Summit of the Stars is enabled; with VALUE set to on or off, enable/disable earning points for the linkshell. Even when off, you still earn points for your personal bank. This is intended for players who don\'t want to affect their LS AMC but still play the game regularly. Only works for people who have completed the Summit of the Stars quest. Once a player has earned any points for the AMC of their LS of this week, there\'s no point in using !summit off since their LS AMC has already increased. The command has a 30-minute cooldown.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !summitcalc POINTS_AMOUNT; Notes: Show a full breakdown of your adjusted points (which will go as contribution towards your linkshell points), where POINTS_AMOUNT is the amount of points you received.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !summitnotify; Notes: Enable/disable Summit of the Stars notifications when zoning in.Summit_of_the_Stars.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !summitreward REWARD_TYPE; Notes: The linkshell owner can choose whether their linkshell receives Gil or Wyrm Gold as a reward for winning the Summit of the Stars. REWARD_TYPE is one of: gil, wyrmgold; Game Modes: [CW]\n• Command: !trials; Notes: View your novice trial progress.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !vault; Notes: Access your Mog Vault in towns if you have completed the quest, otherwise shows your progress towards the quest.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !venture VALUE; Notes: With VALUE set to on or off, enable/disable ventures.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !ventures CATEGORY; Notes: Lists all of the various Ventures objectives for the day. CATEGORY is optional and can be one of: dynamis ([CW] only), exp, fishing, helm. See the corresponding config command above to customize the behavior of this command.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]\n• Command: !wspoints CATEGORY; Notes: Shows how many Weapon Skill points you have accumulated on the piece of equipment in the corresponding slot. CATEGORY can be one of: main, sub or ranged; It defaults to main if omitted.; Game Modes: [ACE] [CW] [WEW]' },
    } },
    { name = 'Custom gear', group = 'Server', desc = 'Custom equipment shown on the wiki whose name is not in this server\'s code-generated gear list (142 items): name (slot, level, jobs, stats). Source: https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Fishing, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Quests, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatsEyeXI_Systems/Synthesis, https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=CatseyeXI_Crafting_Guide', steps = {
